&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A diverse and enriching work environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: Become a valued member of a wonderfully diverse team of individuals from over 50 countries. At GROPYUS we value inclusion above all, ensuring that everyone feels they belong – no matter their background. In this way, our differences become strengths that help us grow as a team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Join us on our mission to design buildings as continuously evolving products to create the most exciting and affordable experience for all. We build for people and conserve the resources of our planet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We can&#39;t wait to get to know you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;For more information, visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gropyus.com/&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/gropyus/rust-software-engineer-industrial-automation-all-genders-richen-baden-wurttemberg-306087","tags":["Product Delivery"],"job_types":[],"location":"Richen, Baden-Württemberg","created_at":1792270514},{"slug":"founders-associate-intern-ops-marketing-munich-96656","company_name":"Mercura","title":"Founders Associate Intern (Ops & Marketing)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Mercura (<strong>YC W25</strong>) helps the companies that build the real world move at software speed, automating the back-office work that runs the <strong>$12 trillion industry</strong> behind every hospital, school, and power plant. We started with one of their biggest bottlenecks - turning messy technical requests into accurate quotes - and <strong>eightfolded our revenue in 12 months</strong>. With a team of 16, we're now targeting $10M by the end of 2026 as well as our expansion into the US.</p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>Founder's Associate Intern (Marketing &amp; Ops)</strong> to help make Mercura one of the most visible and compelling B2B AI companies in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take real ownership of how Mercura shows up externally — to customers, candidates and the broader ecosystem. You’ll work closely with the founders and team to turn ideas, company developments and customer insights into content, campaigns, events and new growth initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not an internship where you execute a predefined marketing calendar. We want someone who comes up with ideas, launches them quickly, measures what works and doubles down.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to learn how to build a company, enjoy creating things from scratch and care deeply about results, this is an opportunity to own a meaningful part of Mercura from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will be working on</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company &amp; Founder Marketing:</strong> Own and grow Mercura's company and founder LinkedIn presence. Turn what happens inside Mercura into content that reaches prospective customers, exceptional candidates and the wider industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Marketing:</strong> Develop and test new ways to generate awareness, inbound demand and talent. Come up with experiments, launch them quickly and measure whether they actually move the numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SEO, AI Visibility &amp; Website:</strong> Help grow Mercura's organic presence across Google and AI search. Work with experienced external experts on SEO, AI visibility, website structure, conversion and design — and turn their recommendations into execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Events:</strong> Build memorable events for both customers and talent — from recruiting events and community formats to intimate dinners with CEOs and strategic prospects. Own everything from the initial idea and guest list to invitations and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Brand &amp; Content:</strong> Create landing pages, customer stories, campaigns, event concepts and other assets that make Mercura stand out and explain why what we are building matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>New Initiatives:</strong> Spot opportunities we haven't thought of yet. If you believe a campaign, partnership, event or completely different idea could create meaningful impact, you will have the freedom to make it happen.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we’re looking for</h2><h3>Skills &amp; Experience</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have already gained <strong>hands-on marketing experience</strong> — for example at a startup, through an internship, your own project, student initiative or company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can write exceptionally well and understand what makes people stop, read and take action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong instinct for content, positioning and what makes a company or person interesting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine creativity with commercial thinking. You care about <strong>reach, qualified leads, great applicants and actual outcomes</strong>, not just producing content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable using AI tools and learn new tools extremely quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take full ownership. If something needs to happen, you figure out how to make it happen rather than waiting for instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your German is C2/native-level. This is a hard requirement.</strong> You are also a strong professional communicator in English.</p></li></ul><h3>Personality &amp; Commitment</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re entrepreneurial, ambitious and highly proactive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong drive and hold yourself to a high standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy starting with a blank page and turning an idea into something real.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are creative, but equally comfortable with execution and the unglamorous details required to make something successful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are highly organized and can run several initiatives simultaneously without losing speed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about results and naturally ask: <em>Did this actually work? How can we make it better?</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to work <strong>in person in Munich</strong> and thrive in an environment with significantly higher intensity and ownership than a typical 9–5 internship.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Availability</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are available for a <strong>minimum 4-month full-time internship</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, you are in the <strong>final semester of your Bachelor's or Master's degree</strong>, or have recently graduated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are explicitly looking for people who could imagine staying at Mercura afterwards. If there is a strong mutual fit, there is an opportunity to transition into a <strong>full-time role</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Mercura</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn how to build a company:</strong> You’ll work close to the founders and see how decisions are made across growth, product, sales, hiring and company building — while owning projects yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership:</strong> You won’t just support marketing. You will own initiatives end-to-end and have the freedom to propose and build things that don't exist yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An unusually steep learning curve:</strong> You’ll work across content, growth, brand, events, SEO, AI visibility and operations rather than spending months on one narrow internship project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional people around you:</strong> Work alongside experienced operators, ex-founders, engineers and top graduates from companies and universities such as Google, Bain, MIT, TUM, Harvard, CDTM and Cambridge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build something with real-world impact:</strong> Mercura brings modern AI into industries that still rely heavily on emails, PDFs, phone calls and manual ERP processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tools without bureaucracy:</strong> Get access to the AI, marketing and productivity tools you need to do great work, as well as expert support where it helps you move faster.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The everyday:</strong> Free team dinners, UrbanSportsClub membership, team workouts and support relocating to Munich.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 1: Intro Call</strong><br />A short conversation to get to know each other and tell you more about Mercura and the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 2: Practical Marketing Case</strong><br />A practical exercise around a real Mercura marketing challenge. We care much more about how you think, create and execute than theoretical marketing knowledge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 3: Offer</strong><br />If there is a strong mutual fit, we'll make you an offer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Founders</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are <strong>Lukas, Stefan &amp; Sean</strong>, the co-founders of Mercura. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We share a deep commitment to excellence and the discipline to pursue what others might consider impossible. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two of us come from non-academic families, and we all know what it means to create our own paths and overcome barriers. This experience shapes our belief in equal opportunity and fuels our dedication to social mobility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lukas</strong> (left) is responsible for business development at Mercura. With his background as a Data Scientist at Allianz and at Google in Silicon Valley, he brings extensive expertise in data and AI. <br />Lukas’ family has been active in the construction industry for over 100 years, giving him a deep understanding and passion for the sector's specific needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sean</strong> (middle) is responsible for technical development at Mercura. As a top 0.01% physicist, Sean earned a Silver medal for Germany at the International Physics Olympiad (IPhO), began researching with the Max Planck Institute at the age of 16, and has since published at leading machine learning conferences. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stefan</strong> (right) leads product development at Mercura. Previously, he worked in management consulting at Bain &amp; Company, where he helped manufacturers improve their operations. <br />Stefan leverages his research experience at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) and Harvard Business School to develop innovative solutions for the industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Mercura, we believe that the best ideas emerge when people from different backgrounds collaborate together. We hire based on ability, mindset, and values, and we live by one simple rule: the best idea wins.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beyond Mercura, we actively support initiatives that promote diversity and gender equity and commit a portion of our personal income each year to organizations expanding opportunity for others.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/aea8071f-e224-4680-b825-9d15c5a9df28/8836b971-88e3-4b84-bebc-66dc92a82ee7/founders-1-2%20(1).jpg" /></div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Our operating principles:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.mercura.ai/careers">https://www.mercura.ai/careers</a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mercura/founders-associate-intern-ops-marketing-munich-96656","tags":["Product & Operations"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792269620},{"slug":"director-of-go-to-market-engineering-berlin-429692","company_name":"Perk","title":"Director of Go-to-Market Engineering","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong><br /><br />Perk (formerly TravelPerk) is the intelligent platform for travel and spend management. Built to tackle the time-consuming, manual work that gets in the way of real work, our tools automate everything from travel bookings to expenses, invoice processing, and more. By eliminating this shadow work that wastes hours, erodes morale, and saps innovation, we're on a mission to power real work, with real impact.<br /><br />We're trusted by more than 12,000 companies worldwide, including Bolt, GoCardless, and Fabletics, and we're tackling the 7 hours of lost productivity per employee each week, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.perk.com/shadow-work-report">a $1.7 trillion problem</a>.<br /><br />Founded in 2015, Perk has grown into a global company of more than 1,800 people across 12 offices globally, with headquarters in London and Boston. We combine innovation, control, and simplicity to transform how businesses work and how people feel at work.<br /><br />At Perk, we're driven by our values, like being an owner, delivering a 7-star experience, and working as one team. We value curiosity, purpose, and mindset, not just knowledge, to unlock the power in your potential. Our talent team brings together leading minds from the travel, fintech, and SaaS industries, representing over 70 countries. If you're excited about having a real impact and shaping how millions of people experience work, we'd love you on the team.<br /><br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.perk.com">www.perk.com</a> to learn more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4899a966-8724-4480-958f-7271e5dc2807/f3e1915d-e346-4987-a1fb-9c447e8786c0" style="top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0" allowfullscreen scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><h2><br /><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring our <strong>first Director of Go-to-Market Engineering</strong>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk's revenue organisation is 800 people selling to more than 10,000 companies. Behind them sits a CRM, an enrichment and signal stack, a growing set of AI agents - and a lot of manual work that no longer needs to exist. Your job is to remove it and to build the automated systems that replace it.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own GTM Engineering end-to-end: which tools we use, how the architecture fits together, what gets built, and what it does for revenue. You report to the <strong>VP of Revenue Operations</strong>, lead a small senior team across Europe and North America, and work across SDR, Account Executive, and Account Management - a few high-impact projects each quarter.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>player-coach</strong> role, and we mean it. You will be in Clay, in the orchestration logic, in the agent workflows, building alongside a team doing the same. You're using your experience to guide and coach them to accelerate the pace.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The other half of the job is commercial. The best GTM engineers we have met can sit with a regional Sales VP, work out why their pipeline isn't converting, and leave with the right thing to build. That instinct matters more to us than any single tool on a CV.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong><br /></h2><h3><strong>Own the strategy and the stack</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define Perk's GTM engineering architecture - how CRM, enrichment, signal, sequencing, orchestration and data layers fit together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the tooling calls: what we adopt, what we consolidate, what we retire, and why it pays for itself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the roadmap with the VP of Revenue Operations, Sales leadership, and the Revenue Systems and Data teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish the standards the team builds to - version control, documentation, testing, and rollback.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Build, hands-on</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build in Clay: tables, waterfall enrichment, AI columns, webhooks and API integrations in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the orchestration layer - the logic deciding which records enter a workflow, when, and on what criteria. This is where GTM automation succeeds or fails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build agentic workflows on modern LLM and agent tooling to take research, qualification, summarisation and data entry off people entirely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write the code the job needs - Python, SQL, SOQL or TypeScript.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Automate across SDR, AE, and AM</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own account prospecting automation globally: TAM sourcing, enrichment, ICP and intent scoring, prioritisation and distribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Give AEs their selling time back - CRM autofill, quoting, meeting prep, opportunity hygiene, first outbounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build account intelligence for Account Management: risk signals, whitespace, account planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take each project from prototype to production properly - instrumented and validated before it scales.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bridge commercial and technical</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn commercial problems into technical architecture, and technical output into impact a revenue VPs recognises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand Perk's revenue goals and how to leverage AI capabilities for us to achieve them quicker and more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand and drive clear and tangible commercial outcomes. For example, how to reduce the time that quota-carrying roles spend on non-core activities such as account research, be able to quantify the impact, and clearly communicate the outcomes to leadership.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Build the team</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and grow a small, senior team across Europe and North America.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set clear ownership, and the review discipline that makes shipping fast also means shipping safely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow the team's technical depth and commercial judgement in equal measure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Will Make You Successful</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep background across Revenue Operations, GTM Engineering, Sales Systems, Growth Engineering, or an adjacent technical commercial function in B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record in GTM Engineering specifically, with delivery at real scale — systems hundreds of sellers relied on, not a pilot for one team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time as both a builder and a leader. This role needs both.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical craft</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clay expertise in production - complex tables, waterfall enrichment, webhook integrations and AI column logic that revenue teams actually depended on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep Salesforce fluency: the data model, integration patterns, and where the constraints really are.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working proficiency in code — Python, SQL, SOQL, TypeScript or equivalent. You pull your own data. Not all coding languages are necessary, but proficiency in one or some is required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecture instincts: you build for scale, monitoring and recovery, not just for the first successful run.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depth across several layers of the modern GTM stack - enrichment and data (Apollo, Clearbit, ZoomInfo, Cognism, PredictLeads), signal and intent (6sense, Bombora, UserGems), sequencing (Outreach, Salesloft), orchestration (n8n, Make, Workato), data infrastructure (Snowflake, dbt, BigQuery) and LLM and agent tooling. Nobody has all of it. We care that you have real depth somewhere and can learn the rest quickly.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commercial instinct</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You judge your work by whether it moved a commercial metric, not by whether it shipped.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have the credibility with Sales leaders to scope the right build - and to say when automation is the wrong answer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the funnel end to end: TAM, ICP, pipeline generation, conversion, expansion, and the economics underneath.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Having stood up a GTM engineering function at a high-growth SaaS business, ideally above $100M ARR.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking an automation programme from pilot to global production, including what you learned when it got bumpy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multi-region GTM experience across EMEA and North America.</p></li></ul><h2></h2><h2><strong>Why This Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">GTM Engineering is a discipline being written right now, and most companies are still treating it as a tooling function. This is the chance to own it properly,  the stack, the architecture, the build, and the commercial outcome across a $300M+ revenue business with 800 people in the field, a genuine appetite for automation, and the budget and executive backing to move fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You would be the first person in this seat, with real systems and real data to work with rather than a blank page, and the freedom to decide what Perk's automation layer should look like. There is a lot to go after, the problems are interesting, and the impact is immediate and visible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to build the automation layer of a commercial engine at this scale and you want to still have your hands on it  come and build it here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Perk</strong><br />AI is embedded in how we work across every function. The tools you'll use day-to-day are AI-enabled so you can move faster and spend more time on the work that matters. In practice, that means using AI to research and prioritise accounts, draft and refine outreach, handle customer interactions more effectively, synthesise information, and cut through shadow work - the invisible tasks that pull people away from the work only they can do - so you can focus on relationships and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Perk, we take an IRL-first approach to work, where our team works together in-person 3 days a week. As such, this role requires you to be based within commuting distance of our hubs. We fundamentally believe in the value of meeting in real life to improve connectivity, productivity, creativity and ultimately making us a great place to work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For certain roles, we can help with relocation from anywhere in the world, English is the official language at the office. Please submit your resume in English if you choose to apply. Do not forget to submit an updated portfolio and/or resume.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk is a global company with a diverse customer base, and we want to make sure the people behind our product reflect that. We’re an equal opportunity employer, which means you’re welcome at Perk regardless of how you look, where you’re from, or anything else that makes you, well, you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All official communication from Perk will always come from email addresses ending in @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://perk.com">perk.com</a> or @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://externalperk.com">externalperk.com</a>, our verified social media channels, or recruiters listed on our official LinkedIn page. We will never ask you to pay for equipment, training, or fees, request sensitive personal information such as bank details early in the process, or communicate through unofficial apps like WhatsApp, Telegram, or Signal. If you receive a message claiming to be from Perk that seems suspicious, please do not respond. Forward it to <u>security [at] perk .com</u>, and we will confirm whether it is legitimate.<br /><br />#LI-Hybrid</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/perk/director-of-go-to-market-engineering-berlin-429692","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792269617},{"slug":"business-development-and-gtm-lead-preseed-proptech-rudi-berlin-9105","company_name":"Founders Factory","title":"Business Development and GTM Lead - PreSeed Proptech (Rudi)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Rudi is building the AI knowledge and decision layer for the skilled trades.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, diagnosing a technical fault often depends on who happens to be on site. Experienced Meisters rely on years of tacit knowledge, technical documentation and intuition. Less experienced technicians frequently need additional visits or senior support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rudi makes that expertise available to every technician and across trades. Our AI assistant guides technicians through diagnosis and repair, combines manufacturer knowledge with real service experience, and learns from the outcome of every job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make every technician perform closer to the best Meister in the organisation — and ultimately build the intelligence layer for technical field services across the skilled trades.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rudi is being built with Founders Factory and a large European residential and field service organisation. The first product is already being tested with experienced Meisters, with live field pilots starting shortly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to validate Rudi's commercial potential beyond our launch partner, identify promising customer segments and build an initial sales pipeline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role focused on customer outreach, commercial validation and early sales opportunities — not a desk research or purely strategic consulting assignment. We're looking for someone who is comfortable approaching new customers, testing commercial assumptions and turning conversations into concrete next steps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer outreach &amp; commercial validation.</strong> Identify and engage potential customers across housing companies, technical service providers and installation businesses. Understand their operational challenges, buying processes and willingness to pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build an initial sales pipeline.</strong> Reach relevant decision-makers, run discovery and sales conversations, and develop promising contacts into concrete pilot or commercial opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GTM strategy &amp; business case.</strong> Identify priority customer segments, test pricing and positioning, and develop a pragmatic GTM recommendation supported by a credible customer ROI case.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we are looking for</strong></h2></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are commercially sharp, entrepreneurial and comfortable operating in the uncertainty of an early-stage startup. You know how to develop a sales strategy, but more importantly, you know how to execute it. You are a team player who enjoys a collaborative environment and working together with the co-founder team that is developing Rudi.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven B2B sales and GTM experience, ideally gained in early-stage startups or through consulting assignments with multiple startups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of conducting external commer