t:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Your tasks</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the campaigns from start to finish. Bring the right people in the room together from the product kickoff onwards, so we get the best concepts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write the campaign briefs, with objectives, targets and all the details needed to approve before kick-off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chase for the deliverables. Manage our marketing channel stakeholders (Creative, storytelling, assets, product copy, influencer briefs, landing pages, CRM flows, retail materials, market adaptation) and keep everyone on the same brief and dates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adapt per market, working with the country leads on what changes locally, ensuring we are agile and localize the campaigns accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are responsible for ensuring that we are ready before go-live. Detail oriented and escalating proactively if anything is missing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the process light and current. Maintain the Notion campaign templates, the RACI and campaign pages so everyone has the information needed to succeed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Put together all learnings and results post-campaigns together. Ensure we have inputs from all teams and stakeholders. The post-mortem is based on evidence,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring in market trends, competitor promotions and cultural moments to sharpen every campaign</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan for every channel according to the calendar: Sephora, Amazon and TikTok Shop alongside our own sites, with assets, timing and price parity aligned.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Your profile</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5 years in advertising (account or strategy side), or in growth or campaign marketing at a D2C brand. You know how to hold others accountable and are detail oriented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have delivered multi-channel, multi-market campaigns on time and can show the plans behind them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can write and judge headlines, hooks and CTAs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work well with Brand and Creative teams, hold the commercial line without friction, and align people you don’t manage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in revenue, sell-through, AOV and margin, and can argue why one offer beats another</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership, bring solutions and keep process light</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; a second EU language is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beauty or D2C experience is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>What We Offer</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dynamic Environment:</strong> The opportunity to work in a start-up environment surrounded by a passionate and dedicated team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accelerate Your Career:</strong> Take on responsibility from day 1, with room for professional growth and advancement as the company continues to expand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inspiring Workspace</strong>: Located in the heart of Berlin's Prenzlauer Berg, a dog-friendly office, with free drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid Working: </strong>We understand that sometimes you get more stuff done from home and need a change of scenery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We Value Diversity: </strong>We seek to build an inclusive workplace that welcomes people from all different backgrounds. A welcoming, international, dedicated team with flat hierarchies and trust by default.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee Discounts: </strong>You’ll get to enjoy the Yepoda products at a discount and share it with friends and family to keep your glow going!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unique Add Ons:</strong> A monthly benefits budget that's yours to spend. Through the Probonio app you pick what actually fits your lifestyle.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Would you like to be part of the team? Then we'd love to hear from you! 🫰✨</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure to apply by clicking on the “Apply for this job” button below. Please upload your CV and Cover Letter in English language. Our Talent Acquisition team will review your application and get back to you as soon as possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Yepoda we are dedicated to providing equal employment opportunities to all individuals, regardless of race, color, ethnicity, ancestry, religion, national origin, citizenship, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, parental status, disability, or any other status protected by applicable law.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/yepoda/campaign-manager-berlin-119461","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792269616},{"slug":"senior-process-development-engineer-2d-growth-aachen-13470","company_name":"Black Semiconductor GmbH","title":"Senior Process Development Engineer - 2D growth","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Process Development Engineer – 2D growth, you will lead high-temperature thermal processing, tool qualification and graphene-synthesis baseline development for FabONE.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will drive the release and optimization of 2D-material growth processes, improve thermal-film properties, and establish stable, repeatable graphene-growth recipes. Working on site in our Aachen cleanroom, you will collaborate with Process Integration and Metrology teams to integrate thermal processes into downstream GFET and optical modules.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead high-temperature process development, layer property mapping and recipe optimization for graphene and other 2D materials</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive tool installation, commissioning, process qualification and system optimization in FabONE</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop, qualify and stabilize repeatable graphene-growth recipes that meet defect-density and film properties specifications</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the integration of graphene growth and transfer processes on target 300 mm substrate wafers</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish SPC baseline charts and routine characterization protocols for daily process monitoring</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Design of Experiments (DOE), SPC and root-cause analysis to improve process performance and resolve process and/or equipment issues</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Process Integration and Metrology teams on film characterization using techniques such as Raman spectroscopy, optical microscopy, sheet-resistance measurement, AFM and SEM</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support inline defect reduction and the continuous improvement of process yield and stability</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create SOPs, safety protocols and technical documentation to reduce single-point-of-failure risks</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-train team members to establish reliable operational coverage for furnace processes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in high-temperature furnace operations and thermal processing</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with semiconductor process development, process control and baseline stabilization in a cleanroom fab environment</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CVD synthesis of graphene or other 2D materials is a strong advantage</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Thermal Furnace processes is an advantage</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of commissioning and qualifying process tools and releasing processes into operation</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using SPC and DOE methodologies, including tools such as JMP or Minitab</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with thin-film characterization techniques, including sheet-resistance measurement, Raman spectroscopy, optical microscopy, AFM or SEM</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem-solving and root-cause analysis skills for process and equipment troubleshooting</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work across multidisciplinary engineering teams</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in an ISO 5/6 cleanroom while wearing full cleanroom PPE</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable handling wafer cassettes, precursor canisters and high-temperature furnace hardware</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to establish graphene-growth processes for FabONE from qualification through stable operation</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on, cleanroom-based role working with high-temperature processing and 2D-material technologies</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A potential career path towards the Senior IC or Technical Principal track, leading the thermal and 2D-material deposition technology roadmap, or towards engineering management leadership</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our work culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People Over Processes.</strong> At Black Semiconductor, flexibility is key - we ensure work adapts to life, not the other way around. We champion work-life harmony, where careers are meaningful and enriching. Our processes are human-centric, allowing you to focus on what matters</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Let’s grow together.</strong> Your potential is our priority. We provide the autonomy to make a lasting impact and nurture your growth through a culture of continuous learning. We invest in your journey for professional and personal development</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Health and Future Matter.</strong> Your well-being is paramount. We offer a comprehensive benefits package with outstanding insurance, pension and virtual stock options for your mental, physical, and financial health. Your peace of mind is our priority - in the present and future</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We Live Openness.</strong> Collaboration and inclusivity are the cornerstones of our culture. We practice openness, fostering trust and respect. Individuality is our collective strength, fueling innovation and driving us forward</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We connect chips – and people.</strong> We encourage qualified individuals from any background to apply. We foster an inclusive and supportive work environment that values collaboration, innovation, and growth. Join our team and be part of an organization dedicated to making a difference in the industry</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Can you picture yourself in this Role and our Company? Let’s connect!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If your application results in an employment relationship, your Applicant Data will be transferred to our personnel records and processed in accordance with applicable legal requirements; otherwise, your Applicant Data will be retained for up to six (6) months after completion of the recruitment process. </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.blacksemi.com/privacy-policy"><em>Read more about our privacy policy here. </em></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/black-semiconductor-gmbh/senior-process-development-engineer-2d-growth-aachen-13470","tags":["Fab Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Aachen, Germany","created_at":1792269615},{"slug":"gtm-growth-engineer-berlin-423784","company_name":"Cosuno","title":"GTM & Growth Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cosuno is a platform for construction tendering in the German-speaking market. It connects general contractors, who publish bid packages, with subcontractors, who bid on them, and both sides pay. As our GTM &amp; Growth Engineer, you build the automation and data behind marketing and growth. You find where work is manual or where data goes unused, build a solution that works in one area, such as paid marketing, lifecycle, sales handovers or content, and then reuse it across the others. You work closely with our Senior Lifecycle &amp; Customer Growth Manager, the Demand Generation Manager and the Marketing Lead, and you ship things with a business outcome attached, not infrastructure for its own sake. You'll be the first engineer in a lean marketing team: you'll shape how our growth stack is built, not just maintain a fixed setup.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You automate marketing and lifecycle operations: triggers, segments, workflows and personalization in ActiveCampaign and Salesforce, so journeys react to what customers do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You automate paid marketing: audience syncs and suppression from CRM and product data, conversion data fed back to the ad platforms, and campaign feeds and landing pages that adapt to where bids are missing on the Marketplace. Demand Generation owns strategy and budget; you build the machinery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build the data and signal plumbing: product events, Salesforce, ActiveCampaign, enrichment, transaction history and our BigQuery warehouse, connected, clean and usable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You automate creative production: ad, email and landing-page variants inside our brand templates, with human review before anything goes live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build once and reuse everywhere: what works in one area becomes a reusable capability for paid, lifecycle, sales and content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You find the manual work and the unused data, such as reporting, list building, call transcripts and enrichment, and replace it with automation and LLM-based tools, including the content engine for SEO and AI search.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You give the team fast experimentation: reusable test set-ups, holdouts and measurement, so tests launch in days, not weeks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You launch with care: human checks in every automation, proof against a control or holdout before you scale, and a launch plan with scope, review steps, rollout and rollback.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built marketing or growth automation that runs in production: paid media integrations, CRM and lifecycle workflows, data pipelines, ideally in B2B SaaS or a two-sided business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're hands-on with APIs, webhooks and automation tools such as n8n, Make, Zapier or Clay; Python or TypeScript and SQL are a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know ad platform and CRM data: audiences, conversion tracking and the limits of attribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've shipped LLM-based or agentic automation into a real workflow, not just used AI to write copy faster.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in outcomes: a working use case in two weeks beats a platform in six months, and you measure what you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're careful with what goes live: you check outputs by hand, test against a control before you trust a result, and plan launches step by step with a way back.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work well with marketers and explain trade-offs plainly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; German is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Room to shape and grow:</strong> The first engineer in Marketing, deciding how our growth stack is built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at the core:</strong> Our product uses AI to analyze millions of price data points and help construction companies bid better — and we invest in it just as much internally. You'll build with the latest tools and move fast, not wait for approval.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation:</strong> Salary above market average, permanent contract in a stable, well-funded company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work-life balance:</strong> Fully remote or from our office in Berlin Kreuzberg, flexible hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Top-notch equipment:</strong> A new MacBook Pro.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A great team:</strong> Open, international, with regular off-sites and team events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth &amp; feedback:</strong> Open feedback culture with regular 1:1s and development conversations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cosuno – Revolutionizing construction through technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Cosuno – a fast-growing tech startup that is making the construction industry more efficient and transparent with our digital platform for tenders and procurement processes. Our goal: to solve the most complex challenges in the industry with innovation and simplicity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us – Build the future of construction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €70K – €80K</p><ul><li> • €70K – €80K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cosuno/gtm-growth-engineer-berlin-423784","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin/Remote","created_at":179