tner Manager for Spain & Portugal - Gastronomy (m/w/d)","description":"<p>Every day, owners, waitstaff and chefs pour their hearts into crafting dining experiences. Yet they are expected to keep up in an always-on world with relentless technological change.</p><p>We build solutions for them to keep up – and yes, with AI. But not for the sake of it.</p><p><strong>What you sell</strong></p><p>Assistent.ai is the AI Suite for Guest Communication, purpose-built for hospitality teams. It answers and converts calls to reservations, orders or tasks – on live data, connected knowledge, and on brand.</p><p>We are looking for a Sales & Partner Manager for Spain and Portugal.</p><ul><li><p>Location: Remote in Germany, with regular travel to Spain and Portugal</p></li><li><p>Start: As soon as possible</p></li><li><p>Employment: Full-time, or part-time from 50% with a path to full-time</p></li></ul><p><strong>How we sell</strong></p><p>We actively listen, understand and work out solutions. We do not push where there is no problem to solve. We build long term, trustworthy relationships. We value lifetime value over shortsighted gains.</p><p>Hit apply if you're humble to learn, ambitious to win, and have a weakness for Iberian food and culture.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p><strong>Open Spain and Portugal. Win restaurants. Build partners.</strong></p><p>You're our first person for Spain and Portugal. No team to hide behind, no playbook to follow. You write it.</p><p>You win restaurants: on the phone, on video calls and in person.</p><p>You win partners: reservation systems that make real-time automation possible, and distributors who already reach the restaurants we want.</p><p>You get restaurants on board, make sure they're up and running, and help them grow with Assistent.ai.</p><p>You are our customers' voice inside the company.</p><p>It's that simple. And that hard.</p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>You have agency: you see what's missing and get things done.</p></li><li><p>You win trust before you win deals.</p></li><li><p>Clear communication is your leverage.</p></li><li><p>You have 'skin in the game' – from a background in Hospitality Tech Sales or your own Front of House experience in a hotel, restaurant or café.</p></li><li><p>We value hands-on work over diplomas. What matters: you're confident with numbers and understand how local businesses work.</p></li><li><p>You speak Spanish at a native level.</p></li><li><p>You are fluent in Portuguese and English, German would be a big plus.</p></li><li><p>We build technology and work with it daily, so we need you to pick up new tools fast.</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Your own markets to grow – both personally and professionally.</p></li><li><p>A bootstrapped, founder-led atmosphere.</p></li><li><p>You earn a competitive fixed salary plus uncapped commission.</p></li><li><p>Remote with a flexible schedule, as long as it works for our prospects, customers and partners.</p></li><li><p>Latest MacBook and the software stack you need to do your best work.</p></li></ul><p></p><p>We decide fast – apply with your CV and we get in touch with you immediately.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/assistentai-software-gmbh/sales-partner-manager-for-spain-portugal-gastronomy-berlin-343976","tags":["Remote","Business Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792247450},{"slug":"business-development-intern-gtm-cologne-177243","company_name":"Ordio GmbH","title":"Business Development Intern (GTM) (m/f/d)","description":"<h2>About Ordio</h2><p>80% of the world’s workforce doesn’t sit at a desk, yet most software is built for the 20% who do. Ordio is the AI-native workforce management (WFM) system for deskless workforces: shift planning, time tracking and payroll for the people who keep restaurants, shops and services running.</p><h2>The role</h2><p>This is not a “support the team and update spreadsheets” internship. You’ll help find out where Ordio’s next stage of growth comes from, and then make it happen. You get real problems and the tools to solve them, and nobody tells you how.</p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Find new growth levers and revenue streams.</strong> Spot opportunities and take them from 0 to 1 and beyond: analyze, test, iterate, scale</p></li><li><p><strong>Understand the problem first.</strong> Talk to customers, map markets and figure out what deskless businesses actually struggle with</p></li><li><p><strong>Get to product-market fit in new verticals.</strong> Find out which industries need Ordio most, validate quickly and build the go-to-market for them</p></li><li><p><strong>Drive geographical expansion.</strong> Evaluate new markets, size the opportunity and build the playbook for entering them</p></li><li><p><strong>Build AI-powered GTM engines.</strong> Automate research, enrichment and outbound with Clay, HubSpot, LLMs and whatever else works</p></li><li><p><strong>Work directly with the founders</strong> on strategy, and own at least one initiative end-to-end</p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><ul><li><p>High agency: you don’t wait for instructions, you figure it out and ship</p></li><li><p>Obsessed with understanding problems, customers and markets before jumping to solutions</p></li><li><p>You already use AI tools beyond ChatGPT prompts, e.g. agents and automations</p></li><li><p>Analytical and numbers-driven, comfortable making decisions with incomplete data</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German and English</p></li><li><p>Student (Bachelor/Master), available for 3–6 months, full-time</p></li></ul><h2>What you get</h2><ul><li><p>Real ownership and visible impact from week one</p></li><li><p>Access to every AI tool you need</p></li><li><p>Founder-level exposure: you sit where strategy and growth decisions are made, and you help make them</p></li><li><p>A front-row seat to building the AI-native category in workforce management</p></li><li><p>Fair internship pay of €2,500 </p></li><li><p>Modern office in Cologne and top-notch equipment</p></li></ul><h2><strong>How to apply</strong></h2><p>Apply with your CV and 2–3 sentences about the coolest thing you’ve built with AI (a link is even better).</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/ordio-gmbh/business-development-intern-gtm-cologne-177243","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":["Internship (praktikum)","internship","no experience required / student"],"location":"Cologne","created_at":1792238465},{"slug":"account-executive-enterprise-366148","company_name":"conga","title":"Account Executive, Enterprise","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;A career that’s the whole package!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Conga, we’ve built a community where our colleagues can thrive. Here you’ll find opportunities to innovate and support growth through individual and team development, all within an environment where every voice is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conga&lt;/strong&gt; lines up commercial operations so companies run as connected, smarter businesses. By unifying the people and processes that drive commerce, Conga aligns pricing, quoting, contracting, rebates, and communications so teams stay in sync and buyers keep moving forward. The result is trusted decisions, consistent buyer experiences, and profitable growth. More than 10,000 customers worldwide, including over 50% of the Fortune 100®, trust Conga when commercial complexity is high and global impact is on the line.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Germany (remote)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: &lt;/strong&gt;RVP Sales&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages: &lt;/strong&gt;native/C2 level German and English&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Quick Snapshot…..&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive,&amp;nbsp;you&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;be at the forefront of our revenue growth strategy, spearheading efforts to uncover and nurture new business prospects while strengthening connections with our current clientele. Your role will involve deeply understanding client requirements, crafting personalized solutions, and ensuring top-notch customer satisfaction. Collaborating closely with Sales Engineering, Business/Sales Development, Marketing, Transformation Specialists,&amp;nbsp;Customer Success, Professional Services, Partners&amp;nbsp;and clients, your primary focus will be on&amp;nbsp;prospecting, managing and closing new business opportunities for enterprise-wide CONGA solutions with organizations across a variety of key strategic industries/verticals in the B2B space.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it’s big deal…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have the chance to sell high-impact, mission-critical projects with substantial value, driving transformational change for our clients in Central Europe. Your role will involve skillfully crafting and implementing territory, account, and opportunity plans to optimize revenue within your assigned selling patch. You&#39;ll expertly manage sales opportunities throughout every stage of the cycle, ensuring success for both our clients and our company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you the person we are looking for?  &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven&amp;nbsp;track record.&lt;/strong&gt;  You have at least 5 years successful B2B technology Enterprise sales experience in the SaaS industry, in Central Europe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency&amp;nbsp;in revenue management principles is crucial.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a consistent track record of&amp;nbsp;over achieving&amp;nbsp;quota and revenue targets. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You cultivate and&amp;nbsp;leverage&amp;nbsp;strategic relationships with partners to drive mutual business growth and success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience in general AI and machine learning can bring significant value. You understand how AI can enhance revenue management processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hunter mentality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;have the opportunity to unleash your inner hunter and drive our growth through relentless pursuit of new business opportunities. You thrive in a fast-paced environment,&amp;nbsp;leveraging&amp;nbsp;your strategic mindset and tenacity to&amp;nbsp;identify, pursue, and close deals with potential clients. The focus is 90%&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Selling. &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with prospects and clients to understand their unique challenges and business goals. Present Conga&#39;s comprehensive suite of solutions and services that align with clients&#39; needs,&amp;nbsp;demonstrating&amp;nbsp;a deep understanding of how Conga can provide value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;You have the ability to successfully leverage resources and take initiative. The most successful Conga reps are the ones who stop at nothing to achieve success no matter the&amp;nbsp;circumstance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: You have the ability to articulate complex technology concepts to a technical and non-technical audience.&amp;nbsp;You also have superb listening&amp;nbsp;skills&amp;nbsp;and you understand objections and overcome them by turning skeptics into enthusiastic new customers and brand ambassadors. You&amp;nbsp;possess&amp;nbsp;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Mindset&lt;/strong&gt;. As the business landscape is constantly&amp;nbsp;evolving&amp;nbsp;you adapt to changes in market conditions, customer preferences, and competitive dynamics. You innovate and develop creative solutions to address challenges and capitalize on opportunities in the revenue management space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;You&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;work closely with cross-functional teams including Sales Engineering, Business Development, Marketing, and Customer Success to deliver exceptional value to our clients and drive mutual success. Together,&amp;nbsp;we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;leverage&amp;nbsp;each other&#39;s&amp;nbsp;expertise&amp;nbsp;and insights to achieve our goals and surpass expectations.&amp;nbsp;You have the gravitas to lead a winning team,&amp;nbsp;leveraging&amp;nbsp;the strengths and skills of the organization to deliver profitable business to the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will give you an edge...&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience selling Revenue Lifecycle Management solutions with a good understanding of CPQ,&amp;nbsp;revenue optimization,&amp;nbsp;CLM, doc-gen and e-signature products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Education and/or experience in Economics, Statistics, Mathematics, Accounting, Marketing, Finance, or Operations Research considered a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Did we pique your interest? &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like the kind of job you would love in the kind of environment where you would thrive, please click apply. &lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you! &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Resume Format&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We accept resumes in any format, we suggest using PDF or plain text. These formats help ensure that your resume’s formatting remains intact, making it easier for our recruiters to review your application promptly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don’t meet every requirement for the role?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and members of ethnic minorities are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every single qualification. At Conga we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace, so if you’re excited about this role but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You just might be the right candidate for this or other roles. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;section id=&quot;st-additionalInformation&quot; class=&quot;job-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Additional Information&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;wysiwyg&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conga is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, parental or pregnancy status, marriage and civil partnership, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. We understand interviewing can be stressful for those with disabilities. If reasonable accommodation is needed to allow you to show us your best self, please let your recruiter know as soon as possible. All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines. Conga is not open to third party solicitation or resumes for our posted FTE positions. Resumes received from third party agencies that are unsolicited will be considered complimentary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;job-apply print-hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conga&#39;s Applicant Privacy Statement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The information you provide during the application process will be used in accordance with Conga’s Applicant Privacy Statement (&lt;a href=&quot;https://conga.com/applicant-privacy-statement&quot;&gt;https://conga.com/applicant-privacy-statement&lt;/a&gt;). By submitting your application, you acknowledge and agree to the terms outlined in this privacy statement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/conga/account-executive-enterprise-366148","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792238116},{"slug":"working-student-academics-104947","company_name":"Think Cell","title":"Working student Academics (f/m/d)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Story&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At thinkcell, we create powerful software solutions that help professionals be more efficient and productive. Founded in 2002 and based in Berlin, our tools integrate seamlessly with Microsoft Office to help users create presentations, charts, and diagrams with ease. Our dynamic, international team values creativity, collaboration, and technical excellence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Working Student in our Academics team&lt;/strong&gt;, you will support the day-to-day operations and growth of thinkcell’s academic program. You will work on a broad range of tasks, from handling program requests and supporting outreach to coordinating workshops and improving processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our academic program gives students and professors free access to thinkcell and helps them develop practical skills in data visualization and storytelling. You will help us bring these opportunities to more universities, faculty members, and student clubs worldwide (find out more &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.think-cell.com/en/order/academics&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;). We have big plans to grow the program significantly with the next years – and you can be apart of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support program operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Help manage our academic inbox, respond to student and faculty inquiries, and coordinate license requests, renewals, and extensions with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review new applications&lt;/strong&gt;: Research faculty members and institutions, assess eligibility against program guidelines, and prepare responses and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support academic outreach&lt;/strong&gt;: Identify relevant professors and student clubs, draft personalized outreach, and follow up with existing contacts to build engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate workshops&lt;/strong&gt;: Work with student clubs and faculty to schedule workshops, organize logistics, and keep contact information up to date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute across the team&lt;/strong&gt;: Support ongoing projects and ad hoc tasks, taking ownership of defined activities as you gain experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You will be great for this position if you have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Studies&lt;/strong&gt;: Currently enrolled in business, computer science, or a related field, with at least two years of university studies completed – undergraduate degree is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset &amp;amp; Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive and comfortable working independently, with strong problem-solving skills and a keen eye for detail. Well organized, reliable, and able to prioritize tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Office&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficient in Microsoft Office, especially Excel and PowerPoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Availability &amp;amp; Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Available for 20 hours per week, including at least two days per week at our headquarters in Berlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presentation experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience creating presentations in PowerPoint is a strong plus; familiarity with thinkcell is an added advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As part of our team, you will embody and help shape the following principles that define us:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Forward Thinking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: We embrace change and challenge the status quo.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Ownership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: We take pride in our work and learn from our mistakes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Customer First&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: We prioritize delivering lasting value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Unified Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: We foster collaboration, respect, and integrity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strive for Excellence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;: We set ambitious goals and pursue quality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in a human hiring process, every application is personally reviewed.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Why is thinkcell the right place for you?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We empower over 1.3 million users across 35,000 companies, including top consulting firms and major global enterprises. With offices in Berlin, Munich, Denver, Boston, London, Tokyo, and Dubai, we’re a diverse team of over 240 people, committed to innovation and excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;thinkcell is more than a job – it&#39;s a chance to be part of an innovative, inclusive team that values collaboration and growth. We encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply. Together, we can shape the future of productivity software. We can’t wait to see what you’ll bring to the team!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/think-cell/working-student-academics-104947","tags":["Strategy & Corporation Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792238114},{"slug":"marketing-associate-special-projects-events-berlin-497425","company_name":"trawa","title":"Marketing Associate – Special Projects & Events","description":"<h1><strong>Marketing Associate – Special Projects &amp; Events</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Festanstellung · Vollzeit · Berlin (HQ)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unsere Mission für dich</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du baust den Kanal, über den trawa dem industriellen Mittelstand begegnet: mehr als 30 Messen, Kongresse und Roundtables im Jahr, von der fünftägigen Leitmesse bis zum Fachkongress auf sechs Quadratmetern. Du entscheidest mit, welche davon stattfinden, führst sie durch und stehst für das Ergebnis ein.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Es bleibt nicht beim Stand. Du baust die Landingpage, bewirbst die Events in Paid und Content und schreibst den LinkedIn-Post zur Messewoche. In kurzer Zeit kennst du den kompletten Weg von der Standfläche bis zur Opportunity im CRM — eine Breite, die dir ein großes Marketingteam nicht bietet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Europas B2B-Sektor gibt jährlich über 200 Milliarden Euro für Energie aus. Die Zeit, diesen Markt zu dekarbonisieren und unsere Markenbekanntheit zu steigern, ist jetzt.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Das Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neben dir sitzen Content, Growth und Product Marketing — Events sind der Kanal, an dem alle drei zusammenlaufen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gleichzeitig bist du näher an Sales als die meisten Marketingrollen. Auf jeder Messe stehen Seller mit am Stand, und der Wert eines Events entsteht erst, wenn aus Gesprächen Termine werden. Du stimmst dich laufend mit Sales, SDRs und Revenue Operations ab.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Du ownst den Eventkalender. </strong>Welche Messe, welches Format, welches Budget. Du planst das Jahr, rechnest jedes Event durch und sagst ab, wenn die Zahl nicht stimmt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Du baust den Auftritt. </strong>Standfläche, Standbau, Grafik, Technik, Logistik. Du verhandelst mit Messegesellschaften und Dienstleistern, hältst die Fristen ein und stehst vor Ort selbst am Stand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Du machst aus Standtagen Termine. </strong>Einladungskampagnen, Teilnehmerlisten, Matchmaking, Terminsetzung vorab. Danach: Lead-Erfassung, Nachfass und Übergabe an Sales entlang eines klaren SLA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Du misst deine eigene Arbeit. </strong>Landingpages, Formulare, HubSpot-Workflows, Lead-Tagging und Reporting baust du selbst — und berichtest MQLs, Pipeline und Signings je Event gegen Plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Du bleibst nicht bei Events. </strong>Newsletter, LinkedIn, PR und eigene Formate gehören dazu, bis hin zu Guerilla-Experimenten wie Briefkampagnen oder OOH. Was funktioniert, wiederholen wir.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nach wem wir suchen</strong></p><h3><strong> </strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein bis vier Jahre B2B-Marketing mit Schwerpunkt Events oder Messen, gern mit Bezug zum deutschen Mittelstand</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bist extrovertiert: Auf dem Stand gehst du auf Menschen zu, statt zu warten, bis jemand stehen bleibt. Viele Gespräche am Tag geben dir Energie</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du behältst den Überblick, wenn ein Dutzend Dienstleister und mehrere Messen parallel laufen – und eskalierst rechtzeitig</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du denkst kaufmännisch und bewertest ein Event an dem, was es an Pipeline bringt</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du baust dir Landingpage, Formular und Reporting selbst</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bias to Action: lieber schnell testen und messen als lange konzipieren</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deutsch muttersprachlich, gutes Englisch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Berlin oder Umzug dorthin, plus Reisebereitschaft in der Messesaison und einen Führerschein</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deine ersten 90 Tage:</strong></p><h3>Nach sechs Wochen: Onboarding</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast trawas Geschäftsmodell, Produkt und Zielgruppe im Detail verstanden und alle relevanten Stakeholder in Marketing und Sales kennengelernt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast das laufende Eventportfolio übernommen, kennst jeden offenen Punkt und jede Frist und hast die Abläufe dokumentiert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du warst auf allen Messen vor Ort, die in dieser Zeit stattfanden, und hast konkrete Verbesserungen benannt und erste Verantwortung übernommen.</p></li></ul><h3>Im dritten Monat: Ramp-up</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du verantwortest eigene Key Results im neuen Planungszyklus und lässt dich an den erzielten Ergebnissen messen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast die Planung für das kommende Halbjahr aufgesetzt, jedes Event durchgerechnet und einen Entscheidungsvorschlag vorgelegt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein wiederverwendbarer Ablauf steht: Vorlauf, Aktivierung, Lead-Erfassung, Nachfass — nachvollziehbar genug, dass jemand anderes ihn ausführen könnte..</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Warum wir?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gestalte mit uns die Zukunft der Energiewirtschaft und treibe eigenverantwortlich Projekte voran, die echten Einfluss auf unsere Produkte, unsere Kund:innen und die Umwelt haben.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dein Impact:</strong> Jede Messe bringt uns mit Unternehmen zusammen, deren Energiekosten wir senken und deren Verbrauch wir dekarbonisieren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Gestaltungsspielraum:</strong> Das Event-Marketing bei trawa ist im Aufbau. Du erbst keine fertigen Strukturen, sondern etablierst sie.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibles Arbeiten:</strong> Dich erwartet ein schönes Büro in Berlin mit einer lebendigen Unternehmenskultur. Homeoffice und flexible Arbeitszeiten sind möglich, 30 Urlaubstage unterstützen deine Work-Life-Balance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Attraktive Benefits:</strong> Neben einem wettbewerbsfähigen Gehalt erhältst du Essensgutscheine, eine Urban-Sports-Mitgliedschaft, reichlich kostenlose Snacks und ein persönliches Weiterbildungsbudget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Persönliche Entwicklung:</strong> Weiterbildungstage, ein jährliches L&amp;D-Budget und Coaching-Sessions über Sparrks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vielfalt und Inklusion:</strong> Bei uns sind alle willkommen. Wir setzen uns für einen inklusiven Arbeitsplatz ein, der Vielfalt wertschätzt, und ermutigen Menschen unabhängig von Geschlecht, Alter, sexueller Orientierung, ethnischer und sozialer Herkunft sowie körperlicher oder neurodiverser Vielfalt zur Bewerbung.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wenn du strategisch denkst, operativ stark bist und gerne Verantwortung übernimmst, dann bewirb dich jetzt! Auch wenn du nicht alle Anforderungen zu 100 % erfüllst: Wir sind offen für Persönlichkeiten mit Potenzial und Leidenschaft.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über uns</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willkommen im trawa-Universum! Wir haben es uns zur Aufgabe gemacht, das grüne Versorgungsunternehmen der Zukunft von Grund auf aufzubauen. Wie machen wir das? Wir schaffen einen direkten Zugang zu erneuerbarer Energie für B2B-Industrieunternehmen. Wir entwickeln Software und Technologie, um die Volatilität des Energiemarktes zu bewältigen. Wir professionalisieren die Energiebeschaffung auf der Käuferseite.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/trawa/marketing-associate-special-projects-events-berlin-497425","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin HQ","created_at":1792237218},{"slug":"senior-associate-energy-markets-business-development-railway-power-ppas-berlin-26883","company_name":"trawa","title":"(Senior) Associate – Energy Markets & Business Development (Railway Power & PPAs)","description":"<h1>(Senior) Associate – Energy Markets &amp; Business Development (Railway Power &amp; PPAs)<br /><br /></h1><h2><strong>Our mission for you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">European energy costs are 2x compared to US and China. Electricity demand is expected to double by 2050. Market price volatility &amp; complexity are here to stay. The backbone of Europe's industrial economy is at risk - and companies need to act now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">trawa is building the solution: the first integrated B2B energy platform that orchestrates procurement, energy management, and flexibility steering in one product. Supply, Manage, Flex - combined. That integration unlocks up to 30% in recurring electricity cost savings - all while helping companies switch to renewable energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're the fastest-growing B2B energy platform in Europe. Active in Germany and Austria now, and expanding operations to a third market in 2027. We're on the road to European scale and move fast - the market window is open and we intend to own it.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>About trawa</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">trawa is a scale-up based in Berlin with ~100 FTE, ~30 of whom work in Product &amp; Tech. We've raised over €35M to date, including a €24M Series A in May 2025, backed by Balderton, Headline, Speedinvest, AENU, Magnetic, and Tiny VC. All three founders are on board and 100% committed to build the utility of the future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a (Senior) Associate – Energy Markets &amp; Business Development (Railway Power &amp; PPAs) to own an important part of our energy value chain. You'll report directly to our Energy Operations Manager with close collaboration with the COO and Trading Team. You'll shape the product that makes European industry competitive again - and you'll do it at pace. This role is based in Berlin. trawa is an "office first" company, which means you will work from the office typically five days per week.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>The Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join our Energy Operations team, which owns the energy side of our business - from sourcing and portfolio management to making sure our customers' energy products work in practice. You'll work hand in hand with our Trading Team as well as with Sales, Pricing, Product and Tech. You start without direct reports, but with a clear mandate: build and grow the business areas you own.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As (Senior) Associate – Energy Markets &amp; Business Development, you combine a strong analytical mind with business building:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our railway power business:</strong> A significant share of our customers comes from the railway power (Bahnstrom) segment. You take ownership of this segment from a trading and energy perspective - you understand its specific market setup, improve how we forecast, source, price and supply railway power, and make us the go-to partner for these customers. You dig into how we currently predict our railway customers' energy demand and find ways to make these forecasts more accurate. You also build partnerships with IT service providers from the railway industry and with infrastructure operators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead international railway expansion:</strong> You drive the expansion of our railway power offering into further European countries - you analyse market structures, regulation and commercial potential, and contribute your findings into a concrete go-to-market plan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expand our long-term product offering:</strong> Our customers buy long-term products from us, such as PPAs and Future/Forwards products. You develop our offering so we can provide more and better-fitting products to our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Architect of the long-term trading process:</strong> You centralise and streamline the end-to-end process from pricing and offer creation to actual trade execution across Sales, Pricing, Trading and Operations - making it faster, more robust and scalable, and ultimately enabling a better product for our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge between trading and business:</strong> You work closely with our quant trading and data science team and turn their models and insights into processes and systems that work across teams and markets - so that pricing, risk and market insights reliably translate into better decisions and products for our customers.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>Who we are looking for</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong quantitative skills:</strong> You think analytically, feel at home with numbers and data and can confidently challenge quantitative results - without having to be a quant or developer yourself. Ideally, you have a degree in a quantitative or business field (e.g. economics, engineering, industrial engineering, business administration).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business acumen &amp; venture mindset:</strong> You think commercially, enjoy building new business areas from scratch and prioritise by impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interest in energy markets &amp; trading:</strong> You are fascinated by how energy markets work - from wholesale and forward markets to PPAs, hedging and pricing - and want to dive deep into them. First exposure to these topics is a strong plus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hungry &amp; ambitious:</strong> You want to grow fast, take on responsibility early and set high standards for yourself. You don't wait for instructions - you find answers, push topics forward and enjoy a steep learning curve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High ownership &amp; structured execution:</strong> You drive topics end-to-end, align stakeholders across departments and turn ideas into scalable processes with tangible business impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication:</strong> You speak German at native level and very good English, and you translate confidently between commercial, quantitative and operational perspectives.<br /><br /></p><h2>90 Day Goals</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>After 6 Weeks (Onboarding):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have understood trawa's business, product and energy value chain in detail and got to know all relevant internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand our railway power customers, their contracts, how we currently forecast their energy demand and how we source, price and supply their energy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have mapped our current long-term trading process - from pricing and offer creation to trade execution - and identified the key pain points.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Month 3 (Ramp-Up):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the go-to person for trading and energy questions in the railway power segment, have implemented first improvements and developed a concept for improving our demand forecasts for railway customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have delivered a first assessment of potential expansion markets for railway power, including a recommendation on which country to tackle first, and have identified and approached first potential partners among railway IT service providers and infrastructure operators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have designed a target process for our long-term trading, started its implementation and proposed first additions to our long-term product offering.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What Will Help You Succeed</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work experience in a high-paced environment, e.g. a start-up, scale-up or consulting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in energy markets - especially in energy trading, origination or pricing - or in financial trading markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of the German energy market and/or the railway power (16.7 Hz traction power) market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An affinity for AI-powered tools and automation to make processes faster and smarter.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why us?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> European SMEs spend between €150k and €10M per year on electricity — most are overpaying and locked into outdated procurement. Your product will directly change how thousands of companies buy, manage, and use energy. The impact is measurable, the market is massive, and the timing is now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role:</strong> You build business areas at the intersection of trading, energy and venture development - with direct impact on our revenue, our product offering and our expansion across Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibility &amp; Support:</strong> You own real business areas from day one - backed by our Energy Operations Manager, the COO and an experienced Trading Team who help you ramp up quickly and grow into the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We empower our team members to take ownership of their work and drive results, regardless of background or experience level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Growth:</strong> We provide an annual budget and dedicated time for professional development. You'll have opportunities for mentorship, learning, and career progression.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity and Inclusion:</strong> We're an equal opportunity employer, and our team reflects that. Our organisation brings together over 15 nationalities, contributing a variety of languages, experiences, and perspectives. At trawa, we're family-friendly with parents across all levels, and our diversity is represented throughout the company, including leadership. We're committed to an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Package &amp; Benefits:</strong> We offer a competitive compensation package including salary and stock options, 30 days of vacation, and a range of benefits including subsidies for home internet and lunches, a Sports Club membership, dedicated learning days with an annual learning budget, plus a weekly team lunch and regular team events.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At trawa, we're dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you're excited about this role but your experience doesn't align perfectly, we encourage you to apply - you may be the right fit for this or another opportunity.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/trawa/senior-associate-energy-markets-business-development-railway-power-ppas-berlin-26883","tags":["Energy Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin HQ","created_at":1792237218},{"slug":"remote-account-executive-enterprise-sports-specialist-3930","company_name":"ElevenLabs","title":"Account Executive - Enterprise - Sports Specialist","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual company offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring the entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia and Italy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is looking for our first Sports Specialist to lead the commercial adoption of our AI audio products across the sports industry. This highly strategic, customer-facing role sits at the intersection of product, sales, and sports.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for someone who combines deep expertise in the sports ecosystem with a strong enterprise sales background. You will become the go-to expert for sports use cases, partnering closely with Account Executives to help customers understand how AI can transform content creation, localization, fan engagement, accessibility, and live and on-demand experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a quota-carrying role. Instead, your success will be measured by driving product adoption, enabling the sales organization, influencing product direction through customer feedback, and helping close strategic opportunities where sports expertise is essential.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>In This Role You Will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the subject matter expert for ElevenLabs’ sports use cases, supporting enterprise sales opportunities from discovery through deployment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Account Executives throughout the sales cycle, providing product expertise, customer education, and strategic guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive adoption across professional sports leagues, teams, federations, broadcasters, streaming platforms, rights holders, agencies, sports technology companies, and other organizations across the sports ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customers apply AI audio to use cases such as multilingual content, commentary, fan engagement, content production, personalization, and accessibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with key stakeholders across sports, including commercial, media, digital, content, innovation, and technology leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver compelling product demonstrations and workshops that showcase the capabilities and business value of ElevenLabs’ products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Engineering, Growth, Legal to bring customer insights into product development and go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop scalable enablement materials, best practices, and sales playbooks to help the broader commercial organization successfully position ElevenLabs within sports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay ahead of emerging trends in AI, sports technology, media, broadcasting, and fan engagement to help shape ElevenLabs’ long-term strategy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of enterprise technology sales experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience selling into or working with sports leagues, teams, broadcasters, streaming platforms, rights holders, agencies, or sports technology companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of the sports ecosystem, including content and production workflows, media rights, fan engagement, partnerships, and digital distribution.</p></li><l