 in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0;width:100%;height:0;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/0ac11447-a862-468b-95a0-40198c971382/5a7e80f3-d875-4693-938a-33455a593625" style="top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0" allowfullscreen scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/notion/general-manager-dach-munich-445118","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich, Germany","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"account-executive-germany-berlin-212011","company_name":"Wayflyer","title":"Account Executive, Germany","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Wayflyer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today's small businesses need a capital provider that keeps pace with their growth ambitions. Traditional financing options are slow, cumbersome and often out of reach. That's why we built Wayflyer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our technology allows us to assess businesses in minutes, generate financing offers that reflect their growth potential and send funds in as little as 24 hours. To date, we've deployed over $6bn to thousands of businesses worldwide, backed by Tier 1 banks like J.P. Morgan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be collaborating with ambitious colleagues from around the world. We have offices in Dublin, London, New York, Charlotte, Berlin and Sydney.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The challenge</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are thousands of businesses globally growing fast and hitting the same wall - they need capital, and traditional lenders are too slow, too rigid, or simply not interested. We've already deployed over $6bn to growing businesses like these. The opportunity in front of us is significant, and we need people who can capitalise on it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the full sales cycle from sourcing your own leads to closing deals with some of the most exciting consumer brands in Germany. You'll run in-depth discovery calls using MEDDPICC, work closely with our underwriting team to move fast without cutting corners, and negotiate deals that genuinely work for both sides. You'll have a dedicated BDR alongside you, but you won't wait around for a full pipeline to land in your lap. The best AEs here source relentlessly, close confidently, and treat their customers like business partners, not transactions. Top performers are hitting ~200% of target. That's not a boast. It's a signal of what’s possible.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What this role could turn into</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Account Executives at Wayflyer tend to grow in one of two directions - first on the ground in one of our emerging verticals, or into team leadership as we scale. We're continuing to launch new products and verticals, which means the people who perform here will have real options. We'd rather promote from within than hire from outside, and our track record reflects that.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who thrives here</strong><br />You've worked a full sales cycle before, and you didn't just hit your number; you understood exactly why you hit it and what to do differently when you didn't. You source your own pipeline without being asked, and you don't wait for perfect conditions to start. You're energised by ambiguity, not paralysed by it. You push deals forward when others would wait for a signal. When a sceptical founder pushes back, you lean in. You've been told "no" and come back with a better question. You care about eCommerce and small business growth, not as a line on a cover letter, but as a genuine reason you want this job.<br /><br /><strong>We hire for range</strong><br />Full sales cycle experience across a range of deal values (think: $10K to 100K) in SaaS or FinTech, ideally with time spent as an outbound BDR/SDR. You know what it takes to build a pipeline from scratch, not just work it. A consistent track record of exceeding targets matters more than tenure. Resilience shows up in your history: you've had a bad quarter, figured out why, and bounced back stronger. MEDDPICC familiarity is required, and you'll need to speak German fluently. Startup or scale-up experience helps; the pace here is real, the playbook is still being written, and we need people who see that as an opportunity, not a risk.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location and working policy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍</strong>Berlin, hybrid (3-4 days per week in the office)</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The good stuff</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days off, plus public holidays. Equity - because you should own a piece of what you're building. Generous parental leave for primary and secondary caregivers. 60 days a year to work abroad from wherever you want.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Wayflyer Limited will process your personal data for the purpose of evaluating your suitability for the role. Such processing is based on the need to take steps prior to entering into a potential employment agreement. To learn more about how we handle your personal data, you can contact our privacy team at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- or review our privacy notice at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://wayflyer.com/privacy-notice"><em>https://wayflyer.com/privacy-notice</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/wayflyer/account-executive-germany-berlin-212011","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-product-designer-berlin-70645","company_name":"Taktile","title":"Senior Product Designer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Taktile empowers financial institutions to transform into truly AI-native organizations. We’re growing rapidly with enterprise customers across banks and insurance companies, and we’re looking for a Senior Product Designer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the world's leading software platform for running critical and highly-automated decisions. Our customers use our product to catch fraudsters, prevent money laundering, and expand access to credit for small businesses, among many other use cases. Taktile is making millions of such decisions across the globe every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We do this through a powerful suite of tools that combine ML/AI with heuristics and logic, flexible data integrations, and an overlay of data analytics. We see a high degree of usability as a key differentiator and have been investing in a world-class UI/UX from day one. To help us deliver our vision, we are seeking talented and experienced Senior Product Designers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Product Designer, you will be responsible for translating highly technical and complex problems into clean and understandable solutions. You will be the voice of user experience and design standards in a cross-functional setting, and responsible for the end-to-end design process for your team. You’ll join a diverse design team and work closely with engineers, marketing and sales to create products that make it easy for our users to make smarter and safer decisions at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Please not that this role is not open to full remote and is Berlin or London based only</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently lead all design efforts for a cross functional team within Taktile.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply design thinking to complex technical problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously learn from user research and be the voice of our customers in product development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct competitive analysis of existing products in the marketplace to identify opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect business strategies, available technologies, and design solutions to deliver great experiences that impact our users and our business goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively validate and iterate to ensure our product concepts are aligned with the business needs and stakeholder expectations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with engineers and ensure that designs are implemented effectively in code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to and work with our Design System</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with other designers to create a coherent user experience across Taktile’s product</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in Product Design, ideally with B2B SaaS, fintech, or similarly complex technical domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience leading design for a product area or cross-functional team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong systems thinking and ability to design complex workflows and data-heavy interfaces</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to translate complex technical and business requirements into clear, scalable user experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience driving discovery and shaping problem definitions with Product and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal, But Not Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing agentic interfaces and interest in AI-powered products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical understanding that allows you to engage in discussions with the Engineering Team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in working in a fast-paced start-up/scale-up environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in fintech and financial services</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with colleagues that lift you up, challenge you, celebrate you and help you grow. We come from many different backgrounds, but what we have in common is the desire to operate at the very top of our fields. If you are similarly capable, caring, and driven, you'll find yourself at home here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience a truly flat hierarchy and communicate directly with founding team members. Having an opinion and voicing your ideas is not only welcome but encouraged, especially when they challenge the status quo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn from experienced mentors and achieve tremendous personal and professional growth. Get to know and leverage our network of leading tech investors and advisors around the globe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive a top-of-market equity and cash compensation package.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get access to a self-development budget you can use to e.g. attend conferences, buy books or take classes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive a new Apple MacBook Pro, as well as meaningful home office set-up.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Stance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're eager to meet talented and driven candidates regardless of whether they tick all the boxes. We're looking for someone who will add to our culture, not just fit within it. We strongly encourage individuals from groups traditionally underestimated and underrepresented in tech to apply</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We seek to actively recognize and combat racism, sexism, ableism and ageism. We embrace and support all gender identities and expressions, and celebrate love in its many forms. We won't inquire about how you identify or if you've experienced discrimination, but if you want to tell your story, we are all ears</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong><br />Taktile enables financial institutions to transform into AI-native organizations that are increasingly powered by autonomous agents. With our modular Agentic Decision Platform, customers combine AI agents, rules, relevant context, and human oversight to safely automate and optimize their decisions—approving more customers, reimbursing claims instantly, stopping fraud before it spreads, and financing every business worth funding. Founded in 2020, Taktile powers millions of decisions daily for institutions including Mercury, Monzo, Faire, and Pleo. With offices in New York, Berlin, London, São Paulo, and Iași, the company has raised $184M from Growth Equity at Goldman Sachs Alternatives, Index Ventures, Tiger Global, Balderton Capital, and Y Combinator. Learn more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://taktile.com">taktile.com</a></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>About Your Employment.</strong> Taktile operates through regional entities worldwide. Depending on the location of this role, your employment or engagement will be with Taktile LLC (US), Taktile GmbH (Germany), Taktile Ltd (UK), or Taktile SRL (Romania). The applicable entity will be confirmed during the offer process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Your Privacy</strong>. Taktile (“we” or “us”) is the controller of the personal data you provide during this</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>application process. We collect and process your name, contact details, resume/CV, work history, education, and any other information you submit or that we obtain from publicly available sources or references.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>How we use your data</strong>: We process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy, communicate with you about the recruitment process, comply with legal obligations (such as right-to-work verification), and, with your consent, to consider you for future opportunities.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Legal basis (EU/UK applicants):</strong> We rely on (i) pre-contractual steps at your request (GDPR/UK GDPR Art.6(1)(b)), (ii) legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)), and (iii) our legitimate interest in evaluating candidates (Art.6(1)(f)).</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Retention:</strong> If your application is unsuccessful, we retain your data for 12 months after the recruitment process concludes, unless you consent to longer retention. Successful candidates’ data becomes part of their employment records.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Your rights: </strong>Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of your personal data, to data portability, and to withdraw consent.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Automated decision-making:</strong> We use automated tools to assist in screening applications. No hiring decision is made solely by automated means without human review.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>International transfers:</strong> Your data may be transferred to and processed in the United States, Germany, the United Kingdom, or Romania. Where required, transfers are protected by Standard Contractual Clauses or other approved mechanisms.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>By submitting your application, you acknowledge that you have read and understood Taktile’s Applicant Privacy Policy. To exercise your rights or ask questions, contact -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/taktile/senior-product-designer-berlin-70645","tags":["Product & Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-integration-specialist-munich-14443","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"(Senior) Integration Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP creates value the moment it is connected to our customers' ERP systems. As an Integration Specialist, you onboard our customers on our integrations and ensure connectivity between BLP and their ERP system. You assess and challenge change requests and specify them for our Integration Engineers. Your work directly drives customer go-lives and revenue. Integration Engineers build, Project Managers lead the project, you make the integration work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard customers on our ERP integrations: analyze their IT landscape, engage the right stakeholders, advise on best practices, install and configure our ERP integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess and challenge change requests and turn them into a clear, implementable specification for our Integration Engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customers during self-onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Integration Engineers to continuously improve our integrations and streamline the onboarding experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag major development needs and blockers early, and make clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Project Managers on technical feasibility, effort and sequencing, through first go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in technical consulting, enterprise integration or technical product work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid grasp of ERP landscapes, interfaces and master data, and how data actually moves between them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of at least one ERP system (e.g., Microsoft Dynamics, Oracle, Infor, Abas), both from a functional and integration perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with common integration formats (CSV, XML, JSON) and transports (REST/SOAP APIs, SFTP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of purchase-to-pay (P2P) and order-to-cash (O2C) processes, including the related finance and accounting workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing specifications that engineers can build from without a translation layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable reading production code, with the help of AI tools, to understand integration behavior and answer customer questions.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real impact: successfully connecting a customer's ERP system decides whether a customer goes live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast-growing, global AI company providing the ideal environment to learn and grow fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear handoffs: Integration Engineers build and own the product code, Project Managers own the plan, and you own the implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one month of onboarding at our Zurich headquarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership through our stock option program.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-integration-specialist-munich-14443","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-munich-498986","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Project Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time position based in Munich or Cologne. Following a comprehensive onboarding period at our HQ in central Zurich (minimum one month), you will work from your home location, with regular visits to customers across the DACH region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team collaboration matters a lot to us. You will regularly spend time with the team in person, in Zurich and at our hubs, for team days, all-hands and offsites. These visits are financially supported by blp.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get customers live. Hands on, end to end, and fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>As a Senior Project Manager</strong>, you make large, global blp transformations happen. These programs touch finance, procurement and supply chain at once, run across multiple ERP systems and legal entities, and roll out country by country. Your job is to orchestrate all of it and get the customer live: the first go-live above all, because that is where credibility is won or lost, and then wave after wave with the same discipline. You run the steering committee, you lead a blp team on each engagement, and you do that across several engagements at once.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At both levels, scope is the single biggest lever on whether a project goes live on time. Protecting it is a daily job, not a contract clause. You escalate early and precisely rather than absorbing problems until they become critical.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will not be alone with the technical side. Integrations Engineers handle the connection into the ERP, Technical Project Managers handle the harder solution design, and our Consultants take over the automation work after go-live. On our largest strategic accounts a Client Partner carries the relationship and the commercial number, so your attention goes to delivery quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have done this many times, so you are not inventing the approach each time. A proven onboarding method and a strong toolkit are what let you carry your own customers from early on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Career Path in Project Management</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the path most of our delivery leadership came through, and we hire at every step of it. We place you according to your experience and the size of the programs you have delivered, and we are explicit about what the next step requires.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Manager:</strong> You get customers live end to end, several in parallel: guided onboarding for commercial customers, leading enterprise projects yourself, or a workstream on our largest programs. <em>Typically you bring 2+ years in consulting, implementation or project management.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Senior Project Manager:</strong> You make large, global transformations happen: multiple ERPs, entities and countries, the steering committee, and a blp team on each engagement. <em>Typically you bring 5+ years delivering complex, multi-country programs.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Next steps:</strong> Lead a delivery team, or move into Consulting and from there towards our Client Partner role on strategic accounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moves into Consulting or Customer Success Engineering are open at every level, and many of our people make them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run implementations end to end: kick-off, scope, planning, configuration, testing and go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage several customers in parallel at different stages, and keep every one of them on date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with customers on their processes, and flag early where a process assumption will not hold.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the specialists on your projects: Integrations Engineers, Technical Project Managers and AI Automation Specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own scope actively. Recognize a change request for what it is and handle it deliberately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the project inside its budget, and raise it early when the effort is drifting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand over cleanly at go-live to our Consultants and support organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In addition, as a Senior Project Manager</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery outcome of global programs from kick-off to the last go-live: plan, scope, dependencies and date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the first go-live relentlessly, then run wave planning across ERPs, entities and countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the steering committee and own the decisions that come out of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and execute the recovery plan when a program is off track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the blp team on each engagement and coach the Project Managers working on your programs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Really Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The following key attributes ensure success in this role:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope Discipline – You notice when a project is quietly growing, and you raise it rather than absorbing it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership &amp; Autonomy – You take initiative, move things forward, and deliver end to end without being chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalation Judgment – You escalate early, to the right person, with a proposal rather than a problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Client Confidence – You are comfortable running a meeting with a customer's finance or IT lead in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Four-Language Fluency – Technology, process, data and people. You speak each well enough to spot where a roadblock really sits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured Under Pressure – When a project goes sideways you get sharper and more organized, not louder.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience delivering complex projects: management consulting, enterprise software implementation, or large-scale transformation delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record running multi-country or multi-entity programs with senior client stakeholders, and steering a committee that includes client executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a delivery team rather than only a plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and communication skills. You can translate a business need into something a technical team can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German and English, spoken and written.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points for ERP implementation experience, finance or supply chain processes, or AI-driven SaaS.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership environment – you shape your projects, outcomes, and career path.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact at scale – your work powers automation across global enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional exposure – work with engineers, data scientists, and business leaders daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real growth – fast-paced environment, steep learning curve, and structured career progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership – be part of a majority employee-owned company with a best-in-class stock option program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amazing team – become part of a driven and collaborative group of innovators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technology exposure – be at the forefront of AI and enjoy continuous learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visits &amp; offsites – paid visits and stays at our HQ in Zurich, including collaborative team offsites.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to build the future of ERP automation?</strong> Join us and own your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blp.digital/company/careers">https://blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-project-manager-munich-498986","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"head-of-consulting-munich-293031","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Head of Consulting","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go-live is where our customers start to see the value of BLP. As Head of Consulting you build and lead the organization that owns everything after go-live: how far each customer's automation goes, the support they rely on every day, the escalations, and whether they stay with BLP and grow. Your organization will more than double over the next year, including new teams in Germany.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead three groups:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Consulting:</strong> Consultants and Associate Consultants who push each customer's automation further after go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Success Engineering:</strong> the CSEs who keep money-critical processes running.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client Partners:</strong> they own our largest strategic accounts within their own practice.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to the VP Customer Success and are part of the Customer Success leadership team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own net revenue retention and expansion across our installed base, and lead the Client Partners who hold the executive relationships on our strategic accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the automation curve after go-live, through consulting and automation sprints, so every customer reaches the productivity we committed to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run Customer Success Engineering on clear service levels: priority handling for strategic accounts, critical incidents solved for every customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the final escalation point. Call a recovery when an account is off track, and hold the organization to the plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the new Consulting and Customer Success Engineering teams in Germany: hire the leads, set the hiring bar and develop your team leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the economics and operating model of the run phase across our Strategic, Enterprise and Commercial segments: cost to serve, service levels, account health and paid services.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in strategy or operations consulting, customer success, professional services or operations leadership, ideally both top-tier consulting and enterprise software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership of organizations of 15+ direct reports, including managing managers, ideally scaled in a fast-growing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of purchase-to-pay and order-to-cash and the ERP landscape behind them, for example from finance transformation, shared services or ERP transformations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning commercial outcomes with strategic accounts on executive level such as retention, expansion or cost to serve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence: you hold the room with a CFO, especially when the conversation is difficult.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in AI-driven enterprise SaaS or in scaling teams across countries is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build an organization: you shape how BLP runs the run phase while it more than doubles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive ownership of our largest and most demanding customer relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration with Customer Success leadership, Product, Engineering and Sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee participation plan</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> We create measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency:</strong> We build trust through openness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We take responsibility for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence:</strong> We relentlessly strive for greatness.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/head-of-consulting-munich-293031","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792226418},{"slug":"people-and-business-operations-specialist-hamburg-148664","company_name":"Mindpeak","title":"People and Business Operations Specialist","description":"<h1><strong>Über Mindpeak</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mindpeak ist ein KI-Unternehmen aus Hamburg mit einer klaren Mission: Krebsdiagnosen genauer, effizienter und personalisierter zu machen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wir entwickeln Deep-Learning-Lösungen für die computergestützte Pathologie, die KI direkt in die klinische Praxis bringen. Unsere Technologie wird bereits in mehr als 25 Ländern in der Routinediagnostik eingesetzt und unterstützt führende Pharma- und Biotech-Unternehmen bei der Entwicklung neuer Krebstherapien.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rund 50 Menschen aus Technologie, Medizin und Wissenschaft arbeiten bei uns gemeinsam an diesem Ziel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Über die Rolle</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bei Mindpeak arbeiten wir daran, mit KI die Krebsdiagnostik zu verbessern. Damit sie sich auf ihre Arbeit konzentrieren können, braucht es im Hintergrund jemanden, der dafür sorgt, dass unsere People Operations funktionieren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genau hier kommst du ins Spiel.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als People &amp; Business Operations Specialist bist du das operative Rückgrat unserer People- und Business Operations. Du sorgst dafür, dass neue Kolleg:innen einen guten Start haben, Mitarbeiterdaten stimmen, die Payroll vorbereitet ist, Rechnungen und administrative Finanzprozesse zuverlässig bearbeitet werden, Dokumente rechtzeitig vorliegen, Trainings im Blick bleiben und unsere Mitarbeitenden bei administrativen und organisatorischen Fragen schnell Unterstützung bekommen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Administration &amp; Personio:</strong> Du hältst Mitarbeiterdaten, Abwesenheiten, Arbeitszeitmodelle und Dokumente aktuell und sorgst für eine verlässliche Datenbasis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On- &amp; Offboarding:</strong> Du koordinierst die administrativen Schritte rund um Ein- und Austritte, von Google-Accounts und Hardware bis zu Zugängen und Rückgaben, und sorgst für einen reibungslosen Ablauf.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Payroll &amp; Finance Administration:</strong> Du bereitest die monatliche Payroll vor, bearbeitest Rückerstattungen für Mitarbeitende und unterstützt unsere Finanzadministration, insbesondere bei der vorbereitenden Buchhaltung, Rechnungsbearbeitung und Verwaltung von Firmenkreditkarten.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Operations &amp; Prozesskoordination</strong>: Du verwaltest administrative Vertragsfristen, hältst Firmenversicherungen aktuell, koordinierst externe Dienstleister und sorgst dafür, dass wiederkehrende administrative Prozesse strukturiert und zuverlässig ablaufen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Dokumente:</strong> Du kümmerst dich um Bescheinigungen, Zeugnisse und weitere administrative Unterlagen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vertragsadministration:</strong> Du bereitest Arbeitsverträge, Vertragsänderungen und Nachträge auf Basis unserer Vorlagen vor und steuerst den Unterschriftenprozess.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sozialversicherung &amp; Benefits:</strong> Du betreust administrative Themen rund um Sozialversicherung, betriebliche Altersvorsorge und Benefits und koordinierst dich mit unseren externen Partnern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance, Trainings &amp; Arbeitssicherheit:</strong> Du administrierst unser Learning Management System, steuerst Pflichttrainings sowie jährliche Unterweisungen zum Arbeits- und Brandschutz  und dokumentierst Trainingsnachweise so, dass sie in Audits (z. B. ISO) belastbar sind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR-Reporting:</strong> Du erstellst Auswertungen zu Themen wie Headcount, Abwesenheiten oder Trainings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People-Prozesse:</strong> Du unterstützt organisatorisch bei Feedback-Zyklen und anderen wiederkehrenden People-Prozessen und kümmerst dich um Teamrituale wie Geburtstage, Jubiläen und Abschiede.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mitarbeitenden-Support:</strong> Du bist eine verlässliche Anlaufstelle für administrative HR-Fragen und sorgst dafür, dass Anliegen nicht liegen bleiben.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Was wir suchen</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du passt gut zu uns, wenn du:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">eine <strong>abgeschlossene kaufmännische Ausbildung oder eine vergleichbare Qualifikation</strong> mitbringst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">bereits <strong>praktische Erfahrung in Business oder HR-Administration, People Operations oder Personalwesen</strong> gesammelt hast,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">strukturiert, sorgfältig und eigenständig arbeitest und Verantwortung für deine Themen übernimmst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">vertraulich und sorgfältig mit sensiblen Personaldaten umgehst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">auch bei vielen parallelen Aufgaben den Überblick behältst und Dinge zuverlässig zu Ende bringst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">gerne organisierst und Freude daran hast, wenn Prozesse reibungslos funktionieren,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">serviceorientiert bist und gerne dafür sorgst, dass andere gut arbeiten können,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">sicher mit digitalen Tools arbeitest – Erfahrung mit <strong>Personio</strong> ist ein Plus,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">idealerweise schon in einem <strong>regulierten Umfeld</strong> gearbeitet hast, z. B. in MedTech oder einem ISO-zertifizierten Unternehmen (kein Muss),</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">sehr gutes Deutsch und sehr gutes Englisch mitbringst.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Warum diese Rolle wichtig ist</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gute People und Business Operations fallen manchmal erst auf, wenn sie <strong>nicht</strong> funktionieren. Für uns sind sie deshalb kein Nebenthema, sondern eine wichtige Grundlage für ein gut funktionierendes Unternehmen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In dieser Rolle hast du direkten Einfluss auf den Arbeitsalltag unseres gesamten Teams. Du schaffst Struktur, Verlässlichkeit und einen guten Service für unsere Mitarbeitenden – und gibst anderen damit den Rücken frei, sich auf ihre eigentliche Arbeit zu konzentrieren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Was wir bieten</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eine <strong>Rolle mit echter Wirkung </strong>in einem Unternehmen, das mit KI die Krebsdiagnostik verbessert</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein Remote-Tag pro Woche</strong> – an den übrigen vier Tagen arbeitest du mit dem Team in unserem Büro in Hamburg, mit kurzen Wegen zu allen Kolleginnen und Kollegen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein wunderschönes Büro mit Blick auf den Hamburger Hafen</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ein tolles, internationales Team</strong> mit kurzen Entscheidungswegen, einer offenen Atmosphäre und gegenseitiger Unterstützung und Wertschätzung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regelmäßige Team-Events</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guter Kaffee, Müsli und Getränke</strong> – für einen guten Start in den Tag und die kleine Pause zwischendurch</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mindpeak/people-and-business-operations-specialist-hamburg-148664","tags":["General & Administration"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792226417},{"slug":"sales-intern-dach-market-munich-184333","company_name":"Emidat GmbH","title":"Sales Intern (DACH Market)","description":"<h1>👷🏻‍♀️ What we do 👷🏻‍♀️</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Emidat, we are building the first climate-native product management system for building material manufacturers. We aim to decarbonise building materials, making up 11% of global GHG emissions. We collect data from physical production processes, generate a digital product passport with verified environmental data and make it usable along the value chain. In short: One solution to assess, design, buy, sell and manage products - with environmental impact at the core.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With this, we are building the digital infrastructure to make it faster, easier, and more sustainable to build the world around us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/emidat/Join-Emidat-Enable-a-built-environment-that-operates-within-planetary-boundaries-dbe707b78a8144cb92583ffab4e46c8c"><strong><u>Find out more about us, the team and our values here.</u></strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you will work on</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate Emidat’s growth by acquiring new leads, being Emidat’s first face to the customer and building our predictable, repeatable revenue engine. Work closely with the Sales Development Rep and Account Executive on the go-to-market plan for the country. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>Sales Intern</strong>, you will be driving our revenue pipeline focussing on the DACH market. In this role, you are the first face and voice to our customer, so this role is perfect if you love being around people and have a talent for convincing, understanding and solving their problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Emidat, we see top-of-funnel as equally important if not more so than closing deals. Without leads, there is no revenue. We are searching for a hungry sales person, who is not scared of approaching people actively and being the face of Emidat. Your customers are manufacturers, so you shouldn’t be shy and bring a curiosity for material manufacturing and construction <em>(note: we think visiting steel, cement and glass plants is the coolest thing in the world next to customers holding their product into the Teams call to show us how it’s done)</em>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your challenge:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining our sales development team involves:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Pipeline Development:</strong> Build and nurture our customer pipeline, from initial prospecting to booking a demo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-to-Market Strategy:</strong> Develop and fine-tune our go-to-market strategy, ensuring alignment with our company objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Revenue Engine:</strong> Build and improve our repeatable and predictable revenue engine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Building</strong>: Play a key role in building and growing the sales team leading us to 3mn ARR.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your first 3 months at Emidat (sample)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any Emidavinci starts with a detailed 3-month OKR sheet, which helps to build clarity and accountability from day 1. This is only a high-level overview how this can look like as a Sales Development Executive, but you will find many of the points on your 3-month list in your first week again.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">1. Deeply understand our customer and market</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Mastery:</strong> Call customers, attend conferences and deeply understand our target customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Discovery Calls:</strong> Conduct your first discovery calls and schedule at least 20 demos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demo Shadowing:</strong> Shadow at least 10 demos to learn how we close deals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">2. Plan and conduct your own outbound campaigns</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Campaign Ownership:</strong> Design your own outbound campaign (incl. list, workflows and sequences). Plan and own 3 campaigns in total</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>RevOps: </strong>Analyze and improve email open/reply rates (target: 25%+ open rate, 5%+ reply rate)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outbound prospecting:</strong> Execute on the campaigns (e.g. follow-up with calls, send emails/LinkedIn requests)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">3. Get to know and improve our revenue engine design</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CRM / RevOps Mastery:</strong> Become comfortable with our CRM and sales material</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales Playbook &amp; Objection Handling:</strong> Read through our sales playbook, as well as our objection- and competitor handling, start using it and suggest improvements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market understanding:</strong> Understand ICP, persona and JTBD framework; start using it to include your insights</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you will bring to this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language</strong>: Fluent in German (C2/Native). Proficiency (B2+) in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales Experience:</strong> Demonstrable experience in a business development, growth or sales role. with quantifiable success selling to business customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market Experience:</strong> Experience working with clients / customers in the DACH market in a B2B or B2C capacity. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong Communication Skills:</strong> Effective communication skills, both verbal and written, to communicate with customers and collaborate with team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Recently completed or close to completion of a Bachelors Degree in a relevant field (i.e business administration, marketing, sustainability, mechanical / chemical engineering). </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have’s</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language:</strong> Proficiency in another Language relevant to our markets (French, Spanish, Portuguese, Turkish, Italian, Arabic, Hindi).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup:</strong> Experience in a start up or scale up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industry: </strong>Experience in the construction, material manufacturing or sustainability industries. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education</strong>: Completing or completed a Master Degree in a relevant field. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>How we support you</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your team lead will be</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/elise-lecocq-gj/">Elise Lecocq</a> (Sales Development)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/janos-gr%C3%BCndling/">Janos Grundling</a> (Team Lead, Growth)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/joey-quest/">Joey Quest</a> (Sales Development)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/camillo-alemdoust/">Camillo Alemdoust</a> (Account Executive)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/katrina-g-b3990b12a/">Katrina Griese</a> (Sales Development)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/giovanni-michele-genzone/">Giovanni Genzone</a> (Sales Development)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet the rest of the team </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Join-Emidat-Enable-a-built-environment-that-operates-within-planetary-boundaries-dbe707b78a8144cb92583ffab4e46c8c?pvs=21"><strong>HERE.</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>See our full benefits </strong><a 