ters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Let's get the tricky part out of the way: this role doesn't fit neatly into a box. It's part client facing accounting advisory, part product specialist, part solutions architect, and part trusted advisor. If you're looking for a role that stays static, this isn't it.<br />Your mission is to help some of the world's leading accounting firms get the absolute most out of Legora. You'll partner with clients to understand how they work today, help them rethink how audit work gets done with AI, and ensure they realise lasting value from the platform.<br />You'll:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted advisor to clients, building strong relationships, solving complex challenges, and identifying opportunities to deepen and scale their use of Legora.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the GTM and Customer Success teams through the sales process from early pilots and onboarding through to firm-wide adoption across Big Four and mid-tier practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design practical solutions to complex accounting workflows, helping clients embed Legora into their day-to-day engagements in ways that deliver measurable impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver engaging product demonstrations, workshops and training that help accounting professionals understand the full potential of the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide clients through one of the biggest shifts in the profession, helping them evaluate the practical application and business value of generative AI across accounting work, including how it sits alongside methodology and documentation requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the voice of the customer within Legora, bringing frontline insights into product development, roadmap priorities and strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build scalable playbooks, best practices and knowledge resources that help us continually improve how we deliver for customers as we grow globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Product, Engineering and Customer Success to ensure customer feedback translates into meaningful product improvements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What you'll bring</strong><br /><br />You're an accountant who enjoys improving the way work gets done. You understand the realities of practice; the deadlines, the review cycles, the file, and are excited by the opportunity to combine that expertise with technology to solve meaningful customer problems.<br /><br />We're looking for someone who has:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A recognised accountancy qualification (ACA, ACCA, CA or equivalent) with experience gained at a leading firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong understanding of accounting workflows and the challenges facing modern engagement teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about technology and AI, with an enthusiasm for learning how products are built and implemented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to communicate complex ideas clearly and confidently with partners, product managers and engineers alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem-solving skills and the judgement to navigate ambiguity with confidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to build credibility quickly and develop trusted relationships with senior practitioners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, self-directed approach, balancing multiple customer engagements while maintaining a high bar for quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias for action; you enjoy experimenting, learning quickly and continuously improving how work gets done.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/legora/legal-engineer-accounting-london-460220","tags":["Legal Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792258816},{"slug":"engagement-manager-mid-market-corporates-london-8483","company_name":"Legora","title":"Engagement Manager - Mid-Market Corporates","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The way legal work gets done is changing, and Engagement is at the centre of that transformation. We're looking for an Engagement Manager to own adoption across a portfolio of mid-market corporate clients and help their in-house legal teams fundamentally change the way they work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for someone who has led change inside complex organisations and knows that real transformation is designed and managed. You will own the adoption and long-term success of 15 – 20 corporate accounts: building the relationships, defining the outcomes and serving as the trusted adviser who turns Legora into an embedded part of how those teams operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mid-market means breadth as well as depth. You will be running adoption programmes across 15 – 20 accounts at once, each with its own stakeholders, timelines and success measures, which makes this a role where strong project management is not a nice-to-have but the thing that determines whether you succeed. You will lean on repeatable playbooks where they work and go bespoke where an account earns it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of the role is designing each client's adoption playbook and delivering the change programmes that transform how they work. For every account you will build a tailored roadmap, sequence initiatives from initial rollout through function-wide scaled adoption, define measurable outcomes and ROI and evolve the programme as new AI capabilities and use cases emerge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be critical as we continue to build a best-in-class adoption programme at Legora, helping clients realise measurable ROI, expand successful use cases and transform the way their teams work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll lead the post-sale customer experience, owning onboarding, adoption and long-term value realisation for a portfolio of 15 – 20 mid-market corporates. Specifically, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design each client's adoption playbook: the tailored change-management approach, stakeholder map and target outcomes for how that legal function adopts Legora and transforms the way it works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute against that playbook, sequencing initiatives from initial rollout to function- and enterprise-wide scaled adoption and adapting as the client's needs and Legora's capabilities evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run those programmes in parallel across the full portfolio, holding the plan, the milestones and the risks for every account and knowing at any moment which ones need your attention this week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a strategic adviser who deeply understands in-house legal priorities — cost, cycle time, risk and doing more without adding headcount — surfaces high-impact opportunities and guides teams towards maximum value from Legora.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive sustained value through a structured operating cadence: success plans, enablement, stakeholder check-ins, training and value reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orchestrate engagement from cross-functional teams to accelerate client success (GTM, Product, Legal Engineering, Engineering, Marketing, Support), maintaining end-to-end account context and coordination.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with GTM on key commercial moments to ensure seamless transitions, continuity and exceptional customer experience, and to identify and realise expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate customer feedback into action by collaborating closely with Product, Engineering and Marketing to inform roadmap, positioning and enablement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build reusable playbooks, templates and enablement material from what works, so the whole Engagement team gets better as you go rather than every account starting from scratch.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You car