1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deepgram is the leading platform underpinning the emerging trillion-dollar Voice AI economy, providing real-time APIs for speech-to-text (STT), text-to-speech (TTS), and building production-grade voice agents at scale. More than 200,000 developers and 1,300+ organizations build voice offerings that are ‘Powered by Deepgram’, including Twilio, Cloudflare, Sierra, Decagon, Vapi, Daily, Cresta, Granola, and Jack in the Box. Deepgram’s voice-native foundation models are accessed through cloud APIs or as self-hosted and on-premises software, with unmatched accuracy, low latency, and cost efficiency. Backed by a recent Series C led by leading global investors and strategic partners, Deepgram has processed over 50,000 years of audio and transcribed more than 1 trillion words. There is no organization in the world that understands voice better than Deepgram.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Company Operating Rhythm</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Deepgram, we expect an AI-first mindset—AI use and comfort aren’t optional, they’re core to how we operate, innovate, and measure performance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every team member who works at Deepgram is expected to actively use and experiment with advanced AI tools, and even build your own into your everyday work. We measure how effectively AI is applied to deliver results, and consistent, creative use of the latest AI capabilities is key to success here. Candidates should be comfortable adopting new models and modes quickly, integrating AI into their workflows, and continuously pushing the boundaries of what these technologies can do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additionally, we move at the pace of AI. Change is rapid, and you can expect your day-to-day work to evolve just as quickly. This may not be the right role if you’re not excited to experiment, adapt, think on your feet, and learn constantly, or if you’re seeking something highly prescriptive with a traditional 9-to-5.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deepgram is expanding into EMEA, and we're seeking a GM, Sales to own the region — building and leading the Enterprise and commercial segments of our Account Executive team, establishing Deepgram's European home in London, and driving growth across the region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is both strategic and hands-on. You'll work with sales leadership to continue optimizing the systems, playbooks, and culture that scale ARR growth, while developing a high-performing team that converts opportunities into long-lasting customers. A core part of your mission is building Deepgram's next generation of sales talent through world-class training, coaching, and structured career development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be more than a revenue leader. As our senior-most voice in EMEA, you'll bring what you learn in the field back into the company and shape what we build — regional product-market fit, roadmap priorities, and the technical requirements European enterprises hold us to.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll partner closely with Marketing, Sales Leadership, RevOps, Customer Success, and Product to align pipeline strategy and leverage modern AI tools to boost productivity, personalization, and team efficiency. Equal parts operator, coach, and builder, you'll combine data-driven rigor with creativity to shape how Deepgram grows its customer base and its sales talent.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale the Region:</strong> Own the EMEA number. Build and execute a strategic roadmap to drive hyper-growth in ARR, from initial land to enterprise-wide expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Open London:</strong> Stand up Deepgram's London office as our EMEA hub — and treat it as a commercial asset, not just real estate. It will host customer and developer events, executive briefings, partner sessions, and the team you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>"Challenge &amp; Lead":</strong> Recruit and mentor a high-performance team of Account Executives. Manage Customer Success, Marketing, and Forward Deployed Engineers in a dotted-line structure. You will instill a culture of "Challenger" selling — teaching AEs how to disrupt legacy incumbents and lead with technical ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the Product:</strong> Act as the voice of EMEA inside Deepgram. Translate field signal — deal losses, evaluation criteria, data residency and compliance requirements, language and accent coverage — into specific, prioritized input that changes what we build and when.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the Ecosystem:</strong> Identify and sign strategic regional partners, GSIs, and local resellers to act as a force multiplier for Deepgram's direct sales efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Implement rigorous forecasting, pipeline hygiene, and territory management across multiple countries, languages, and buying cultures. You will bridge the gap between London and our US HQ.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>C-Suite Influence:</strong> Act as the primary executive sponsor for major regional accounts, navigating complex procurement cycles and technical AI evaluations.</p></li></ul><h2>You'll Love This Role If You</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrive on building and scaling high-performing teams that consistently beat targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to build something from the ground up — including the office, the team, and the regional playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Value working with tenured, high-caliber leaders who prioritize clarity, accountability, collaboration, and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy blending data-driven sales operations with creative, human-centered leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are energized by developing AEs and building a culture of growth and continuous learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Believe in the power of AI to transform productivity, and are eager to harness cutting-edge tools to optimize performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are passionate about Deepgram's mission to redefine what's possible with speech technology.</p></li></ul><h2>It's Important to Us That You Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 12+ years in B2B SaaS sales, with 5+ years in a senior leadership role (Director/VP) covering EMEA — including the UK and at least one of DACH, the Nordics, France, or Southern Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The "Deepgram DNA":</strong> A deep fascination with AI, LLMs, and API-first products. You should be comfortable discussing technical architecture as easily as you discuss revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Influence:</strong> You've done more than sell — you've changed what your company built. You can point to specific roadmap decisions, features, or product bets that happened because of how you brought the market back to Product and Engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven Growth:</strong> A track record of scaling a regional business from early traction to high-scale maturity ($10M+ ARR growth experience preferred).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership Prowess:</strong> Demonstrable experience building channel programs that significantly contribute to the total revenue mix.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High ASP Focus:</strong> Expertise in value-based selling to increase Average Selling Price and win rates in a competitive technical landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Rigor:</strong> Deep familiarity with modern sales stacks (Salesforce, Gong, Clari, etc.) and a commitment to data-driven decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Bachelor's degree required; MBA or technical degree is a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>It Would Be Great If You Had</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience opening a new office or first in-region presence for a US-headquartered company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading AE organizations at a high-growth, Series B+ startup or scaling tech company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background selling developer tools, infrastructure, or AI/ML technologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in navigating EU data protection and AI regulation as a commercial topic, not just a legal one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expertise in building talent development programs or performance coaching frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in dynamic, fast-moving environments with evolving goals and systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Notice</strong>: We're aware of individuals impersonating Deepgram recruiters. All legitimate Deepgram recruiting communication comes from an @</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://deepgram.com"><em>deepgram.com</em></a><em> email address. If you've received a message claiming to be Deepgram, please forward it to -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/deepgram/gm-sales-emea-london-498633","tags":["Sales - Leadership"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1792258816},{"slug":"account-executive-api-mid-market-enterprise-london-478801","company_name":"Recraft","title":"Account Executive, API — Mid-Market & Enterprise","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Recraft is a graphic design research lab building state-of-the-art image generation models and tools for designers, illustrators, marketers, and developers.<br /><br />Founded in 2022 and based in London, we build for commercial design standards: full creative control, style consistency, and native vector outputs, an API for teams who want to integrate that capability directly into their workflows, plus mobile app for those who prefer not to be distracted from the process without a computer.<br /><br />Over 3 million creators across 190+ countries use Recraft. Our mission is to help everyone who works with visuals get the job done, without lowering the bar on design.<br /><br />If you want to help set that standard, we'd like to hear from you.</p><h2><strong>Job Description</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Large enterprise companies need huge volumes of visual content — product photography, campaign creative, brand assets — produced fast enough to match their business and consistent enough to stay on-brand everywhere. Recraft <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.recraft.ai/blog/introducing-recraft-v4-design-taste-meets-image-generation">V4</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.recraft.ai/blog/recraft-v4-1-more-beautiful-by-nature">V4.1</a> go beyond prompt accuracy to deliver that: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.recraft.ai/blog/best-image-vectorizers">production-ready vector</a> and photorealistic output, with style consistency that holds without custom training. Retail and advertising companies are where we see the clearest opportunity to bring that into a business's own pipeline via our API — it's a classic enterprise B2B motion, and a part of our business we're actively building out. We're hiring an Account Executive to build that pipeline from scratch and close it end to end. This is one of our most urgent hires right now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full sales cycle end-to-end — manage inbound and outbound opportunities from first outreach and qualification through discovery, technical evaluation, negotiation, and closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own enterprise pipeline in retail and advertising — identify and research companies that would integrate Recraft's API for their own internal use, across the UK, EU, US, and Australia, and map out the people who have budget and the people who have veto power.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go deep on research before you pitch — understand a prospect's existing creative or image production pipeline well enough to know exactly where Recraft's API fits, how their teams evaluate new solutions, and how the purchasing decision actually gets made.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn that research into a tailored pitch — customize demos, use cases, and commercial proposals so each prospect sees a specific case for Recraft, not a generic deck.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Navigate and close complex enterprise deals — build relationships with champions and decision-makers, handle objections and commercial negotiation, and drive deals through to signed contracts.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You'll Work With</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join a lean Sales team of three, including this role. You'll work closely with our CEO on enterprise strategy, and collaborate regularly with our technical, marketing, product, and creative teams to get deals across the line — from technical evaluation to a proposal that actually reflects what Recraft can do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of B2B sales experience selling technical products, APIs, developer tools, or complex B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of running the full deal cycle yourself — research, outreach, discovery, negotiation, and close — rather than closing warm leads someone else generated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling into enterprise accounts in the UK, EU, US, or Australia.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong discovery skills — you're good at getting people to talk honestly about what isn't working for them, and you can turn that into a concrete opportunity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building a genuinely customized proposal and demo for each prospect, rather than running the same deck for everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable doing your own outreach and research into cold accounts, and building a funnel from nothing — this isn't a role where leads arrive pre-qualified.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on, individual-contributor role — you want to be running your own pipeline and closing your own deals, not managing a team of reps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing relationships or contacts within retail or advertising enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling design or creative tools, or familiarity with an image or creative production pipeline in B2B advertising.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling AI products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to build Recraft's enterprise retail and advertising vertical from the ground up — the accounts you land now become the reference customers and case studies for everything that follows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct ownership of your own pipeline and deals, with real autonomy in how you run them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hybrid setup based in London, with the team around you day to day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're too unwell to work, you're covered — up to 10 working days of sick pay at your normal base salary, in any rolling 12-month period.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A team that means it when it says it wants to build the best product in the category — people who give each other direct, useful feedback, share context openly, and step in to help without being asked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're able to sponsor visas for this role where needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our Process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">HR screen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales interview with the hiring team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Live demo / case study exercise </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/recraft/account-executive-api-mid-market-enterprise-london-478801","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1792258815},{"slug":"senior-technical-support-engineer-ii-sydney-australia-357935","company_name":"Pingidentity","title":"Senior Technical Support Engineer II","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose Statement:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Technical Support Engineer II, you will play a critical role in ensuring seamless customer experiences by providing high-quality technical assistance. You will be part of the global support team, working on a shifted schedule that includes weekends to ensure continuous support coverage. In this role, you will assist with product-specific cases, manage case escalations, provide phone support and respond to alerts, helping Ping Identity deliver superior customer support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interacting with customers, responding in a professional and efficient manner, helping them identify and resolve technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting or exceeding customer expectations on response quality, timeliness and overall customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as Queue Manager (QM) during weekend shifts, ensuring efficient case handling and triaging support requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing technical support across multiple products, ensuring efficient troubleshooting, identification of root cause and issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where assigned products are not within their core expertise, work within established product runbooks and escalate to the on-call Product SME as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and responding to phone support and alerts, escalating cases as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicating with customers and partners via the online support tool, and via audio and video calls and screen-sharing sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reproducing customer problems internally, to enable the development and testing of a resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with Support, Engineering, SREs, Product Management and Customer Success teams. Showing a respect for all team members and customers at all times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collecting information and documenting bugs with Engineering or Training/Documentation for product/service issues that are impacting customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively prioritizing tasks/workload with self-discipline and good timekeeping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adopting an &#39;always-learning&#39; mentality, with a humble attitude about knowledge limitations, and the ability to learn from experience and informal/formal instruction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in escalation calls, when required, to brief stakeholder management on support cases, and assist in the creation of action plans aiming to solve customer issues as quickly as possible. Showing empathy for the customer&#39;s situation and listening with the intent to understand the situation clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring best practices are followed and processes are adhered to, especially with regard to ISO27001/9001 compliance, security incidents and data breaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically requires a minimum of 5+ years of related experience with a Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent Communication - both verbal and written; support is conducted via web-based ticketing system, web conferencing and phone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable collaboration and teamwork skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize workload and adapt to a fast-paced, follow-the-sun support model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be a good listener; identifying key information in order to reproduce a customer’s problem remotely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background of working on Linux, Unix &amp;amp; Windows Enterprise Server OS, with mixed skills around administration and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of the technical fundamentals of the Internet - you should have a solid knowledge of protocols such as HTTP, SSL and IPv4/v6&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Java, web containers (e.g. Tomcat, JBoss) and web servers (e.g. Apache, IIS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of virtualisation in an enterprise environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud-based platform services - AWS, Azure, Google Cloud Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps deployments - Docker, Scripting, Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking infrastructure - Proxies, Load balancers, Firewalls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Installing/tuning/code analysis of Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java performance analysis - Heap maps/JMAP/GC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directory - LDAP, AD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databases – SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming languages - JavaScript, Groovy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Ping:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in and facilitate a flexible, collaborative work environment. We’re growing quickly, but remain true to the innovative, can-do startup values that got us here. Most importantly, we keep hiring talented, smart, fun, and genuinely nice people because that’s who we want to succeed with every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are just a few of the things that make Ping special:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture that empowers you to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that create a sense of belonging for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team bonding events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive benefits and perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global volunteering and community initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO &amp;amp; Holiday Schedule&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Healthcare Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity for Education Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Offset (Specific locations)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ping is the collective sum of all our individual experiences, backgrounds and influences and we pride ourselves in growing and learning together. We are committed to building an inclusive and diverse environment where everyone’s individuality is respected and everyone has an Identity. In recruiting for new colleagues, we welcome the unique contributions you can bring and encourage you to be your best self.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.&amp;nbsp; All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex including sexual orientation and gender identity, national origin, disability, protected Veteran Status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pingidentity/senior-technical-support-engineer-ii-sydney-australia-357935","tags":["3110 Support Engineers"],"job_types":[],"location":"Sydney, Australia","created_at":1792248916},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-reference-data-ai-ml-uk-edinburgh-465630","company_name":"Addepar1","title":"Staff Software Engineer - Reference Data - AI/ML (UK)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking a Staff Software Engineer with AI/ML background to join our Reference Data team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reference data team at Addepar is responsible to manage the data reconciliation and curation process for market data providers to build a single source of truth and provide alignment across public and alternative investment data products for the client to manage their investment portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an engineer on the team you will partner with product teams at Addepar to understand their business needs. The team is focused on enabling and building disruptive, innovative solutions to transform the wealth technology landscape with AI across our product suite and is growing quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for architecting, leading, and driving the execution of the core AI capabilities that power our platform. This is a high-impact role for an engineer who thrives on the frontier of applied AI and maintains a relentless focus on shipping. You will not just work with LLMs and agentic frameworks; you will own the end-to-end delivery of AI-native products, ensuring that cutting-edge AI systems are hardened into robust, scalable, and high-performance production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the end-to-end execution and delivery of AI-native products, moving from initial prototype to scalable production services with high velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build, and productionize core components of our AI platform – including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LLMs and the surrounding ecosystem (e.g., vector DBs, prompt tuning, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core agent capabilities like MCP/ cross-platform tool use, web browsing, computer use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce technical discipline and operational excellence for all of our AI products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly iterate on AI products based on performance metrics and user feedback to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the evaluation and adoption of new AI technologies and frameworks to keep Addepar on the frontier of the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers and other engineering teams to translate strategic goals into technical realities, abstracting AI complexity so they can iterate quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with our engineering leads to define and implement our platform architecture to meet Addepar’s growth and scalability needs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and drive strategic business and technology decisions for the company and for customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a technical thought leader in multiple areas who educates and shares best practices. Your contributions deliver strategic and prescriptive guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S., or M.S. in Computer Science or similar technical field of study (or equivalent practical experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of owning and shipping complex, production-grade systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience shipping and maintaining AI-native products or features, or demonstrable passion through significant personal projects in AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep ownership mindset, seeing projects through to completion and raising the bar for execution across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong bias for action, with a passion for shipping rapidly and iterating with feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS in Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, or another quantitative field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Preferred] Specific experience with LLMs and agentic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Preferred] Hands-on experience with technologies in the modern AI/LLM ecosystem, such as Databricks, Langchain, or MLFlow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Preferred] Advanced understanding of the probabilistic systems underpinning modern LLMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Preferred] Experience building AI products in highly accuracy-sensitive domains such as finance is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Think and operate with intention, purpose and care. Own outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
