&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roku is changing how the world watches TV&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we&#39;ve set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From your first day at Roku, you&#39;ll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We&#39;re a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does the team work on?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is the No. 1 TV streaming platform in the US, Canada and Mexico, with more than 100 million active accounts. Every ad impression across that platform has to be cleared and priced in real time — that is what the Ads Auctions and Marketplace Optimization team does. We build the auction mechanics, the pricing and pacing logic, and the low-latency systems that run them, balancing outcomes for advertisers, publishers, viewers, and Roku on every request. We are growing the team in Cambridge, which is becoming its largest hub, alongside colleagues in Amsterdam, Austin, San Jose, Ukraine and Uruguay — so you would be shaping how the UK side of this team works rather than inheriting it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is the role?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build the systems that apply mathematical and algorithmic rigour to optimise across multiple objectives, deciding which ads get served, in which placements, and when. The work spans auction mechanics, optimisation, the output of predictive ML models, and the real-time infrastructure underneath, mostly in Java on the JVM. It is hands-on and senior in scope: expect to move between whiteboard-level design and production code in the same week, and to own problems from framing through rollout. You will work directly with the hiring manager and a small group of senior engineers, in codebases shared with other ads engineers, on problems where your decisions are visible in revenue. You will optimise for second-order effects in a marketplace where participants react to each other, and to us, in real time. We are looking for people who are enthusiastic about solving these kinds of problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How will I use AI at Roku?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Roku, we don&#39;t just use AI, we work with it. AI agents and smart tools help power drafts, analysis, and repetitive workflows, while our people bring direction, judgment, and accountability. We&#39;re looking for curious, adaptable builders who can show how they&#39;ve used AI or automation to move faster, raise the bar, and scale their impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value your AI skills if you have built fluency across the agentic engineering toolchain — coding harnesses like Claude Code or Cursor, MCP servers, custom skills, or agent frameworks. And you can describe projects where you shipped real work with these tools. You know how to drive an agent, verify its output, and ramp on an unfamiliar codebase with an agent helping you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are the responsibilities of the role?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build components of Roku&#39;s real-time ad auction and marketplace systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-objective optimisation at the core of the auction, balancing what advertisers, publishers, viewers, and Roku each want from the same impression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own development work end to end, from framing the problem through production rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate JVM services where latency and reliability are product requirements, not stretch goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use probability, statistics and experimentation to test changes before and after launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with AI tooling as a normal part of how you design, build, test and review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain technical trade-offs clearly to engineering and cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What experience would help someone be successful in this role at Roku?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Around six or more years building production software, with strong systems judgement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience in Java or another JVM language, or depth in a comparable statically typed language such as C#, C++ or Go, and the appetite to ramp on Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort designing and operating distributed systems at scale and low latency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid grounding in maths, algorithms, probability and statistics as applied to real systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI and agentic-tooling fluency, as described above&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ad tech, auctions or marketplace experience is preferred, and we move quickly for candidates who have it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comparable experience on mathematically rigorous or optimisation-heavy problems in another domain is an acceptable alternative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;#LI-MS3&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;What&#39;s Roku&#39;s approach to hybrid working?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku fosters an inclusive and collaborative environment where teams generally work in the office Monday through Thursday. Fridays are generally flexible for remote work, except for employees whose specific roles or assigned office location require five days&#39; a week attendance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are some of the benefits?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is committed to offering a diverse range of benefits as part of our compensation package to support our employees and their families. Our comprehensive benefits include global access to mental health and financial wellness support and resources. Local benefits include statutory and voluntary benefits which may include healthcare (medical, dental, and vision), life, accident, disability, commuter, and retirement options (401(k)/pension). Employees are supported in taking time off, in accordance with local leave policies and other personal needs to support their evolving work and life needs. It&#39;s important to note that not every benefit is available in all locations or for every role. For details specific to your location, please consult with your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku welcomes applicants of all backgrounds and provides reasonable accommodations and adjustments in accordance with applicable law. If you require reasonable accommodation at any point in the hiring process, please direct your inquiries to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What should I know about Roku&#39;s culture?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is a great place for people who want to work in a fast-paced environment where everyone is focused on the company&#39;s success rather than their own. We try to surround ourselves with people who are great at their jobs, who are easy to work with, and who keep their egos in check. We appreciate a sense of humor. We believe a fewer number of very talented folks can do more for less cost than a larger number of less talented teams. We&#39;re independent thinkers with big ideas who act boldly, move fast and accomplish extraordinary things through collaboration and trust. In short, at Roku you&#39;ll be part of a company that&#39;s changing how the world watches TV. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a unique culture that we are proud of. We think of ourselves primarily as problem-solvers, which itself is a two-part idea. We come up with the solution, but the solution isn&#39;t real until it is built and delivered to the customer. That penchant for action gives us a pragmatic approach to innovation, one that has served us well since 2002. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about Roku, our global footprint, and how we&#39;ve grown, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.weareroku.com/factsheet&quot;&gt;https://www.weareroku.com/factsheet&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By providing your information, you acknowledge that you want Roku to contact you about job roles, that you have read Roku&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.weareroku.com/roku-job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-job-applicants&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;, and understand that Roku will use your information as described in that notice. If you do not wish to receive any communications from Roku regarding this role or similar roles in the future, you may unsubscribe at any time by emailing &lt;a ----- -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/roku/sr-software-engineer-ads-auctions-marketplace-optimization-cambridge-493899","tags":["225 - Advertising Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Cambridge","created_at":1792248914},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-web-development-ai-manchester-245249","company_name":"Roku","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Web Development – AI","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color: #662d91;&quot;&gt;Teamwork makes the stream work.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roku is changing how the world watches TV&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we&#39;ve set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From your first day at Roku, you&#39;ll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We&#39;re a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What does the team work on?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ads Customer Interfaces team develops full-stack web application services, APIs, and UIs that provide a unified approach to interfacing with internal and external customers across Roku&#39;s suite of advertising products. Our mission is to provide the best-in-class user experience and service while aiming to delight users of our products by making their jobs easier and allowing them to focus on their customers instead of getting bogged down by tedious business processes. In this role, you will work as a key member of the Ads Customer Interfaces team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What is the role?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku pioneered streaming to the TV and continues to innovate and lead the industry. While we are well-positioned to help shape the future of television and streaming media worldwide, continued success stems from experienced software engineers like you developing core features for the Roku platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our new Senior Software Engineer will be contributing extensively to our container orchestrated platform, bringing together some of the latest web technologies with Ai expertise to develop a truly scalable and responsive web applications. To be successful you’ll need extensive experience of building reliable and scalable cloud-based solutions, a strong background in software engineering and an appetite to keep on top of modern software practices. This is a great role for a senior professional who enjoys a high level of visibility and thrives on great business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The features and performance improvements you implement directly impact millions of users every day. This is a great role for an experienced professional who has innovative ideas for complex problems and can translate these ideas into ultra-reliable software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How will I use AI at Roku?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;At Roku, we don’t just use AI, we work with it. AI agents and smart tools help power drafts, analysis, and repetitive workflows, while our people bring direction, judgment, and accountability. We’re looking for curious, adaptable builders who can show how they’ve used AI or automation to move faster, raise the bar, and scale their impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We value your AI skills if have built fluency across the agentic engineering toolchain — coding harnesses like Claude Code or Cursor, MCP servers, custom skills, or agent frameworks. And you can describe projects where you shipped real work with these tools. You know how to drive an agent, verify its output, and ramp on an unfamiliar codebase with an agent helping you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What are the responsiblities of the role?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop and deliver high-quality web applications and back-end services with modern frameworks and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a part of a high functioning team consisting of UX designers, software engineers, dev-ops, quality assurance and product management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and integrate AI-powered features into web applications and enterprise tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) solutions to power chatbot interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work both independently and paired with other team members to ensure efficient delivery of prioritised features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in the planning and refinement of features along with the team to come up with innovative and collaborative designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new features and write test cases to ensure the quality of your code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with CI/CD tools to ensure that all software developed adheres to both quality and scaling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a role in continuously improving our software delivery process, making it as efficient as possible, reducing wasteful activities and creating value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See a feature go all the way from design stage to being deployed into customer facing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate the ability to dig deep to find solutions to challenging problems affecting our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What experience would help someone be successful in this role at Roku?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive expeirence&amp;nbsp; in JavaScript/TypeScript and modern web frameworks (React, Next.js, Angular, Node.js, Express) on cloud-based technology, such as AWS and GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of building large scale and low latency distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of algorithms, data structures, performance optimisation techniques, object-oriented programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using modern AI-assisted and agentic development workflows in day-to-day engineering using&amp;nbsp;AI/ML APIs and SDKs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience developing RAG solutions or working with LLMs for chatbots is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of CI/CD and the tools used to implement them, such as Jenkins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software repository tools, such as GitLab and GitHub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with productivity tools, such as Jira and Confluence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A good understanding of Agile practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to accurately estimate software tasks and work to schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to observability tools and practices (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana) are preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of databases and data architecture choices (SQL vs NoSQL, caching layers, and data access patterns)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of tuning performance and reliability for highly available services and web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with web security fundamentals and secure engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors of Masters Degree in Compute Science/Software Engineering or related subject&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;#LI-PA1&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-P&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;What&#39;s Roku&#39;s approach to hybrid working?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku fosters an inclusive and collaborative environment where teams generally work in the office Monday through Thursday. Fridays are generally flexible for remote work, except for employees whose specific roles or assigned office location require five days&#39; a week attendance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are some of the benefits?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is committed to offering a diverse range of benefits as part of our compensation package to support our employees and their families. Our comprehensive benefits include global access to mental health and financial wellness support and resources. Local benefits include statutory and voluntary benefits which may include healthcare (medical, dental, and vision), life, accident, disability, commuter, and retirement options (401(k)/pension). Employees are supported in taking time off, in accordance with local leave policies and other personal needs to support their evolving work and life needs. It&#39;s important to note that not every benefit is available in all locations or for every role. For details specific to your location, please consult with your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku welcomes applicants of all backgrounds and provides reasonable accommodations and adjustments in accordance with applicable law. If you require reasonable accommodation at any point in the hiring process, please direct your inquiries to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What should I know about Roku&#39;s culture?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is a great place for people who want to work in a fast-paced environment where everyone is focused on the company&#39;s success rather than their own. We try to surround ourselves with people who are great at their jobs, who are easy to work with, and who keep their egos in check. We appreciate a sense of humor. We believe a fewer number of very talented folks can do more for less cost than a larger number of less talented teams. We&#39;re independent thinkers with big ideas who act boldly, move fast and accomplish extraordinary things through collaboration and trust. In short, at Roku you&#39;ll be part of a company that&#39;s changing how the world watches TV. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a unique culture that we are proud of. We think of ourselves primarily as problem-solvers, which itself is a two-part idea. We come up with the solution, but the solution isn&#39;t real until it is built and delivered to the customer. That penchant for action gives us a pragmatic approach to innovation, one that has served us well since 2002. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about Roku, our global footprint, and how we&#39;ve grown, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.weareroku.com/factsheet&quot;&gt;https://www.weareroku.com/factsheet&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By providing your information, you acknowledge that you want Roku to contact you about job roles, that you have read Roku&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.weareroku.com/roku-job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-job-applicants&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;, and understand that Roku will use your information as described in that notice. If you do not wish to receive any communications from Roku regarding this role or similar roles in the future, you may unsubscribe at any time by emailing &lt;a ----- -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/roku/senior-software-engineer-web-development-ai-manchester-245249","tags":["225 - Advertising Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792248914},{"slug":"assembly-and-test-technician-cirencester-271810","company_name":"Arcticrd","title":"Assembly and Test Technician","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">LOCATION: CALMSDEN, CIRENCESTER, UK. LIMITED FIELD TRAVEL AS REQUIRED | 5 DAYS ONSITE</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE LAST FRONTIER</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ARD was founded on a paradox. The Arctic is both the next great economic frontier and one of the most hostile environments on Earth. Rich in resources and strategically vital, yet bone-chillingly cold, dark for months, and fundamentally inhospitable to humans. This paradox - an explosion of activity in a place that resists human presence - is why we exist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our solution is autonomy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build systems that operate reliably and intelligently in the Arctic, so that humans don't always have to.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by record-holding pioneers with decades of polar experience, we take calculated risks on hard problems that matter. If you want to build and deploy ground-up technology with real-world impact, at an inflection point in history that won’t reappear, we’d like to talk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ARD is growing and we’re looking for an <strong>Assembly and Test Technician</strong> to help us build and test our ruggedized hardware - from field-ready energy and battery systems to the autonomous platforms we deploy in the Arctic. Right now, our biggest constraint isn’t design. It’s the time it takes to assemble and test what we’ve designed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to our <strong>Senior Test Engineer</strong>, you’ll join our engineering team, working alongside our mechanical and electrical engineers and across our main hardware workstreams. You’ll take hands-on ownership of assembly and testing, helping with the practical implementation and testing of engineering designs. Within your first 3 months, you’ll have helped to take assembly and test off the critical path on our key projects, and helped put in place the documentation and test processes that let us build and test consistently, unit after unit.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CORE RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assemble mechanical and electrical sub-assemblies, harnesses, PCBAs,  and complete units to drawings and build instructions, so they’re ready for test on schedule.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run test phases on assemblies and finished units and record the results accurately, so issues are found and fixed before hardware reaches the field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help set up repeatable test processes, from test plans and rigs to how results are captured, working closely with our Senior Test Engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and maintain build instructions, test procedures and records, raising the standard of our engineering documentation as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot and report problems found during build and test, giving engineers the detail they need to debug and improve the next design revision.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a practical, hands-on technician who takes pride in building things properly and getting the details right. You’re methodical, you like a clear process, and you’d rather write something down than rely on memory. You might come from a technician role in engineering, manufacturing or a test lab, an engineering apprenticeship, the armed forces, or a mechanical or electrical engineering degree with plenty of hands-on build experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">* <u>Please note: this role is not eligible for visa sponsorship</u> *</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An engineering qualification (such as an HNC/HND, apprenticeship or degree in mechanical or electrical engineering), or equivalent hands-on experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience assembling mechanical or electrical hardware in a workshop, lab or production setting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with basic soldering equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work from engineering drawings, schematics and written build instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running tests on hardware and recording the results accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident using common workshop tools and electrical test equipment, such as multimeters and bench power supplies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable owning your own tasks with guidance from the engineering team, and raising problems early when a build or test doesn’t go to plan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing or improving build instructions, test procedures or other technical documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with electrical assembly such as wiring looms, crimping or soldering, or working with battery systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building hardware in small batches or repeat runs, rather than one-off prototypes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with surface-mount PCB assembly</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Future Security Clearance Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our business scales into the defence and security sectors, the responsibilities of this role are expected to evolve to include projects requiring <strong>UK Security Check (SC) clearance</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">While an active clearance is not required to apply or start in this role, candidates must be willing and eligible to undergo UK Government security vetting in the future should project requirements dictate it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To meet the standard eligibility criteria for UK standard SC vetting, you must typically have resided in the UK for the <strong>past 5 continuous years</strong>, hold a valid passport, and be capable of passing comprehensive background, financial, and criminal record checks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why ARD</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The mission </strong>- The Arctic is the fastest-changing region on Earth. You'll build the intelligence layer that helps understand and steward it — an early-warning system for the planet's coldest edge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early stage, real influence</strong> - ARD is at an exciting early stage. You'll join while our products, team and culture are still taking shape, and your ideas will directly influence where we go next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and accountability</strong> - We give people real responsibility from day one. You'll own your work end to end, be trusted to make decisions, and be accountable for delivering results that ship and get used.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A small but growing team</strong> - You'll work closely with experienced colleagues across science, software and hardware, with no layers in between. As we grow, you'll help build the team and the ways of working that come next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Health Insurance from Day 1</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dental &amp; Vision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity - meaningful options as an early employee at an early-stage company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real field exposure - travel to Arctic sites and Outposts when needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission-driven culture - focus on impact, not hours logged</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ARD is an equal opportunities employer. We hire on merit, based on skills, experience and potential, and welcome applications from everyone regardless of age, disability, gender reassignment, marriage or civil partnership, pregnancy or maternity, race, religion or belief, sex or sexual orientation. We know great candidates sometimes hold back unless they tick every box, so if this role excites you but your experience doesn’t match every point, we’d still love to hear from you, especially if you bring a background or perspective that is under-represented in science and engineering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you need any adjustments during the application or interview process, please don't hesitate to let us know at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-TK1</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/arcticrd/assembly-and-test-technician-cirencester-271810","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Calmsden, Cirencester","created_at":1792248017},{"slug":"sales-director-london-14714","company_name":"Neudata","title":"Sales Director","description":"<h2>Join Neudata - Sales Director (EMEA &amp; Asia-Pacific)</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Introducing Neudata:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neudata is the global leader in alternative and market data intelligence, helping investors, hedge funds and corporates discover, evaluate, and use data to make smarter decisions. Our independence is what really sets us apart - we provide objective, unbiased intelligence that our clients trust and depend on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With offices in London, New York, and Shanghai and a team of 100 people, we connect a vast global network of buyers and providers through our market-leading platforms and specialist consulting - and by providing a clear view of the data landscape, we help organisations navigate complexity and find their competitive edge. Joining Neudata really puts you at the heart of the fintech industry, where your work directly influences the data-driven strategies of the world's most sophisticated organisations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an experienced, entrepreneurial Sales Director to take our Scout and Ranger platforms to data buyers across EMEA and APAC: hedge funds, asset managers, private equity firms and the fast-growing world of AI. This is a pure new business role, and you'll own your territory end to end, from spotting the opportunity through to signing the deal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnering directly with our Chief Revenue Officer, you'll play an important part in refining how we approach the EMEA and APAC data buyer markets, identifying opportunities for growth, developing repeatable sales practices, and laying the foundations for an expanded European sales team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be the face of Neudata in front of some of the most sophisticated investors in the market, running story-led demonstrations, guiding hands-on trials alongside our research analysts, and building relationships with the people who decide how their firms use external data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage applications from high-performing Sales Reps looking to take on greater ownership and responsibility in a fast-growing organisation. There is potential for the successful candidate to take on a leadership role over time. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the EMEA and Asia-Pacific territory of institutional investor prospects, driving new business through proactive outreach, travelling to meet prospects in-person, and lead generation campaigns across email and socials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the full sales cycle: leading discovery and qualification calls, delivering value-based, story-led demonstrations of Scout and Ranger, then negotiating commercial terms and closing in line with quota</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage hands-on platform trials in partnership with our research analysts, aligning technical and business criteria so prospects can see the value for themselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Neudata on stage and on the ground, presenting at our own high-profile events and at external conferences in the UK and overseas</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become a trusted advisor to senior stakeholders, from Heads of Data and Portfolio Managers through to Procurement Leads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the CRO to develop and execute territory plans, prioritise attractive markets and client segments, and identify opportunities to accelerate growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep your pipeline sharp with rigorous CRM discipline and accurate forecasting, and feed market insight back to our product and research teams to help shape where we go next</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the development of repeatable sales processes, messaging and best practices that can support an expanded European sales team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the team expands, contribute to the recruitment, onboarding, coaching and development of new sales colleagues, with scope to take on formal management responsibilities</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in data, research or information sales, ideally into financial services, with a proven track record of originating and closing complex new logo deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp commercial acumen and the confidence to negotiate and close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience independently developing new territories, market segments and commercial opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Outstanding presentation and communication skills, in person and online, in front of senior and technical audiences alike</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with how investment firms buy, particularly asset managers and hedge funds, and with the stakeholders involved along the way</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine enthusiasm for alternative data, market data and investment research, and curiosity about where the data landscape is heading</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coaching or managing people in a commercial setting is a bonus, but not essential</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Benefits &amp; Perks:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days' annual leave + bank holidays, plus an extra day for each year of service (up to 30 days), alongside one paid volunteering day and two paid study days per year 📅</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid and flexible working, including working from anywhere for up to 10 working days per year from a location of your choosing 🌍</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private medical insurance via Vitality (including dental, optical, and hearing) ✚</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced maternity, paternity, adoption and shared parental policies 🏠</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced pension scheme via NEST 📈</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee referral bonus of £1,000 per successful new hire you refer 💸</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Details:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: </strong>London (Moorgate) with hybrid working. Frequent travel across EMEA and Asia is anticipated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary:</strong> Competitive base salary and commission structure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start Date: </strong>ASAP</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Line Manager: </strong>Chief Revenue Officer</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruitment Process:</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial screening call with our Talent Acquisition Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First-stage competency interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meetings with key Neudata stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final stage interview</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis, and shortlisted candidates will be invited to an initial screening call with our Talent Acquisition Manager.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applicants must be eligible to work in the UK. Candidates who may require visa sponsorship should discuss this with the hiring manager during the interview process. Further information on Skilled Worker sponsorship can be found <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa/your-job"><u>here</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/neudata/sales-director-london-14714","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792248017},{"slug":"sales-development-representative-london-193395","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Sales Development Representative","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join the go-to-market team at a Series A HR technology company and help build its outbound sales engine. You will connect with HR, Finance, and executive leaders at multinational businesses, helping grow a modern employee 