/></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 What you'll own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, develop, and inspire a team of four People BPs globally, fostering a high-performance, collaborative, and commercially-minded team culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted strategic advisor to senior leaders and executive stakeholders, translating business priorities into people plans that drive performance and engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the evolving people  partnering operating model - setting the standard for how the function delivers across the employee lifecycle; from org design and workforce planning to talent management,employee relations, and offboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with the Chief People Officer and Chief of Staff to shape and execute Kraken's people strategy, ensuring it reflects the culture, and the needs of a rapidly growing and changing global business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Coach, advise, and collaborate on complex, sensitive, and high-profile ER matters, bringing sound judgement, clear process, and a fair and empathetic approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive organisational effectiveness initiatives including restructures, role design, capability building, and team design, partnering cross-functionally to ensure execution is smooth and thoughtful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion data-led people practices - using workforce insights and people analytics to inform decisions and demonstrate impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the People BP function in leadership forums, contributing to the broader People Capability agenda and influencing how we attract, develop, and retain talent globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Kraken's international growth by providing people partnering expertise as we enter new markets and scale existing ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with COE partners (Talent Acquisition, Total Rewards, L&amp;D, and People Operations) to ensure a  consistent people experience developed with our culture in mind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 What you bring to the party</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in senior People Business Partnering or HR leadership roles (10 years), ideally within a fast-growing technology or global organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of leading and developing a team of People BPs, with the ability to coach, delegate, and agree clear direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A credible and confident communicator with demonstrated experience influencing C-suite and senior business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of the full people partner toolkit - org design, workforce planning, talent management, succession, and complex ER.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data-literate with the ability to use people insights to shape strategy and tell compelling stories to stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong commercial acumen; you understand how people decisions drive business outcomes and can connect the dots between the two.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience operating across multiple geographies and time zones, with an understanding of employment frameworks in the UK, Europe, and ideally APAC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to operate with pace and pragmatism in an ambiguous, high-growth environment while maintaining rigour and quality in delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative by nature - you build bridges across teams and bring people with you, rather than working in silos.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⭐️ Bonus points</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in the energy, utilities, or climate tech sector.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to scaling teams and organisations through rapid growth phases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting international expansion, including standing up people partnering capability in new markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with  employment law landscapes beyond the UK, Europe, and APAC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with a Chief People Officer and/or Chief of Staff in a global business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Are you ready for a career with us? We want to ensure you have the right tools and environment to unleash your potential. If you have any accommodation requests, please contact us at ----- We’ll do our best to tailor the experience to your needs so you can feel comfortable, confident and be at your best!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Studies have shown that some groups of people, like women, are less likely to apply to a role unless they meet 100% of the job requirements. Whoever you are, if you like one of our jobs, we encourage you to apply as you might just be the candidate we’re looking for! At Kraken, we're creating a team of genuine, honest, empathetic people. Our people are our strongest asset and the unique skills and perspectives people bring to the team are the driving force of our success. As an equal opportunity employer, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute. We consider all applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, national origin, age, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, disability, or any other legally protected status.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">*Our (i) <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://kraken.tech/candidate-privacy-not