Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trainline/senior-engineering-manager-customer-growth-london-464131","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792248015},{"slug":"machine-learning-engineering-manager-london-162059","company_name":"Trainline","title":"Machine Learning Engineering Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trainline, our purpose is to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.thetrainline.com/terms/sustainability-faqs">empower greener travel choices, connecting people and places.</a> Trainline enables millions of travellers to find and book the best value tickets across carriers, fares, and journey options through our highly rated mobile app, website, and B2B partner channels. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Great journeys start with Trainline 🚄 </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Europe’s leading independent rail platform, helping millions of travellers find and book the best-value rail and coach journeys across our app, website and partner channels.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our job is to make the green travel choice the best choice. By building a better train travel experience, we help more people choose rail - creating a positive impact for customers, our business and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of more than 1,000 Trainliners from over 50 nationalities, working across London, Paris, Barcelona, Milan, Edinburgh and Madrid. Now is a brilliant time to join us and help shape the future of travel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Introducing the Trainline Machine Learning and AI Team 👋</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Machine learning is at the heart of Trainline’s mission to help millions of people make sustainable travel choices every day. Our models and AI agents support customers when journeys go wrong, power search and recommendations across our apps and website, find the best fares through pricing and routing optimisation, personalise the experience with generative AI, and make our digital marketing smarter. Our teams own the full lifecycle from idea to production, and work closely with colleagues across the business to grow the impact of ML and AI at Trainline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Machine Learning Engineering Manager to lead a team of 7 ML engineers and data engineers within our Core Experience pillar, which covers Search, Supply and Commerce. Your team’s work sits at the centre of how customers find, compare and buy their tickets. You’ll be accountable for what your team ships and how it ships it: the quality of the systems, the pace of delivery and the growth of the people building them. You’ll work alongside data scientists, software engineers and product managers. You’ll stay close enough to the technical work to make good calls on architecture, trade-offs and risk. What unites us is curiosity, a love of what we do and a desire to make sustainable travel the easy choice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In this role, you will... 🚄</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach and grow a team of ML and data engineers. That means setting clear expectations, giving regular feedback, managing performance and building an inclusive team where people do their best work</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire for the team, shaping the roles we need and running a fair, rigorous interview process</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own delivery: plan and prioritise with your product partners across Search, Supply and Commerce, unblock the team, and ship ML and AI systems that move measurable customer and business outcomes</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the technical direction for your team’s systems, including architecture, build-versus-buy, and knowing when a simpler approach beats a more sophisticated one</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure the team builds well across the whole lifecycle: reliable data pipelines, high-quality features, rigorous offline and online evaluation (including A/B testing), reliable deployment, monitoring and ongoing maintenance</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the team in building production-grade agentic systems, using orchestration harnesses such as LangGraph to design multi-step workflows, tool use and human-in-the-loop controls</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make evaluation a first-class engineering discipline for LLM and agent work. That means curated eval sets, LLM-as-judge and human review, tracing, regression testing of prompts and agents, and online monitoring of quality, cost and latency</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the guardrails for responsible use of AI, covering safety, privacy and clear fallbacks when an agent shouldn’t act on its own</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the bar on engineering practice through code and design reviews, CI/CD, MLOps, observability and on-call</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with senior leaders and partner teams, explaining progress, trade-offs and impact in plain language</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to our wider AI and ML community and help keep a culture of learning, curiosity and experimentation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’d love to hear from you if you have... 🔎</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience line-managing engineers, including hiring, performance management and career development</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong background as an ML engineer, with a track record of taking models into production and keeping them healthy at scale</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough grounding in data engineering (pipelines, data modelling and data quality) to lead data engineers as well as ML engineers</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid Python and software engineering fundamentals, with enough hands-on depth to review code and designs credibly</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depth in at least one area such as ranking and recommendation, predictive modelling, optimisation or NLP, backed by a solid grasp of statistics, experimentation and feature engineering</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with modern ML infrastructure on a major cloud platform, ideally AWS, covering distributed data processing, orchestration, model management and infrastructure as code</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience shipping agentic or LLM-based systems, including agent orchestration frameworks, tool use, RAG, and fine-tuning where it earns its place</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A disciplined approach to evaluating LLM and agent systems, using tools such as Braintrust, and a clear view on how to know whether an agent is working well in production</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication with technical and non-technical colleagues, and good judgement on priorities when there’s more to do than people to do it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our tech stack 💻</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build mostly in Python on AWS, and choose tools for what they do in production rather than for novelty. You don’t need to know all of it on day one.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data and compute: </strong>S3, Athena, Spark on EMR, SQL</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Orchestration and MLOps: </strong>Airflow, MLflow, Docker, ECS, Terraform, GitHub Actions for CI/CD</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Models: </strong>foundation models served through Amazon Bedrock</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agents: </strong>LangGraph for orchestration, deployed and run on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, with MCP for tool integration</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluation: </strong>Braintrust for evals, tracing and monitoring agent quality in production</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More information:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy fantastic perks like private healthcare &amp; dental insurance, a generous work from abroad policy, 2-for-1 share purchase plans, an EV Scheme to further reduce carbon emissions, extra festive time off, and excellent family-friendly benefits. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We prioritise career growth with clear career paths, transparent pay bands, personal learning budgets, and regular learning days. Jump on board and supercharge your career from day one! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're operating a hybrid model and ask that Trainliners work from the office a minimum of 60% of their time over a 12-week period. We also have a 28-day Work from Abroad policy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our values represent the things that matter most to us and what we live and breathe everyday, in everything we do: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💭 <strong>Think Big</strong> - We're building the future of rail </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✔️ <strong>Own It </strong>- We focus on every customer, partner and journey </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 <strong> Travel Together</strong> - We're one team </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">♻️<strong> Do Good</strong> - We make a positive impact </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that having a diverse team makes us better and helps us succeed. And we mean all forms of diversity - gender, ethnicity, sexuality, disability, nationality and diversity of thought. That's why we're committed to creating inclusive places to work, where everyone belongs and differences are valued and celebrated.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interested in finding out more about what it's like to work at Trainline? Why not check us out on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/trainline/">LinkedIn</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/lifeattrainline/">Instagram</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Trainline-EI_IE249203.11,20.htm">Glassdoor</a>! </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trainline/machine-learning-engineering-manager-london-162059","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792248015},{"slug":"corporate-account-executive-public-sector-london-468387","company_name":"Avepoint","title":"Corporate Account Executive - Public Sector","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Corporate Account Executive, Public Sector, you will own new-logo acquisition across a defined vertical and account set in the UK, Ireland and South Africa. Your focus will be public sector organisations with 2,000–7,499 employees. This is a dedicated new-business role and you are unlikely to inherit existing customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will use available account, industry and SKU growth data to create, own and execute a clear territory strategy focused on sustainable net-new ARR growth. You will manage the full sales cycle—from prospecting and opportunity creation through procurement, negotiation and close—while building trusted relationships with business, technical, procurement and executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a self-sourcing role. You will have access to Business Development, Solutions Engineering, Partner Account Management and marketing resources, but this support is intended to complement—not replace—your personal accountability for creating pipeline. As a channel-first organisation, close alignment with the Partner Account Manager and partner ecosystem will be central to how you develop routes to market, generate demand and win business. Customer Success support will become available once a customer reaches the applicable ARR threshold.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating, validating, owning and executing a data-led territory and account plan that sets out how you will achieve an annual net-new ARR target of approximately $900,000 USD once fully ramped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using account intelligence, industry trends, SKU performance and growth data to prioritise target accounts, identify whitespace and focus resources on the strongest ARR opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally sourcing pipeline through disciplined prospecting, executive outreach, networking, events, social selling and account-based activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the BDR to increase coverage and accelerate opportunity creation, while retaining personal ownership of pipeline generation and territory performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading new-logo acquisition across assigned public sector accounts within your defined vertical, with no reliance on an inherited customer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the full sales cycle from initial engagement and qualification through discovery, solution development, business case, procurement, negotiation and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating effectively within a channel-first model by working closely with the PAM to build and execute partner-led account plans and routes to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing productive relationships with resellers, framework providers, distributors, system integrators and strategic alliance partners to create pipeline and close business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and progressing opportunities through public procurement frameworks, tenders, direct awards and other compliant purchasing routes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with Solutions Engineering to shape discovery, technical validation, demonstrations and solution design around customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with marketing to develop and execute targeted vertical, territory and account-based campaigns that generate measurable pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging Customer Success at the appropriate stage for customers that meet the applicable ARR threshold, ensuring a strong transition from sale to adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing complex sales cycles involving procurement, IT leadership, information governance, security, records management, finance and executive sponsors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positioning AvePoint&#39;s platform solutions against public sector priorities including digital transformation, cyber resilience, AI adoption, compliance, data governance and modern workplace initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering compelling presentations, workshops and value-based business cases that demonstrate measurable outcomes, commercial impact and return on investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining an accurate, current and sufficiently covered pipeline, forecast and account strategy within the CRM, with clear next steps and stakeholder ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attending virtual and face-to-face customer meetings, partner engagements, industry events and conferences across the territory as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Is this the role for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines agility, passion, accountability and teamwork with the commercial drive to build a territory from the ground up. You will be comfortable creating your own opportunities, mobilising supporting resources and remaining accountable for the overall ARR outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will understand how public sector organisations buy technology and be able to translate policy priorities, funding signals, market trends and customer challenges into focused account plans and commercially qualified opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be strategic and data-led, but equally willing to execute. Success requires a consistent prospecting cadence, disciplined qualification, strong internal orchestration and effective use of BDR, SE, PAM and marketing support without becoming dependent on those resources for pipeline creation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy winning new logos, developing partner-led routes to market, navigating complex public procurement and helping organisations achieve meaningful outcomes through technology, this role offers the opportunity to build and own a high-growth public sector territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience and qualities required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in a new-business software, SaaS, cloud, cybersecurity, information management or enterprise technology sales role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to self-source, develop and close net-new business opportunities against an ARR or recurring-revenue target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and executing a territory plan for a defined account set, segment or vertical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into public sector organisations is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of public procurement processes, framework agreements, tendering environments and partner-led purchasing routes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong channel mindset, with experience working effectively with Partner Account Managers, resellers, system integrators and alliance ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use market, account and performance data to prioritise activity and make sound commercial decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging and influencing executive, business, procurement and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultative, value-based sales approach with the ability to develop credible business cases and articulate measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prospecting, communication, presentation, negotiation and listening skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple complex opportunities and coordinate cross-functional resources without losing personal accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong forecasting discipline and experience maintaining accurate pipeline and account data in CRM systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience, curiosity, pace and a clear ownership mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market-competitive compensation including bonus scheme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career progression and internal mobility opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 days of annual leave, in addition to public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GBP 1.000,00/Year towards our Tuition Reimbursement Program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Referral Program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate Donation Matching Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maternity policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company sponsored events / regular team building events &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra paid perk days - Birthday off, Family/Life Event Day, Volunteering...&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-SB1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ui-provider a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak&quot;&gt;Any personal data you share with us during the application process will be processed strictly in compliance with applicable data protection laws and our &lt;a id=&quot;menur12n&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.avepoint.com/company/privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/avepoint/corporate-account-executive-public-sector-london-468387","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792238116},{"slug":"remote-senior-software-engineer-search-ai-80625","company_name":"Muckrack","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Search & AI","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Muck Rack is trusted by thousands of organizations around the world to understand how their brands show up across news, social media and AI-generated answers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI-powered platform connects the entire PR workflow in one place, helping communications teams manage media relationships, understand the conversations shaping their brands, take action and measure their impact. Combined with analyst-led Media Intelligence and advisory services, Muck Rack turns signals into insights and insights into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founder-controlled and growing&amp;nbsp; profitably and sustainably, we have the freedom to build forward-thinking products, put our customers first, and offer an inclusive culture that welcomes diverse perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a collaborative, self-motivated &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Search &amp;amp; AI&lt;/strong&gt; to join our growing team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you’ll help build and evolve the customer-facing search experiences that help users discover relevant, high-quality content, along with the backend systems that power them. You’ll work across the stack, with a slight emphasis on frontend development, and collaborate closely with engineers, Product, and Design to deliver intuitive search experiences backed by reliable, scalable search and data systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver customer-facing search features and workflows across frontend and backend systems, from technical planning through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-powered product experiences end to end, from the services behind them to the interfaces that make their output useful and trustworthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build intuitive, responsive user experiences using Vue while contributing to the Python and Django services that power them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and improve search, indexing, and retrieval systems that support high-quality content discovery across large volumes of data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain features and data workflows that leverage technologies such as Elasticsearch, Kafka, Celery, and MySQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful technical decisions and trade-offs that balance customer experience, delivery speed, performance, reliability, and long-term maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product, Design, and engineering teammates to shape solutions, clarify requirements, and deliver high-quality customer experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex production issues and drive improvements to the performance, reliability, observability, and maintainability of the systems you work on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call and incident response rotation, helping diagnose and resolve production issues and improve system reliability over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To Be Set Up for Success in This Role, You&#39;ll Need to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional software engineering experience building and maintaining production software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working across frontend and backend systems and independently delivering features throughout the application stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python or a similar programming language and experience with Django or a comparable web framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building polished, maintainable user-facing applications with Vue.js or another modern JavaScript framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Elasticsearch or a comparable search technology, or significant experience working with data-intensive systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making technical trade-offs within complex production systems while balancing immediate delivery needs with long-term quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing production issues and contributing to the reliability and operational health of the systems you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with TypeScript in a large codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with design systems or shared component libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to adjust working hours for overlap with teammates in US time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If Any of the Below Also Describe You, This Could Be an Exciting Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kafka or other streaming or event-driven technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MySQL, Postgres, or other relational databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Celery or other asynchronous task-processing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building search, discovery, indexing, or information-retrieval features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving frontend architecture, performance, or complex customer-facing workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with high-traffic SaaS applications or systems that process large volumes of data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building customer-facing features backed by LLMs or other AI models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience judging whether an AI-backed feature is actually working, through evaluation, testing, or user feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in journalism, news, media, or social media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In Addition, We&#39;re Always Looking for Candidates Who&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complex technical ideas clearly and collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of problems and drive work forward independently while knowing when to involve others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take pride in building readable, testable, maintainable software while making pragmatic technical trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach ambiguous or complex problems thoughtfully and use sound judgment to identify effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a strong engineering culture through thoughtful code reviews, knowledge sharing, feedback, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively incorporates AI tools into day-to-day work to improve productivity and accelerate delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Interview Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below you&#39;ll find an outline of the interview plan for this role. Please note that this is what we expect the process to look like; we may ask you for supplemental information or require an additional step before making a final decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 min interview with a member of our Talent Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 1 hour zoom interview with the hiring manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Peer interviews with several team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute Bar Raiser&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel &amp;amp; Team Engagement Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires up to 10% travel for team collaboration, customer engagements, and company events. As part of our commitment to building strong connections across our fully distributed team, attendance at our annual company offsite (typically held in Mexico) is expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;108&quot;&gt;The anticipated salary range for this role in Ireland is €95,000–€110,000 annually, depending on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;110&quot; data-end=&quot;211&quot;&gt;The anticipated salary for this role in Bulgaria is €6,000+ gross per month, depending on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual compensation decisions are based on a number of factors, including experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to peers at the company. We expect the majority of the candidates who are offered roles at our company to fall healthily throughout the range based on these factors. We recognize that the person we hire may be less experienced (or more senior) than this job description as posted. If that ends up being the case, the updated salary range will be communicated with you as a candidate.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Muck Rack?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote Work, Forever&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully distributed team with a permanent remote setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office stipend, phone and internet reimbursement, coworking membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtual and in-person team bonding (lunches, events, competitions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent &amp;amp; Fair Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive geo-neutral pay in the U.S.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual reviews to ensure equity and market alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardized bonus or commission structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance for employees and dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% premium coverage for individuals on high-deductible plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;24/7 Virtual Care and Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-funded HSA contributions and other pre-tax benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly wellness stipend and free Headspace subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off &amp;amp; Family Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;4+ weeks of PTO, plus paid sick and mental health days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;13 paid holidays with the option to swap for personal days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transparent pathways for internal mobility and promotion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bi-annual performance reviews, team workshops, and leadership training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited access to Coursera and O’Reilly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 additional PTO days annually for learning and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusive, Customer-First Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to equity and valuing diverse perspectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile, founder-led company focused on collaboration and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted by 3,000+ companies worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: Benefits and compensation reflect offerings for U.S.-based employees. Support is provided for employees in other locations, in compliance with local laws and regulations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we are a fully distributed team, we do have limitations on where we can hire and maintain a list of acceptable working locations based on job function. If we are unable to hire in your current location for the role for which you applied, you will be notified via email. While we enjoy many benefits as a permanently distributed and remote company, we cannot always support relocation or extended travel and have guidelines in place to ensure compliant work away from your designated permanent residence.&lt;/p&gt;
