al &amp; Operational Leadership:</strong> Make key build/buy/partner evaluations on blockchain networks, custody, and audit solutions. Guide team evolution as products move from build to operational phases, maintaining hands-on involvement during critical incidents.</li></ul><p></p><p>Requirements</p><ul><li><strong>Experience:</strong> Minimum 7 years of solution architecture experience, including at least 3 years dedicated to DLT or blockchain projects within high-value, 24/7 financial systems.</li><li><strong>DLT &amp; Distributed Systems Expertise:</strong> Deep fluency with EVM and permissioned chains (e.g., Canton, Hyperledger Besu).</li><li><strong>Regulated Token Standards:</strong> Hands-on experience with regulated security token standards (ERC-3643 / T-REX or equivalent), on-chain compliance models, and security considerations around smart contracts and cross-chain bridges.</li><li><strong>Capital Markets Knowledge:</strong> Strong working knowledge of capital markets settlement mechanisms (delivery-versus-payment, CSD operations, CCP/clearing) to effectively design system integrations.</li><li><strong>AI Engineering Competency:</strong> Proven ability to evaluate, select, and integrate AI tooling into the development lifecycle (e.g., testing, scaffolding) while establishing strict guardrails around prompt hygiene, secret security, and license provenance. Ability to specify in-product AI capabilities (e.g., anomaly detection) with proper risk controls.</li><li><strong>Leadership &amp; Communication:</strong> Strong decision-making skills and composure under pressure. Excellent stakeholder management skills to bridge technical, business, legal, and regulatory domains.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field. Professional certifications in cloud or blockchain technologies are advantageous.</li><li><strong>Work Arrangement:</strong> Openness to work onsite in Paris, France, 4 days p