ng-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mlabs/lead-architect-digital-assets-paris-298405","tags":["EUX"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1792221621},{"slug":"software-hardware-integration-qa-engineer-massy-396697","company_name":"Quandela","title":"Software & Hardware Integration QA Engineer","description":"<p>Quandela is a global leader in quantum computing, designing, building, and delivering cutting-edge quantum solutions for research and industry. Its offerings include the most energy-efficient quantum computers for data centers, full-stack quantum computing solutions accessible via the cloud, and algorithm access services for academic and industrial customers. Following a pragmatic, step-by-step roadmap, Quandela has been deploying industrial-grade systems since 2023 while developing future generations of fault-tolerant quantum computers capable of scaling through the integration of thousands of photonic components. Quandela is committed to making quantum computing accessible to all in order to address the most complex industrial and societal challenges.</p><p><strong>Join Us at the Forefront of Quantum Computing Innovation 🚀&nbsp;</strong></p><p></p><p>Your role</p><h3>Your Role</h3><p>As a <strong>Software &amp; Hardware Integration QA Engineer</strong>, you will play a key role in ensuring the quality and reliability of Quandela’s quantum computing systems.</p><p>Your main focus will be on validating the integration between software and physical hardware: ensuring that our software interfaces correctly control, communicate with, and monitor equipment such as photon sources, laser control systems and other optical and electronic components.</p><p>You will design and automate integration and end-to-end testing, while helping structure robust validation processes as Quandela moves from low-volume, highly complex systems toward more scalable and repeatable production.</p><p>Working closely with software, hardware, systems and industrialization teams, you will contribute to building the testing methods, tools, documentation and quality standards required for this next stage of growth.</p><p></p><h3><strong>Your Key Responsibilities&nbsp;</strong></h3><ul><li>Define QA plans, test strategies, acceptance criteria and validation procedures for software/hardware integrated systems.</li><li>Design and execute functional, integration, system, regression and robustness tests on real equipment.</li><li>Build automated <strong>software-to-hardware integration and end-to-end tests</strong>.</li><li>Validate complete workflows, from software interfaces and commands to their execution by physical equipment.</li><li>Test and troubleshoot communication between software and hardware through interfaces and protocols such as <strong>Ethernet and serial connections</strong>.</li><li>Develop and maintain automated tests and test tools using <strong>Python</strong> and testing frameworks such as <strong>Behave</strong>, with reporting tools such as <strong>Allure</strong>.</li><li>Integrate automated testing into continuous integration pipelines where relevant.</li><li>Reproduce, document and track defects through resolution, verify fixes and assess regression risks.</li><li>Maintain clear traceability between requirements, test cases, defects and test results.</li><li>Produce test reports, quality metrics and technical documentation to support validation and release decisions.</li><li>Help define and continuously improve <strong>industrial-grade validation processes</strong>, test procedures and quality practices.</li><li>Build reusable and scalable testing methods to support the progressive ramp-up of Quandela’s quantum computing systems.</li><li>Collaborate closely with software, hardware, systems and industrialization engineers to improve overall product quality.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Around <strong>5 years of experience</strong> in software QA, system validation, verification &amp; validation, test engineering or a similar role.</li><li>Hands-on experience testing <strong>systems combining software and hardware</strong>.</li><li>Strong experience with <strong>test automation and scripting</strong>, ideally using Python.</li><li>Ability to understand, test and troubleshoot hardware/software interactions and communication protocols.</li><li>Experience with automated testing frameworks and reporting tools; experience with <strong>Behave and/or Allure</strong> is a plus.</li><li>Experience working within structured software development and QA processes, including requirements traceability, documented testing, defect management and release validation.</li><li>An interest in building and improving testing processes, rather than only executing existing test plans.</li><li>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail.</li><li>Ability to produce clear and structured technical documentation.</li><li>Good communication skills and the ability to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams.</li><li>Professional proficiency in <strong>English</strong>, both written and spoken.</li></ul><p>Experience in industrial environments such as <strong>robotics, embedded systems, scientific instrumentation, photonics, semiconductor equipment, medical devices, automotive, aerospace or other complex hardware/software systems</strong> would be particularly relevant.</p><p>Knowledge of quality standards such as <strong>IEC 61508 or ISO 9001</strong> would be appreciated but is not mandatory.</p><p>An engineering degree or equivalent technical background is welcome, but we value relevant hands-on experience and demonstrated technical skills above all.</p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive salary, flexible based on your experience </li></ul><ul><li>Profit-sharing &amp; company savings plan</li><li>100% health coverage (Alan)</li><li>50% transport reimbursement or sustainable mobility bonus</li><li>Meal vouchers (Swile), Gymlib fitness support</li><li>Childcare assistance &amp; referral bonuses (€1,000–€2,000)</li></ul><p></p><h3>What we offer: </h3><ul><li>A meaningful role with real ownership, from day one</li><li>A team eager to collaborate and grow with you</li><li>A hybrid work model (3 days/week onsite in Massy, 1 day in Paris, 1 to 2 days remotely)</li><li>Daily exposure to the entire quantum stack — from high-level APIs to low-level firmware, and everything in between.<br> </li></ul><h3><strong>Process </strong></h3><ul><li>Talent Acquisition Interview (30' - 45')</li><li>Hiring Manager Interview (45')</li><li>Use Case (a live use case or one to be prepared at home and presented afterward)</li><li>Meeting with the teams </li><li>2 reference check</li><li>Offer </li></ul><p><em>(This process is provided for guidance only and may evolve depending on the roles)</em></p><p></p><p>At Quandela, we believe that the strength of our team is the plurality of experiences, perspectives, and journeys. We are committed to building a respectful, inclusive, and welcoming work environment. All applications are welcome.&nbsp;</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/quandela/software-hardware-integration-qa-engineer-massy-396697","tags":["Engineering","Computer Hardware","IT & Software"],"job_types":["Full time","associate"],"location":"Massy, France","created_at":1792221617},{"slug":"cloud-devops-engineer-massy-321786","company_name":"Quandela","title":"Cloud DevOps Engineer","description":"<p>Quandela is a global leader in quantum computing, designing, building, and delivering cutting-edge quantum solutions for research and industry. Its offerings include the most energy-efficient quantum computers for data centers, full-stack quantum computing solutions accessible via the cloud, and algorithm access services for academic and industrial customers. Following a pragmatic, step-by-step roadmap, Quandela has been deploying industrial-grade systems since 2023 while developing future generations of fault-tolerant quantum computers capable of scaling through the integration of thousands of photonic components. Quandela is committed to making quantum computing accessible to all in order to address the most complex industrial and societal challenges.</p><p><strong>Join Us at the Forefront of Quantum Computing Innovation 🚀&nbsp;</strong></p><p></p><p>Your role</p><p>As a <strong>Cloud DevOps Engineer</strong>, you will contribute to the infrastructure powering Quandela's cloud and software platforms.</p><p>Working closely with our software and infrastructure teams, you will design, deploy and operate our infrastructure across <strong>multiple cloud environments</strong>, with a strong focus on <strong>Infrastructure as Code, automation, reliability and scalability</strong>.</p><p>You will contribute both to day-to-day operations and to the continuous evolution of our cloud architecture and DevOps practices.</p><p></p><h3><strong>Your Key Responsibilities&nbsp;</strong></h3><ul><ul><li>Design, deploy and maintain robust, scalable and secure infrastructure across multiple cloud environments.</li><li>Provision and manage cloud infrastructure through <strong>Infrastructure as Code, primarily using Terraform</strong>.</li><li>Build and improve CI/CD pipelines supporting our applications and services.</li><li>Deploy and operate containerized workloads using Docker/Podman and Kubernetes.</li><li>Automate infrastructure configuration and operational tasks using tools such as Ansible, Python and Bash.</li><li>Monitor infrastructure and applications to ensure availability, reliability and performance.</li><li>Implement networking and security best practices across cloud environments.</li><li>Troubleshoot infrastructure, deployment and application issues in collaboration with development teams.</li><li>Improve observability, automation and operational processes.</li><li>Optimize infrastructure usage and cloud resources.</li><li>Contribute to architectural decisions and the continuous improvement of our cloud platform.</li></ul></ul><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p>You have hands-on experience as a <strong>Cloud, DevOps, Platform or Infrastructure Engineer</strong>, with a strong understanding of cloud infrastructure and automation.</p><p>You are comfortable managing infrastructure through code and working across cloud, containers, networking and software deployment.</p><p>You bring experience with:</p><ul><li><strong>Terraform and Infrastructure as Code practices.</strong></li><li>Cloud infrastructure and cloud providers.</li><li>Linux environments and system administration.</li><li>Containers and orchestration technologies such as <strong>Docker, Podman and Kubernetes</strong>.</li><li>CI/CD environments, ideally <strong>GitLab CI/CD</strong>.</li><li>Configuration management tools such as <strong>Ansible</strong>.</li><li>Scripting and automation with <strong>Python and/or Bash</strong>.</li><li>Networking and security principles in cloud environments.</li><li>Monitoring, troubleshooting and operating production infrastructure.</li></ul><p>Experience with <strong>OpenStack</strong> would be a plus.</p><p>You are comfortable working in English and enjoy collaborating with international and multidisciplinary teams.</p><p></p><p>Qualifications</p><ul><li>Master's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or a related field.</li><li>Previous professional experience, ideally 3+ years of experience in Cloud, DevOps, Platform Engineering, SRE or a related infrastructure role.</li><li>Professional working proficiency in English.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive salary, flexible based on your experience </li></ul><ul><li>Profit-sharing &amp; company savings plan</li><li>100% health coverage (Alan)</li><li>50% transport reimbursement or sustainable mobility bonus</li><li>Meal vouchers (Swile), Gymlib fitness support</li><li>Childcare assistance &amp; referral bonuses (€1,000–€2,000)</li></ul><p></p><h3>What we offer: </h3><ul><li>A meaningful role with real ownership, from day one</li><li>A team eager to collaborate and grow with you</li><li>Daily exposure to the entire quantum stack — from high-level APIs to low-level firmware, and everything in between.<br> </li></ul><h3><strong>Process </strong></h3><ul><li>Talent Acquisition Interview (30' - 45')</li><li>Hiring Manager Interview (45')</li><li>Use Case (a live use case or one to be prepared at home and presented afterward)</li><li>Meeting with the teams </li><li>2 reference check</li><li>Offer </li></ul><p><em>(This process is provided for guidance only and may evolve depending on the roles)</em></p><p></p><p>At Quandela, we believe that the strength of our team is the plurality of experiences, perspectives, and journeys. We are committed to building a respectful, inclusive, and welcoming work environment. All applications are welcome.&nbsp;</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/quandela/cloud-devops-engineer-massy-321786","tags":["Computer Hardware"],"job_types":[],"location":"Massy, France","created_at":1792221617},{"slug":"remote-lead-solutions-engineer-france-354209","company_name":"Exotec","title":"Lead Solutions Engineer","description":"<p>At Exotec, we are at the forefront of technological excellence in order to redefine the relationship between humans and robots. Our solutions are contributing to the success of some of the largest brands in retail and e-Commerce by revolutionizing the way they fulfill their orders to the end consumers, all while mitigating labor constraints and increasing workplace safety.</p><p>Through the unification of artificial intelligence and high-performance hardware, our robotic solutions are now deployed across the globe and our exponential growth has led us to become the first industrial unicorn in France.</p><p>Working at Exotec is an exciting opportunity to give purpose to your skills. Learn and grow with over 1000 ExoPeople around the world to help turn your ideas into a reality.</p><p><strong>The robotics revolution is just the beginning at Exotec. Will you be part of it?</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>As Lead Solutions Engineer, in charge of France within the Solutions Engineering Western Europe team, you will:</strong></p><ul><li>Lead the design of high-impact, complex solutions, ensuring robustness from concept to delivery (costing, risk mitigation, scalability)</li><li>Shape customers’ logistics strategies by challenging the status quo and proposing innovative, value-driven alternatives</li><li>Translate customer challenges into compelling technical sales strategies that drive winning outcomes</li><li>Influence key stakeholders by clearly articulating the value of Exotec solutions and building strong technical alignment</li><li>Collaborate with partners and suppliers to co-create best-in-class solutions, challenging them to reach the highest standards</li><li>Drive technical excellence by embedding Exotec methodologies and supporting Sales through complex project leadership</li><li>Act as a recognized expert in a key technical domain, elevating team capabilities and decision-making</li><li>Empower teams and partners by creating impactful training content and sharing best practices</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Travel is required: twice a month to visit our clients, once a month to our headquarters near Lille.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Experience selling complex solutions in a warehouse automation environment</li><li>Engineering or supply chain background, with a strong track record in complex solution design</li><li>Proven experience in engaging with demanding customers in a pre-sales or solution-driven environment</li><li>Strong business acumen combined with deep technical expertise</li><li>Ability to influence, convince and navigate complex stakeholder environments</li><li>Natural leadership, with a drive to mentor and elevate others</li><li>Fluent French and English, comfortable operating in an international context.</li></ul><p></p><p>Exotec is an equal opportunity employer and all applicants will be considered without regard to race, religion, color, sex, gender, sexual orientation, pregnancy, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military or veteran status, genetic information, marital status, ethnicity, or any other protected classification, in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. We provide an inclusive work environment that respects all differences.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/exotec/remote-lead-solutions-engineer-france-354209","tags":["Sales","Logistics and Supply Chain","Marketing & Sales","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"France","created_at":1792221614},{"slug":"senior-manager-product-design-security-paris-414722","company_name":"Datadog","title":"Senior Manager, Product Design - Security","description":"&lt;p&gt;The Datadog Security design team (K9 Design, as we lovingly call it) is hiring a senior product design manager to lead design across our security products. This is a chance to shape an industry-leading experience for a new kind of Datadog user: security practitioners who need to catch threats where they start, stop them when they land, and shut down exposures before they turn into something worse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead a team of designers at various stages of their careers across cloud, code and data security, turning an overwhelming amount of signal into something a security team can act on. The goal: build the security product people want to spend their day in. You&#39;ll own the design, push for excellence, and partner closely with Product and Engineering leadership to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design direction across your team&#39;s products, and hold the bar for design excellence end to end: interactions, visual detail, consistency and cohesion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re in the work. Run critiques, give direct and useful feedback, and push the team toward bolder, more opinionated solutions rather than safe ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and grow designers across our Paris, Madrid and New York offices, helping each of them do the best work of their careers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define a security design system built on top of Datadog&#39;s existing components, with the security practitioner&#39;s workflows in mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering leaders to evolve cross-platform thinking, shape roadmaps, and to set how the three disciplines work together day to day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take accountability for the product and business outcomes your team&#39;s design work influences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring AI fluency to how your team works, from how design gets explored and validated to how it gets shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in design, including experience leading and growing high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A design leader first: a user advocate with a sharp eye for detail, strong taste and the willingness to get into the work and give direct feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leveling up a team&#39;s output, with before-and-after examples of how your leadership transformed the design of a product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve led complex products or features: a zero-to-one launch, a reimagining of something established, or both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator who collaborates effectively with executive and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to demonstrate AI fluency, either in your own work or in how you&#39;ve led teams through it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating the technical complexity of modern software development and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally&lt;/strong&gt;: security domain experience, or a portfolio of information-dense, data-rich interfaces. Industry-leading work on complex B2B, B2C or consumer products counts for just as much here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits and Growth&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product training to develop an in-depth understanding of our product and space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous career development and pathing opportunities for internal mobility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intradepartmental mentor and buddy program for in-house networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive company culture, ability to join our Community Guilds (Datadog employee resource groups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire stock equity (RSUs) and employee stock purchase plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free, global mental health benefits for employees and dependents age 6+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous global benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading observability and security platform for the AI era, providing businesses with unified visibility across the technology stack to manage complexity at scale. It brings applications, infrastructure, data, models, and security into one place, using AI to detect and resolve issues before they impact customers. Trusted globally by Fortune 500 companies and high-growth AI leaders, Datadog enables businesses to move faster with clarity and confidence. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
