ip integrations and data products on Tetra OS that serve scientific teams across the globe. You will also mentor other scientific data engineers, lead internal design sessions, and partner with Product Managers and Solution Architects to turn customer, product, and engineering objectives into commercialized solutions.</p><p></p><ul><li>Act as a forward deployed engineer for a portfolio of biotech, pharmaceutical, and scientific customers. Own the technical relationship, understand their scientific workflows, and deliver solutions that move their programs forward.</li><li>Drive AI agents to design and build bidirectional integrations between Tetra OS and customer systems such as ELN, LIMS, MES, and process historians, including serverless push and pull pipelines, stateful connectors, and full stack data applications in Python and TypeScript.</li><li>Drive AI agents to design and build comprehensive data schemas and parsers for scientific data from R&amp;D lab instruments, manufacturing, CRO, CDMO, ELN, and LIMS sources, across formats such as .xlsx, .pdf, .txt, .raw, .fid, and many other vendor binaries.</li><li>Deploy and test solutions in customer environments, including cloud, on-premises, and hybrid networks, and troubleshoot across the full stack when something breaks.</li><li>Create and enforce designs with quality backed by comprehensive test automation to prove expected behaviors.</li><li>Lead process and technology improvements supporting product quality, developer experience, and platform capabilities.</li><li>Provide mentorship to junior scientific data engineers and show leadership on every front.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p>We hire Sciborg team members with potential, passion, and values alignment, not just a checklist of requirements. If you have related skills and a desire to learn, we want to hear from you.</p><ul><ul><li>Demonstrated history building and delivering data products, integrations, and scientific applicat