<li>Prepare German VAT filings, including Umsatzsteuervoranmeldung and Zusammenfassende Meldung, and support payroll tax declarations (Lohnsteuer-Anmeldung) in collaboration with external payroll providers and tax advisors.</li>
<li>Assist with the preparation of annual financial statements in accordance with German Commercial Code (HGB) requirements, as well as statutory audits and tax filings.</li>
<li>Maintain and strengthen internal financial controls, accounting procedures, and compliance practices.</li>
<li>Review and improve existing accounting processes, resolve outstanding items, clean up historical ledger discrepancies, and establish more efficient financial workflows.</li>
<li>Prepare financial KPIs and management reports, validating data accuracy and consistency before submission.</li>
<li>Support monthly variance analysis by comparing actual results against budgets and forecasts, investigating discrepancies, and providing relevant insights.</li>
<li>Collaborate with the wider finance team on daily accounting operations, reporting activities, process improvements, and special projects.</li>

<h2>Requirements:</h2>

<li>At least 3 years of professional accounting experience, including hands-on responsibility for German accounting practices under HGB and German tax requirements.</li>
<li>Experience in the software, technology, or Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) industry.</li>
<li>Solid understanding of accrual accounting, financial reconciliations, journal entries, closing procedures, and financial reporting.</li>
<li>Practical knowledge of German VAT requirements and familiarity with payroll tax declarations and statutory reporting obligations.</li>
<li>Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, with the ability to work confidently with financial data and accounting reports.</li>
<li>Experience with NetSuite or similar accounting and enterprise resource planning systems is an advantage.</li>
<li>Experience managing multiple legal entities or multi-currency accounting is a plus.</li>
<li>A professional qualification in accounting, bookkeeping, or a related discipline is desirable.</li>
<li>Strong attention to detail, accuracy, and reliability, with a commitment to maintaining high standards in financial documentation and reporting.</li>
<li>A proactive, problem-solving mindset and willingness to resolve historical accounting issues, organize incomplete records, and improve existing processes.</li>
<li>Ability to work independently, manage priorities effectively, and take ownership of responsibilities in a fully remote environment.</li>
<li>Strong teamwork and communication skills, including the ability to collaborate proactively with colleagues, external advisors, and service providers across remote teams.</li>
<li>Curiosity, adaptability, and a willingness to learn new systems, expand responsibilities, and develop professionally over time.</li>
<li>Fluency in both German and English, written and spoken.</li>
<li>Residence in Europe and legal authorization to work in the country of residence. Being based in or near Berlin is an advantage.</li>

