&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/auterion/fullstack-web-developer-zurich-434693","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792065314},{"slug":"leiter-automatisierungstechnik-siemens-tia-nyon-453150","company_name":"Eh Group","title":"Leiter Automatisierungstechnik Siemens TIA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About EH Group Engineering</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">EHG is developing cutting-edge fuel cell technology for heavy duty mobility and large-scale stationary power applications. Our uniquely redesigned product is a significantly more compact fuel cell with high power density and lower costs of production. Faced with the challenges of climate change and the transition to a decentralised energy system, EHG seeks to provide high performance and cost-effective fuel cell solutions to our clients and partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To help bring this vision to life, we are looking for a Senior Control Engineer to coordinate our efforts in designing control strategies for containerized systems integrating our fuel cell technology alongside equipment such as gas reformers, batteries, and climate control units. You will coordinate the control team and play a key role in shaping how these complex, multi-equipment systems operate safely and efficiently in the field. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Based in the US? You’re welcome to apply.</strong> This is an on-site role in Nyon, Switzerland. We ask that you relocate within 3 months of starting, and we’ll support 