a.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nonconformance and corrective action across both sites</strong>, including NCR and CAPA processes and structured problem solving, with findings at one site systematically applied at the other.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Traceability and product records</strong> — a common lot genealogy model from raw material through stack serial to delivered system, and the test and inspection data that supports warranty, certification, and customer acceptance, held consistently across both entities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Certification across regions</strong>, working with external certification partners on the standards applicable to stationary hydrogen power systems in Europe and the US, authority having jurisdiction approvals, and marine classification where relevant.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality culture on both floors</strong>, including operator training, work instruction discipline, and establishing the habits in Houston that are already proven in Nyon, as US headcount grows quickly.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building the US quality capability</strong>, defining what needs to sit on the ground in Houston versus what is run centrally from Nyon, and recruiting into it as volumes grow.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning quality across more than one manufacturing site, ideally in more than one country, with a demonstrated ability to hold two sites to genuinely the same standard from a distance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establishing or substantially rebuilding a quality function, including authoring a quality management system rather than administering an existing one.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on in-process and incoming quality in a production setting, with real familiarity with control plans, inspection methods, measurement systems, and process capability.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supplier quality experience, including auditing suppliers and holding them to standard.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured problem solving and root cause analysis, with a track record of permanently closing out recurring defects.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of product certification processes and the evidence they require, ideally in energy, power equipment, or another regulated product category. Exposure to both European and US regimes is a strong advantage.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgment to know which controls are essential at low volume and which can wait, and the confidence to hold a quality position under schedule pressure.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working across time zones and influencing a site you are not physically based at, including building quality capability remotely.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Especially compelling</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fuel cell, battery cell, or similar electrochemical assembly experience.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with cleanliness-critical or contamination-sensitive assembly processes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting a technology transfer between sites or countries, and establishing quality at the receiving end.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience qualifying and auditing contract manufacturers or system integrators.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup or scale-up experience as an early hire during hyper-growth.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working between Europe and the US, and with US codes and certification practice in particular. French is useful but not required.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and meaningful equity, calibrated to the market and discussed directly with you.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relocation support to Nyon, Switzerland.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to build EHG's global quality function during a defining phase of hyper-growth.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: Swiss work authorization or eligibility is required for this role, along with the ability to travel to the United States.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">EH Group is an equal opportunity employer. We value a diverse workforce and an inclusive culture, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/eh-group/global-quality-manager-fuel-cell-manufacturing-nyon-409021","tags":["Production"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nyon","created_at":1792064442},{"slug":"robotics-integration-engineer-zurich-16755","company_name":"Enactintelligence","title":"Robotics Integration Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Enact</strong><br /><br />The next defining technological breakthrough will be in the physical world. We stand at a historical inflection point: bringing general-purpose intelligence into robotics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Enact we rethink the entire robotic tech stack from model architectures and data pipelines, to the actuators and sensors that feed the model. Pushing beyond pure vision and language approaches, we build a proprioceptive nerve system, and the cortex that makes sense of it, to solve dexterity through whole-body force-awareness and deploy robots for thousands of tasks in industry and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are shaping a company where brilliant and unconventional people thrive together on solving the hardest challenges of our time. We are truth seekers. We reason from first principles, test our beliefs against reality, and trust that the best ideas can come from anyone.  We move fast. We care deeply about our work and colleagues and are driven by passion to change the status quo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this resonates, we're excited to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In This Role You Will</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design, integrate and test the electromechanical systems at the core of our dexterous robots: </strong>actuator modules, joints, and end-effectors, sensors, PCBs, and cable harnesses into compact, reliable units for high-DoF robotics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring hardware to life: </strong>lead system assembly &amp; bring-up, debug across mechanics, electronics, and firmware, and work with controls &amp; AI