ermining how we assemble them: the processes, the fixtures, the production space itself, getting the very best out of our Amsterdam facilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more context on building hardware at Monumental, read Niall’s Substack: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://open.substack.com/pub/buildmonumental/p/i-quit-my-job-and-moved-country-to?r=68ngjs&amp;utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&amp;utm_medium=post%20viewer">I quit my job and moved country to make robots that will fix Europe’s housing crisis.</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bottom line, you'll own increasing our quarterly production from 30 sets of robot systems to 100 within a year. This is a challenge. You'll be building the production capabilities at Monumental rather than inheriting them, and you'll do it alongside engineers and technicians who care a great deal about getting this right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take prototypes through to production-ready modules. Find and address design flaws, validate improvements, and push these modules to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assembling modules, understand the friction slowing production, and address issues yourself along with the hardware team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop fixtures, jigs and light automation solutions to support module assembly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find production processes that bring minimal value when done in-house. Work with external suppliers to outsource them, while maintaining production quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce drawings, assembly instructions and quality checks to make sure our modules are integrated together and our robots are brought up with no errors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Industry experience, ideally in a VC-backed start-up, transitioning products from prototype to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on, analytical mindset: skilled at building assemblies, running studies, analysing data, solving production and quality issues, and collaborating with technicians to implement and validate improvements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in mechanical assembly (press fits, fastener selection, harness, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of GD&amp;T and producing 3D and 2D drawings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating structured process documentation (work instructions, SOPs, quality checklists)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good communication skills in English, both written and spoken</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BSc in Mechanical, Electrical, Manufacturing or Industrial Engineering, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with robotics or complex electromechanical systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ERP tools (Odoo or similar)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Monumental?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Monumental means being at the forefront of a movement aimed at making significant strides in the construction industry. Here, your work has the potential to impact not just the company but the future of how we build. If you're driven by innovation, eager to tackle complex challenges, and ready to make a tangible difference, we want to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">For open applications (where you don’t see an exact role match), 