he founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2><strong>The Problem You'll Solve</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prosus is building an AI-first future across a global portfolio that spans food delivery, e-commerce, fintech, and education. We invest over $100 million annually in AI, run 800+ models in production, and have deployed Toqan — our internal platform for building, testing, and deploying GenAI and agentic workflows — across the organisation. The scale of ambition is real; the challenge now is focus, coherence, and velocity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Group Product Manager for our AI Platform, you will own the multi-year product strategy for the platform that underpins every AI initiative across Prosus. This means defining and sequencing the roadmap for agent infrastructure, evaluation frameworks, model deployment pipelines, and the shared capabilities that internal teams — from applied science to application engineering — rely on to build and ship AI products. You will balance long-term platform investments against the immediate, high-impact needs of teams across the portfolio who are racing to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead and mentor a team of product managers, instilling product discipline and building the PM talent pipeline that scales with the platform. You will partner closely with engineering and applied science leadership to shape the technical strategy — making the hard trade-offs between model performance, latency, cost, and reliability that determine what we can promise the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And you will be the connective tissue: the person who turns ambiguous, fast-moving business needs into clear requirements, who aligns stakeholders across functions and geographies, and who ensures that what we build is not just technically impressive but adopted, trusted, and measurably impactful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a senior product leader who has lived through the messy reality of building platform products for internal teams — and loved it. You measure your success not by features shipped but by the velocity and quality of the teams who build on top of your platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are deeply technical. You can engage substantively with engineering and applied science teams on model lifecycle, MLOps, evaluation frameworks, and infrastructure trade-offs — not as a bystander, but as a thought partner. You understand agentic architectures, LLM capabilities and limitations, and the operational realities of running AI in production at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a people leader. You have managed and mentored product managers, and you take genuine pride in their growth. You set strategic direction, coordinate overlapping roadmaps into a coherent plan, and create the clarity that lets your team operate with autonomy and purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive in ambiguity. You have worked in fast-paced, high-scale environments where priorities shift and the path forward is not always clear. You do not wait for perfect information — you run rapid experiments, test hypotheses, and let data and user feedback guide the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a communicator. You can simplify complex technical concepts for executive leadership one hour and dig into detailed requirements with an engineering team the next. You build trust across functions and geographies, and you are as comfortable pushing back as you are building consensus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are customer-obsessed — even when your customers are internal teams. You connect frequently with the people who use your platform, validate solutions through product discovery, and treat adoption as a first-class metric.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years in product management, with at least 3–5 years in formal people-management roles leading a team of product managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success owning platform-level or infrastructure products used by internal teams — ideally including AI/ML platform capabilities, MLOps tooling, or developer-facing services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with generative AI, LLMs, and the model lifecycle (training, fine-tuning, evaluation, deployment, and monitoring) in production environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of defining and executing multi-year product strategies in fast-moving, high-scale environments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Depth</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to engage substantively with engineering and applied science teams on architectural decisions, infrastructure trade-offs, and AI system design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with agentic workflows, agent frameworks, and the operational patterns that make AI agents reliable at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong data-driven decision-making: comfortable with analytics tooling, A/B testing, defining and tracking KPIs, and using metrics to measure adoption, accuracy, latency, and ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with modern product and engineering tooling (e.g., Databricks, Jira, Confluence, Figma) and agile methodologies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership &amp; Influence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to mentor and grow product managers, instilling PM best practices and building talent pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholder management across functions and geographies — aligning engineering, applied science, business teams, and executive leadership around a shared roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias toward ownership: you take accountability for outcomes, protect your engineers' focus, and course-correct execution without waiting to be asked.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-first: you translate needs into technical requirements, push back when scope dilutes value, and advocate relentlessly for the people who use your platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity: you structure complex problems, propose pilots to validate direction, and create clarity for new and evolving teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI intuition: you stay current on models, frameworks, and evaluation methods — not as a researcher, but with the hands-on curiosity of a builder.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/group-product-manager-amsterdam-138407","tags":["AI & ML"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792204835},{"slug":"project-manager-mid-alkmaar-106567","company_name":"Wearebeyondsports","title":"Project Manager (mid)","description":"<h1>Project Manager</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Alkmaar, Netherlands<br /><strong>Working Arrangement:</strong> 5 Days Onsite, Alkmaar Office</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Join Our Team as a Project Manager at Beyond Sports</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re someone who thrives on bringing people, technology, and clients together, enjoys taking ownership of projects from start to finish, and gets energy from delivering high-quality digital products, this could be the perfect opportunity for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, you’ll work on innovative consumer-facing products and experiences within the sports world, collaborating with multidisciplinary teams to turn ideas and client requirements into successful deliveries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What Your Day Will Look Like</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Project Manager within the Beyond Sports Delivery Team, you’ll be responsible for the end-to-end delivery of consumer-facing software projects, including websites, mobile applications, data visualizations, and other digital sports experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll take ownership of scoping, planning, budgeting, and project delivery, while making sure projects stay on track and meet the quality our clients and users expect. You’ll work closely with our Design, Engineering, and QA teams, facilitating collaboration and ensuring everyone has the clarity they need to deliver successfully.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll also be a key point of contact for our external clients. From translating customer requirements and feedback into clear scopes, functional requirements, and user stories to managing expectations, risks, and project progress, you’ll make sure communication stays clear throughout the entire project lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">When our products go live, you’ll be there too, acting as a central point of communication and helping coordinate and escalate where necessary during live events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Value</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, we value people who take ownership, communicate clearly, and are comfortable working in a fast-paced and collaborative environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Project Manager, you’ll need to be proactive and organised, while also being able to adapt your approach depending on the project, client, and team you’re working with. You should be comfortable managing several projects at once and confident bringing together different perspectives to keep everyone moving towards the same goal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for someone who understands the world of technology and software development and can comfortably translate between technical and non-technical stakeholders. Experience working with data-driven products or projects is particularly valuable for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While this role is based in Alkmaar, Netherlands, we believe in the power of in-person collaboration, so we expect you to be available for <strong>32–40 hours per week in the office</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Skills and Experience</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to tick every box, but here’s what we’re looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience managing <strong>software </strong>or <strong>digital </strong>projects from start to finish, ideally including consumer-facing products such as websites, mobile applications, or data visualization products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with project scoping, planning, budgeting, and resource coordination</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of software development processes and working with multidisciplinary teams across Design, Engineering, and QA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience translating customer requirements and feedback into clear scopes, functional requirements, and user stories</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong client and stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to act as the main point of contact throughout project delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills and the ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing project risks, issues, reporting, documentation, and delivery progress</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining quality and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive and solution-oriented approach to problem-solving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong collaboration and facilitation skills, with the ability to bring teams and stakeholders together around decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The confidence to negotiate, manage expectations, and resolve conflicts professionally when needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with project management and delivery tools such as <strong>Azure DevOps</strong> and <strong>Jira</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with modern AI tools such as Copilot and Claude</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of data or data-driven products is strongly preferred</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with tools such as <strong>Figma </strong>and <strong>Trello</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within the sports, media, broadcast, or technology industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting the delivery of live products or events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience identifying and implementing improvements to delivery processes and ways of working</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Ready to Make an Impact?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re ready to take ownership of exciting digital projects, work directly with clients, and bring together talented multidisciplinary teams to deliver innovative sports experiences, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, you won’t just be managing timelines and budgets. You’ll play an important role in turning ideas, technology, and sports data into experiences that reach fans around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Level Up Your Career at Beyond Sports?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-impact, fast-paced environment:</strong> Manage exciting projects at the intersection of sports, technology, and digital experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and responsibility:</strong> Take projects from initial scope and planning all the way through to successful delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional collaboration:</strong> Work closely with Design, Engineering, QA, Business Development, and external clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovation:</strong> Be part of a company building new ways for fans and clients to experience sports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ongoing learning and development:</strong> Continue developing your project management, technical, and stakeholder management skills in a dynamic environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We also offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>25 days off per year</strong> – Because we know rest is important for performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension program</strong> – Secure your future</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lunch included</strong> – No need to worry about food logistics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Gym card</strong> – Stay sharp on and off the screen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fresh fruit, coffee, and Friday drinks</strong> – Fuel and fun throughout the week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bi-monthly outings</strong> – Team bonding and relaxation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Office games</strong> – FIFA, chess, and ping-pong breaks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to level up your career, apply now and help us deliver the future of sports tech!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wearebeyondsports/project-manager-mid-alkmaar-106567","tags":["Beyond Sports"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Alkmaar","created_at":1792204834},{"slug":"indomo-ai-marketing-transformation-internship-amsterdam-48897","company_name":"Ogilvy","title":"InDomo | AI & Marketing Transformation Internship","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy has been creating impact for brands through iconic, culture-changing, value-driving ideas since the company was founded by David Ogilvy more than 75 years ago. It builds on that rich legacy through Borderless Creativity—innovating at the intersection of intelligence, imagination and influence, with experts across advertising, sports &amp;amp; entertainment, PR &amp;amp; social, consulting, and health collaborating seamlessly across more than 120 offices spanning 90 countries. Ogilvy was named &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-brings-home-network-year-2026-cannes-lions-international-festival-creativity&quot;&gt;Network of the Year&lt;/a&gt; at the 2026 Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-tops-warc-effective-100-creative-100-4th-straight-year&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;e2c78315-ff05-4544-925f-9288319dea2c&quot;&gt;ranks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;as the #1 global agency network for creative excellence and effectiveness by WARC for the fourth consecutive year, signifying its ability to deliver creative solutions that drive unreasonable impact for clients and communities. Ogilvy is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ogilvy.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;39833259-880d-4fd8-930f-0d84b1c14850&quot;&gt;Ogilvy.com&lt;/a&gt;, and follow us on&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;735e393e-6e8a-4ca8-804a-74f1bd8166b6&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ogilvy&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d10960ce-761b-48c5-81d5-0a7c4cc6013a&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;92ffcb70-6ca7-4d9a-88d5-c130e36e6c4f&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;3bd2010d-00a2-401b-8cfb-7e8c24deac52&quot;&gt; Facebook.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&amp;nbsp;in a single company –&amp;nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&amp;nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;7f087527-f491-4cb6-a79d-3b4a67d1ec89&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About InDomo&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InDomo is a WPP company and the trusted transformation partner for multinationals ready to unlock rapid digital business growth. We work shoulder-to-shoulder with marketing leaders to build bespoke, in-house performance marketing capabilities that break down silos, put the consumer at the centre, and drive measurable commercial impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2026, our focus has sharpened around AI-powered marketing transformation. We help brands navigate the shift to an AI-driven world by designing new ways of working, deploying intelligent marketing agents, and leveraging WPP Open (WPP’s proprietary AI platform) to deliver breakthrough results. We are scaling our AI practice rapidly and looking for a sharp, motivated intern to join the team and contribute from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a coffee-and-PowerPoint internship. As our AI &amp;amp; Marketing Transformation Intern, you will be embedded in a small, high-impact team working at the intersection of strategy, technology, and execution. You’ll support real client engagements, help build AI-powered solutions, and contribute to shaping how some of the world’s biggest brands adopt AI in their marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be given real responsibility, direct access to senior team members, and the opportunity to develop skills that sit at the cutting edge of where marketing is heading. If you’re finishing a Master’s programme and want to hit the ground running in AI-driven marketing transformation, this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AI Agent Development Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the design, testing, and iteration of custom AI expert agents for enterprise marketing clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and refine AI-powered workflows using WPP Open and adjacent tooling, working alongside senior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and experiment with AI tools, techniques, and frameworks (such as prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, and API integrations) to support solution development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document agent performance, capture learnings, and contribute to our internal knowledge base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Workshops &amp;amp; Client Engagement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation and delivery of AI Discovery Workshops and transformation sessions for senior marketing leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop workshop materials, including diagnostic frameworks, interactive exercises, and output templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and contribute to client meetings, with the opportunity to present specific sections or findings as your confidence grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the delivery of internal training and enablement sessions on AI tools and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Go-to-Market &amp;amp; Research&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop pitch decks, case studies, proposals, and other sales collateral for new business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct competitive analysis and market research to keep our AI propositions sharp and well-positioned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the packaging and refinement of InDomo’s AI service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become proficient in WPP Open, exploring new features and capabilities and sharing findings with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of the rapidly evolving AI and marketing technology landscape, surfacing relevant tools, trends, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring fresh thinking. We value your perspective as someone close to the latest academic research and emerging ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing or recently completed a Master’s degree in Marketing, Business, Digital Strategy, Data Science, Computer Science, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine, demonstrable interest in AI and its application to marketing or business. You’ve explored AI tools beyond the basics and can talk about what you’ve learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and strategic thinking skills. You can take a complex topic, break it down, and communicate it clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator who is comfortable presenting ideas to a room, whether that’s a team meeting or a client session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and visual communication. You can structure a compelling deck or write a clear, persuasive brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mentality. You take initiative, work independently when needed, and don’t wait to be told what to do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for a full-time, 6-month internship based in Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong Pluses&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI tools in an academic or personal project context, such as building chatbots, experimenting with LLMs, using AI coding assistants, or working with APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with concepts like prompt engineering, large language models, retrieval-augmented generation, or agent architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship or work experience in marketing, consulting, or a technology-related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise platforms (e.g., CRM systems, marketing automation tools, or analytics platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Dutch and/or international market dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the WPP network, you’ll have access to a world-class professional environment and a comprehensive set of benefits:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real, meaningful work on live client engagements with some of the world’s biggest brands. No busywork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentorship from experienced AI and marketing transformation leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with WPP Open and cutting-edge AI tooling that most people only read about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive internship compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to WPP’s global learning resources and professional development programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Light, open-plan office space with roof terrace, on-site bar, and stunning views over central Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is based at WPP Amsteldok Amsterdam and requires 3–4 days of on-site work, with the flexibility to work remotely 1–2 days a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong foundation for a career in one of the fastest-growing areas in marketing. High-performing interns may be considered for permanent roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ogilvy, our people are at the heart of what we do: a creative agency that sparks game-changing ideas across culture and business through collaboration, integrity, and a celebration of self-expression.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in building powerful teams with purpose - and we relentlessly curate transformative initiatives that make our commitment to fairness, and equity a reality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ultimate mission is to leave a positive impact on the world, creating a better future for all, while supporting and uplifting the global communities we serve.&amp;nbsp; This is central to our mantra of Borderless Creativity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ogilvy is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any assistance seeking a job opportunity, or if you need reasonable accommodation with the application process, please contact us at ----- Please note that this contact is only for candidates who are requesting accommodation. Emails for other purposes, including application status requests, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/ogilvy/indomo-ai-marketing-transformation-internship-amsterdam-48897","tags":["Consulting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792194924},{"slug":"staff-forward-deployed-engineer-ai-native-software-development-amsterdam-326389","company_name":"jetbrains","title":"Staff Forward Deployed Engineer – AI-Native Software Development","description":"&lt;p&gt;At JetBrains, code is our passion. Ever since we started, back in 2000, we have strived to make the strongest, most effective developer tools on earth. By automating routine checks and corrections, our tools speed up production, freeing developers to grow, discover, and create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We just unveiled JetBrains Central,&amp;nbsp; a platform for agent-driven software development that connects tools, agents, and infrastructure. It enables automated AI workflows to run, be monitored, and be managed across teams – with clear visibility into results, costs, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JetBrains Central provides three core capabilities:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and control: &lt;/strong&gt;Policy enforcement, identity and access management, observability, auditability, and cost attribution for agent-driven work. Some of these functionalities are already available via the &lt;a href=&quot;http://console.jetbrains.cloud/&quot;&gt;JetBrains Central Console&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent execution infrastructure:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Cloud agent runtimes and computation provisioning that allow agents to run reliably across development environments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent optimization and context:&lt;/strong&gt; Shared semantic context across repositories and projects, enabling agents to access relevant knowledge, and task routing to the most appropriate models or tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inside the Professional Services department, we are building a team of Forward Deployed Engineers to help our customers adopt AI-native development with JetBrains Central and enable JetBrains consulting partners to transform their customers’ AI-native software development lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Forward Deployed Engineer, you will work directly with early adopter customers to deploy JetBrains Central platform into complex enterprise environments and help them move from experimental AI usage to governed, scalable AI-native development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted advisor to customer engineering teams and consulting partners, while also mentoring other Forward Deployed Engineers and helping with complex deployments. In this role, you will help establish best practices for enterprise AI adoption and influence how organizations implement AI-driven software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is often a strong fit for engineers who have previously served as Principal or Staff Engineers, Heads of Engineering, CTOs, or Solutions Architects and who enjoy working directly with customers while staying deeply involved with complex technical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines consulting, architecture, and hands-on engineering. Your work in the field will directly influence how our platform evolves and how enterprises adopt AI-driven development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the world’s most innovative companies — our client base includes 420 of the Fortune 500 — ensuring they maximize the value of their JetBrains investments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy JetBrains Central platform into enterprise development environments, CI/CD systems, and internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help organizations transition from ad-hoc AI experimentation to governed AI-native development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement enterprise AI governance, including security policies, access management, and data privacy controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable observability for AI-driven development to help organizations understand their AI usage and its impact on productivity, as well as their code-generation patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design sustainable AI adoption strategies, including usage controls and cost visibility across multiple model providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate our cloud-based agent execution layer, allowing AI agents to run securely and at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with JetBrains product teams to shape the platform based on real-world deployments and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create delivery frameworks and train JetBrains partners to deliver the desired scope of service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other Forward Deployed Engineers, sharing architectural expertise and helping to scale the team’s deployment practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultant at heart who can communicate effectively with both engineers and technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to see the whole picture of the software development lifecycle across developer tools, infrastructure, APIs, and cloud systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced at integrating complex software systems into enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about the future of AI agents and AI-native software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with early adopters and overcoming ambiguous technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated to mentor other engineers and contribute to building a new technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
