s &amp; Community Manager to turn that into a program that runs in several markets at the same time. You’ll plan and run our partner and owned events, and find new ways to grow Tebi through the hospitality community in each city, neighbourhood and market. You’ll work closely with our local sales teams so every event and partnership turns into real conversations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. One week you'll be hosting a merchant dinner in Milan, the next you'll be setting up a distributor breakfast in Amsterdam. You'll report to the Head of Marketing and work closely with our Marketing team to extend these programs to our channel ecosystem, plus align closely with the General Managers and Account Managers in each market.</p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run events across markets:</strong> Plan and deliver partner and owned events in 2–3 markets at a time, from intimate merchant dinners and industry breakfasts to city launches. You own the calendar, budget, venues, suppliers, guest lists and the plan for the night.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the playbook as you go:</strong> Turn each event into templates, checklists and supplier lists, so we can launch a city campaign in weeks, not months. Improve them after every event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build local partner networks:</strong> Find the people operators already trust: drinks distributors, wholesalers, food creators, hospitality associations, accountants and the advisers who help new venues open. Build partnerships that bring us introductions and referrals, not just logos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put our merchants front and center:</strong> Work with our best merchants as hosts and anchors, so prospects hear about Tebi from the people they respect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn connections into pipeline:</strong> Agree with local Sales and Account Management who to involve, how to follow up and who owns what conversations. Track every event in HubSpot from invite to demo to signed merchant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow Tebi through the community:</strong> Find new ways to reach operators through the people and places they already trust, in each city, neighborhood and across borders. Keep guests and partners engaged after events, so one introduction leads to the next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Open new community channels:</strong> Test new ways to grow through our close-knit industry, such as an affiliate or referral program for partners, sharing useful insights from our merchants, and showing up in the forums and groups where operators talk shop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Capture the stories:</strong> Work with our creative team and relevant freelancers to turn events and partner moments into social content, case studies and sales material.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we'll measure success:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events delivered each quarter across markets, on time and on budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demos, pipeline and new merchants from each event and partnership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductions, referrals and leads from partners, affiliates and community channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cost per demo compared with our other channels</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built something people show up for: an event series, a supper club, a community, a program. You can point to what it led to, not just how many people came</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feel at home in hospitality. You've worked in or around restaurants, bars or food and drink brands, and you're comfortable leading a room full of operators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are high agency. You own your calendar, your relationships and your results, and you don't wait to be told what to do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own playbook when there isn't one, and you enjoy doing the work as much as planning it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know the difference between a real community and a guest list</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">See growth opportunities beyond events, and are curious enough to test them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can run several markets at once without dropping details, and are happy to travel regularly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track what you do: comfortable with a CRM (HubSpot a plus), UTMs and simple reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speak fluent English. Dutch, German, Italian, Spanish or a Nordic language is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically this means 3–5 years in events, community, field marketing or partnerships, but we care more about what you've built than how long you've been doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role isn't for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather plan the program than run it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need a fixed playbook and a clear org chart to get going</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're not willing to roll up your sleeves on the night</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch Provided in Office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team building events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited time off</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><h3>How we use AI at Tebi</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/events-community-manager-amsterdam-496347","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792183219},{"slug":"director-product-physical-amsterdam-44643","company_name":"hellofresh","title":"Director, Product (physical) (f/m/x)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting Relationships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Primary Manager: &lt;/strong&gt;COO and Co-MD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Dotted Line: &lt;/strong&gt;CMO and Co-MD&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports: &lt;/strong&gt;~10 people spanning Culinary, Product Innovation, Product Strategy, Product Operations, and Product Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Factor is a healthy, ready-to-heat meal delivery service that has built a category-defining business in the US and Canada. Now we&#39;re building &lt;strong&gt;Factor in Europe&lt;/strong&gt; — and although we have strong blueprints from North America, we have the opportunity to leverage the very rich multi-cultural environment in Europe to tailor both our physical and digital products to five different markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our &lt;strong&gt;Director, Product&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the full product vision and execution for Factor Europe. You will lead a multi-layered team of ~10 people, sit on the Factor Europe leadership team, and maintain a close dotted-line relationship with our CMO to ensure product and marketing move as one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare kind of role: senior strategic ownership and real infrastructure, with the pace and ambition of an early-stage scale up. If you are a visionary builder who leads with curiosity, earns conviction through data, and holds your team to the same high standard you hold yourself — we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Lead and Develop a High-Performance Product Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Build, inspire, and manage a multi-disciplinary team — setting a clear vision, establishing the operating rhythms that allow the team to move fast, and investing in the people who will drive Factor Europe&#39;s next chapter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Own and Challenge the Product Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Define a clear and compelling vision for what Factor&#39;s physical product must become in Europe — grounded in customer insight, commercially rigorous, and differentiated enough to win. Develop a deep, independent point of view on where the North American model translates and where European markets demand something different.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Push the team and the business to think beyond the current roadmap — challenging assumptions, interrogating trade-offs, and ensuring we are always working on the highest-leverage version of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Act as the liaison to our global Digital Product team — representing Factor Europe&#39;s priorities in the feature roadmap and collaborating on shared global initiatives that benefit the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Drive Customer Retention and Commercial Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Own customer retention levers as your north star. Build a rigorous, evidence-based view of what drives it and rally the team around interventions that move the needle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Make product decisions with full awareness of their P&amp;amp;L implications. Take calculated risks, track outcomes honestly, and move quickly to learn and adjust when bets don&#39;t pay off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Build for Multiple European Markets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Lead our effort to find product-market fit across five distinct markets — understanding how consumer preferences vary by culture, and building a proposition that resonates locally while scaling efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Share learnings across geographies and partner with peers across the HelloFresh Group to continuously raise the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Support new channel strategies, understanding and adapting products for different customer bases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Align Product and Marketing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Work closely with the brand &amp;amp; marketing team to ensure product roadmap and marketing strategies are fully synchronised — so what we build, how we talk about it, and how we sell it form one coherent proposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Act as the product voice on the leadership team, articulating a compelling vision for where the product needs to go and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;A visionary leader who executes. &lt;/strong&gt;You set a compelling direction, bring your team with you, and roll up your sleeves to make it happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Customer-obsessed and analytically rigorous. &lt;/strong&gt;Sharp instincts backed by disciplined discovery. Comfortable querying your own data and stress-testing assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Commercially minded. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand how product decisions flow through to the P&amp;amp;L — and hold yourself accountable to outcomes, not just outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;A cross-functional influencer. &lt;/strong&gt;You build trust quickly, drive execution through others, and get the right priorities onto other teams&#39; roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Internationally curious. &lt;/strong&gt;You find the complexity of building for multiple European cultures energising, and you seek out the nuances that matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;An exceptional communicator. &lt;/strong&gt;You write and present with clarity and conviction — from strategy narratives to leadership updates to product briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Food and/or nutrition obsessed!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;8–10+ years in Product, Strategy, or a closely related commercial leadership role; 3+ years managing multi-disciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Technical toolkit: &lt;/strong&gt;Advanced Excel/Google Sheets; AI proficiency and curiosity required.&lt;/li&gt;
