&lt;p&gt;Want to help solve the world&#39;s toughest problems with data and AI? This is what we do every day at Databricks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks operates at the leading edge of the Data and AI space. Our customers turn to us to lead the accelerated innovation their businesses need to gain first-mover advantage in today&#39;s ultra-competitive landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a creative, delivery-oriented Named Account Executive to join the Healthcare and Life Science to maximise the phenomenal market opportunity that exists for Databricks in the Benelux Region. As an Account Executive, you know how to sell innovation and value to existing customers, identify new use cases and grow consumption and can guide deals forward to compress decision cycles. You love understanding a product in depth and are passionate about communicating its value to customers and partners. You will be offered huge potential for career progression with the pace of the team&#39;s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Sales Director for Healthcare and Life Science, Benelux.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will co-develop a business plan, with your team and ecosystem partners, that accelerates customer success to exceed quarterly/annual consumption and booking goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will lead your team, customers and partners to identify impactful data and AI use cases whilst proving out their value on the Databricks Data Intelligence platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will implement the data and AI transformation goals of your customer through a combination of strategic partnerships, well scoped professional services, training and targeted Executive engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will develop an understanding of technical product details and roadmap to build trust with executives and technical champions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exstensive experience selling complex solutions to Enterprise Customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have experience managing and leading complex, federated sales campaigns in major accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have experience working in Data, Cloud industries with some technical sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proof of exceeding sales quotas in high-growth Enterprise software companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have experience driving consumption and commit-based engagement models and strategies working with professional services and training teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have experience co-selling and scaling your business with Cloud Vendors (AWS, Azure and Google Cloud teams) and Global Solution Integrators (GSI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of building effective champions, collaborative teams and partnerships to support execution of your account / territory plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how to identify all key uses cases and buying centres in an opportunity to increase the impact of Databricks in an organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of following robust sales methodologies and process, e.g. account planning, MEDDPICC, Value Selling and accurate forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or relevant work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and in Dutch are required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/named-core-account-executive-health-insurance-amsterdam-241365","tags":["Enterprise Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792173335},{"slug":"lead-solutions-architect-generative-ai-emea-emerging-dnb-amsterdam-234185","company_name":"databricks","title":"Lead Solutions Architect - Generative AI (EMEA Emerging DNB)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQ ID: FEQ227R147&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Netherlands (Remote/Hybrid) - will require travel across Europe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiter: Dina Hussain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Solution Architect focused on Generative AI to support our &lt;strong&gt;EMEA Emerging Digital Natives and Startups &lt;/strong&gt;business unit — one of the fastest-moving, most technically ambitious patches in EMEA. Our customers are digital-native and cloud-native companies who build on the frontier: they adopt GenAI early, scale fast, and expect their technical partners to be as sharp as their own engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the go-to expert our Account Teams and customers turn to when a GenAI or LLM use case needs to move from an ambitious idea to a production-grade reality across our high-growth accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly technical, customer-facing individual contributor role for someone who lives at the frontier of applied GenAI. You will shape architectures, prove out the hard problems, challenge and influence customer roadmaps, and raise the GenAI capability of the entire EMEA Emerging DNB field organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the deep technical authority on Generative AI, LLMs, and applied machine learning for the EMEA Emerging DNB business unit, supporting the most strategic and complex customer engagements across our digital-native and born-in-the-cloud accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our EMEA Emerging DNB Solutions Architects, Solutions Engineers, and Account teams to scope, design, and de-risk GenAI use cases — from retrieval-augmented generation and agentic systems to fine-tuning and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build hands-on proofs of concept and reference implementations that operationalise large-scale LLM and deep learning workloads on Databricks (Mosaic AI, MLflow, Model Serving, Vector Search, Unity Catalog governance), tuned to the fast iteration cycles Emerging DNB customers expect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead fine-tuning and model-customisation engagements on open LLMs (e.g., Llama-family models), including judge-based and label-efficient evaluation approaches for domains where quality and safety are paramount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a bridge to Product and Engineering — channel field and customer feedback into the roadmap and represent the roadmap back to the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable and mentor the broader EMEA Emerging DNB Field Engineering team through workshops, reference architectures, and internal enablement, multiplying GenAI expertise across our ~70-person SA/SE organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Databricks externally as a technical thought leader — conference talks (e.g., Data + AI Summit), blogs, and customer executive briefings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the LLM landscape, including leading proprietary and open-source models and providers, with the ability to differentiate their capabilities, trade-offs, and suitability for different use cases, and to articulate a clear, informed point of view (POV) to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in the modern GenAI stack: LLM application patterns (RAG, agents, tool use), fine-tuning and model customization, prompt and evaluation engineering, and LLM guardrails/safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundations in machine learning and deep learning, including distributed training, GPU workloads, and the full MLOps lifecycle (tracking, registry, serving, monitoring).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and the ML ecosystem (PyTorch/Transformers, MLflow, Spark), and comfort building production-quality reference implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Databricks platform — or the ability to ramp on it quickly — including Mosaic AI, Model Serving, Vector Search, and Unity Catalog. Cloud experience across AWS, Azure, or GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and consultative skills: able to earn the trust of both hands-on engineers and senior technical executives, and to explain complex GenAI trade-offs clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of technical leadership and mentorship — someone who elevates the people around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating at the pace of digital-native and high-growth customers, where speed, iteration, and technical credibility win the deal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in the United Kingdom and able to work across EMEA time zones, with willingness to travel to customer sites within the region as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background helping digital-native customers build data and ML solutions (e.g., prior experience at a data/ML platform or consulting vendor) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public technical presence: conference speaking, published talks, blogs, or open-source contributions in the ML/GenAI space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain depth in a regulated or high-stakes industry (healthcare/life sciences, financial services) where model quality, evaluation, and safety are critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product and Engineering teams to influence roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on the hardest and most exciting GenAI problems our EMEA Emerging DNB customers have — companies building the future in real time — with the platform and the people to actually solve them, not just advise. You&#39;ll shape how one of EMEA&#39;s highest-growth business units adopts Generative AI, influence the direction of the product, and build a public profile as a recognised expert in the field. This is the role for a builder and a teacher, who wants their expertise to have outsized impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/lead-solutions-architect-generative-ai-emea-emerging-dnb-amsterdam-234185","tags":["Field Engineering - Other"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792173335},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-firefox-security-223417","company_name":"mozilla","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Firefox Security","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot; style=&quot;font-size: small;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Mozilla?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mozilla Corporation is the non-profit-backed technology company that has shaped the internet for the better over the last 25 years. We make pioneering brands like Firefox, the privacy-minded web browser. Now, with more than 225 million people around the world using our products each month, we’re shaping the next 25 years of technology and helping to reclaim an internet built for people, not companies. Our work focuses on diverse areas including AI, social media, security and more. And we’re doing this while never losing our focus on our core mission – to make the internet better for people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Mozilla Corporation is wholly owned by the non-profit 501(c) Mozilla Foundation. This means we aren’t beholden to any shareholders — only to our mission. Along with thousands of volunteer contributors and collaborators all over the world, Mozillians design, build and distribute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open-source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; software that enables people to enjoy the internet on their terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, build and implement security and hardening features for enterprise users:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Design, implement, test, and ship cutting-edge security features that strengthen Firefox’s security posture.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance Firefox’s security architecture across multiple operating systems: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contribute to and drive cutting-edge improvements to Firefox’s core security posture, by building privilege isolation and moving trust boundaries &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or Strengthen Firefox’s security architecture:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Improve Firefox’s core security mechanisms including cryptographic protocols, WebPKI, and security-sensitive web APIs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to our security initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Work across teams to investigate security issues, identify root causes, and deliver robust, maintainable fixes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve browser reliability and performance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Diagnose and resolve issues affecting stability, correctness, performance, and memory usage in a complex, multithreaded environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems programming experience and security knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; 3+ years of experience in low-level software engineering, strong proficiency in C and/or C++, and a solid understanding of security fundamentals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging and problem-solving skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Experience diagnosing and resolving issues in multithreaded, cross-platform native applications, including memory and performance challenges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web platform and modern systems experience: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) and interest or experience in Rust; ability to work effectively within large, complex, multi-language codebases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effective collaboration and communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Experience working with distributed teams and communicating technical ideas clearly in writing and conversation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous performance-based bonus plans to all eligible employees - we share in our success as one team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous retirement contributions with 100% immediate vesting (regardless of whether you contribute)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Quarterly all-company wellness days where everyone takes a pause together&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Country specific holidays plus a day off for your birthday&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;One-time home office stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Annual professional development budget&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Quarterly well-being stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Considerable paid parental leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee referral bonus program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Other benefits (life/AD&amp;amp;D, disability, EAP, etc. - varies by country)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mozilla&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mozilla exists to build the Internet as a public resource accessible to all because we believe that open and free is better than closed and controlled. When you work at Mozilla, you give yourself a chance to make a difference in the lives of Web users everywhere. And you give us a chance to make a difference in your life every single day. Join us to work on the Web as the platform and help create more opportunity and innovation for everyone online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mozilla understands that valuing diverse creative practices and forms of knowledge are crucial to and enrich the company’s core mission.&amp;nbsp; We encourage applications from everyone, including members of all equity-seeking communities, such as (but certainly not limited to) women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all sexual orientation&lt;span style=&quot;color: #003366;&quot;&gt;s, &lt;/span&gt;gender identities, and expressions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will ensure that qualified individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, as appropriate. Please contact us at &lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; ---------- to request accommodation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race (including hairstyle and texture), religion (including religious grooming and dress practices), gender, gender identity, gender expression, color, national origin, pregnancy, ancestry, domestic partner status, disability, sexual orientation, age, genetic predisposition, medical condition, marital status, citizenship status, military or veteran status, or any other basis covered by applicable laws.&amp;nbsp; Mozilla will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics or any other unlawful behavior, conduct, or purpose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Group: D&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: R3247&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Remote Netherlands&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€66.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€88.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mozilla/senior-software-engineer-firefox-security-223417","tags":["Firefox"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792173331},{"slug":"contract-software-engineer-dom-core-firefox-gecko-402762","company_name":"mozilla","title":"Contract Software Engineer - DOM Core Firefox/Gecko","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You will help the Firefox DOM Core team improve the health of the Session History area. You will write tests to improve the coverage; you will fix tests and/or problems to improve the Gecko correctness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Write Web-Platform tests to improve the coverage, and Gecko mochitests as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Fix the problems and pass the tests to improve the Gecko correctness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work through code review with the relevant Gecko module owners and iterate to landing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Definition of done&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Improved Session History test coverage and code correctness in Gecko, measured by passed test cases, allowing the team’s senior engineers to focus on security, performance and strategic projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Substantial experience in a browser-engine codebase or in automating for a browser-engine, ideally Firefox/Gecko.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Solid Javascript and applying that language skill to write automated tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proficiency in and experience developing software in C++.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong debugging skills in a mature larget codebase.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfort working in the open: public bugs, code review, and upstream landing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior contributions to Gecko or another major browser engine.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with web standards and Web Platform Tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mozilla/contract-software-engineer-dom-core-firefox-gecko-402762","tags":["Firefox"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792173331},{"slug":"office-manager-the-hague-225324","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Office manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re the first face people see when they walk into the Eye office, and a big reason they enjoy coming back. Guests, new colleagues, our SecOps analysts, the sales team, our founders: you know them all. As our Office Manager, you run the office in The Hague as if it were your own. You notice what needs doing, decide what matters most today, and get it done without waiting for someone to ask.<br /><br /><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the office running day to day. Make sure the  meeting rooms are set up, the kitchen is clean, the plants get water, and supplies and inventory are up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Welcome guests and new colleagues. For onboarding and offboarding, you have desks, access and welcome packs ready before day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work together with our event manager on our events from planning to the night itself: quarterly meetups, Thursday socials, the summer and Christmas parties. In the evening, you’re the host.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remember the moments that matter, like work anniversaries and gifts, so nobody slips through the cracks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow up when someone flags a problem, and stay on it until it’s actually fixed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with vendors, service providers and building management. You request quotes, compare them, order, and keep the office budget, invoices and expenses in check.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with our founders..</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think ahead about our offices. When we talk about opening in a new cities in Europe, you’re the one who works out what that takes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with our Office Assistant, and with our Office Manager in Germany.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in office management, front office, facilities or hospitality (hotels, events, restaurants)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take initiative. You set your own priorities and you’re happy to roll up your sleeves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re warm and approachable, and hosting people comes naturally to you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent Dutch and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like being where the people are: 4 days a week in our The Hague office , especially on Thursdays which is our official office day. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">32 - 40 hours availability. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real ownership. You decide how the office runs and how our events look.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A flat organisation where you work closely with our founders and connect with every team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company retreats abroad (Spain, Portugal, Italy…), quarterly meetups and Thursday socials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous time-off policy, including wellbeing and volunteering days</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Room to grow with us as the team and our number of offices grow<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye</strong><br />Eye Security provides cybersecurity and embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations across Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we’ve grown to over 170 employees and continue to expand internationally.<br /><br />We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team unites professionals from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds - all driven by one mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.<br /><br />At Eye, you’ll work on international projects, solving real-world challenges and helping to build a safer digital future for our clients.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/office-manager-the-hague-225324","tags":["Foundation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1792172419},{"slug":"channel-lead-benelux-nordics-the-hague-382829","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Channel Lead Benelux & Nordics (m/f/x)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role at Eye</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and Own MSP Partnerships: Manage the complete channel portfolio, recruit new partners, coach and develop your team, and scale operations to drive channel-led revenue growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic Partnership Management: Develop and execute partner business plans, design co-sell strategies, and create partner enablement programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve Channel Strategy: Redefine processes for partner recruitment, onboarding, and management, particularly in new markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with sales and marketing teams to ensure alignment on goals, execution plans, and resource allocation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performance Management: Monitor partner performance, implement enforcement mechanisms where needed, and continuously optimize partner productivity and profitability.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1+ years of leadership experience with 6+ years total in sales, business development, or</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">channel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record in partner management, channel development and/or new business sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cybersecurity, IT infrastructure, backup, disaster recovery, or cloud storage background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in Dutch language is required; German fluency is considered a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with ambiguity, are proactive and results driven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a team player and thrive in a scale-up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are willing to travel 50% of the time to visit partners or be present on events.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become part of one of the fastest growing cybersecurity scale-ups in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play a key role in building an innovative cybersecurity product line where we combine effective cybersecurity with cyber insurance on a global scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An attractive remuneration package and bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Car allowance and “floating holidays” for additional time off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MacBook or Windows Laptop and iPhone or Samsung company phone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong support for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular company-wide get-togethers, giving you the opportunity to collaborate in person and build strong team connections.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security provides cybersecurity and embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations across Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we’ve grown to over 170 employees and continue to expand internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team unites professionals from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds - all driven by one mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/channel-lead-benelux-nordics-the-hague-382829","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1792172419},{"slug":"total-rewards-people-business-partner-the-hague-403353","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Total Rewards & People Business Partner","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People Business Partner &amp; Total Rewards</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most People roles ask you to run processes someone else built. This one asks you to build them, and to own one of them outright: how Eye rewards and recognises its people. You’ll do that while partnering the part of the business where cybersecurity actually happens, with managers who are still learning to lead and specialists who know exactly how rare they are. If you need a mature organization around you to do your best work, this isn’t it. If you get energy from building one, keep reading.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role has two halves, and you’ll split your time roughly evenly between them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first half is Total Rewards. You’ll own compensation and benefits at Eye, including salary reviews, benchmarking, levelling, benefits and our equity program. There’s no finished framework waiting for you. You’ll shape it, make it hold up as we grow, and get us ready for EU pay transparency. You don’t need to be a reward specialist yet. If you owned reward projects before and want to make this your expertise, this is where you do it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The second half is partnering. You’ll be the People Business Partner for our core business: security operations, incident response, customer support &amp; onboarding, and project management. It’s the most varied population in the company: working students running shift rosters next to deeply specialized senior engineers, and managers at very different stages of their leadership journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That mix is exactly why this role needs presence more than years. You’ll coach a first-time manager on the basics one hour and align a salary band with C-level the next. You’ll need to be comfortable doing both, and to enjoy it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own Total Rewards end to end:</strong> run the annual salary review, keep our benchmarks honest, and build levelling and salary bands that make sense to managers and employees alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage benefits:</strong> run our benefits across the Netherlands, the UK, Germany and Belgium, work with providers, and keep improving what actually matters to our people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage our equity program:</strong> grants, refreshers, and making sure people understand what their equity means.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prepare Eye for pay transparency:</strong> work with Legal and Finance so we’re ready for the EU directive, not scrambling to catch up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the trusted partner for leaders in security operations and customer support:</strong> coaching, challenging and advising at every level of maturity, up to and including the executive team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be visible.</strong> This is an office where face-to-face matters: you’ll be on the floor in The Hague, listening to what’s actually going on, not partnering from a distance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Handle the real side of employee relations:</strong> sick leave and reintegration, conduct issues and complex cases, working with external counsel when needed. You’ve seen the challenging cases and you don’t flinch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work as part of a small, tight People team:</strong> everyone picks things up, and so will you.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HRBP experience in a scaling tech environment.</strong> You know what good looks like at 200+ people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on reward experience.</strong> Around a year in a reward or C&amp;B role, or several reward projects you led yourself: salary reviews, benchmarking, levelling or benefits. Specialist depth is not required; curiosity to build it is.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable with numbers.</strong> You can build a comp analysis in a spreadsheet and explain it to a manager who has never seen one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong stakeholder management</strong> and the presence to challenge back, including senior leadership, without becoming the policy police.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuinely comfortable with ambiguity.</strong> Our problems don’t come with a manual, and you’d rather solve them creatively than wait for one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on, working knowledge of Dutch labor law,</strong> and you know when to bring in an expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional English.</strong> Dutch is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Based in the Netherlands</strong> and happy coming into the office: at least 1 day a week in The Hague, ideally 3.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real impact:</strong> help build the People foundations of a company protecting businesses across Europe, alongside colleagues from intelligence, military, tech and consulting backgrounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A clear path to make Total Rewards your specialism,</strong> with direct exposure to the leadership team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thursday borrels and regular team socials to catch up in person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quarterly get-togethers and an annual company-wide retreat (Spain, Portugal, Italy…).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous time off, including wellbeing days, floating holidays and a volunteering day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive base salary and company equity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MacBook Pro or Dell XPS, plus iPhone or Samsung.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye Security</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security protects European mid-market businesses from cyber threats: 24/7 monitoring and response, incident response, and integrated cyber insurance, all in one. We’re 170+ people across the Netherlands, UK, Germany and Belgium, with roots in Dutch intelligence and national CERTs. Our mission is simple: enterprise-grade security shouldn’t only be for enterprises</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/total-rewards-people-business-partner-the-hague-403353","tags":["Foundation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1792172419},{"slug":"working-student-talent-acquisition-the-hague-29126","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Working Student Talent Acquisition","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About this role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to find out what recruitment really is, from the inside? At Eye, you won't be filing CVs in a corner. You'll help a growing recruitment team build how we hire, and if it clicks, we'd love to grow you into a recruiter.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help find candidates for our harder-to-fill roles, side by side with our recruiters</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screen applications for our junior and high-volume roles, many of them in Dutch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recruitment data into clear reports the team and hiring managers actually use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clean up and improve how we use our ATS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure to our recruitment knowledge base, starting with every job description in one place</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep interviews running smoothly: scheduling, coordination and candidate communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help build our relationships with universities and students</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is new, so it will grow with you and with what the team needs most.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you wil need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak Dutch fluently and work comfortably in English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a 3rd or 4th year student, available 20 hours a week, with 2–3 days in our office in The Hague or Berlin</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have at least six months of admin or office experience (a board year at a study association counts) and you're at home in Excel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to build a career in recruitment and are curious about how it works</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership: you spot what needs doing, find the help you need and ask good questions<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy working with data, or want to get better at it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some experience with recruitment, HR or an ATS, or admin work.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real responsibility from week one, with a recruiter beside you to learn from</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear chance to grow into a junior recruiter role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible hours around your studies, and a hybrid setup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A team that celebrates together, from monthly team gatherings to our annual "Eye-cation"</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>About Eye Security</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security is providing cybersecurity with embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations in Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we are already over 170 FTEs and continue to grow internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team brings together talent from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds, all united by a shared mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Eye, you will work on projects with an international footprint, solving real-world challenges and helping to build a safer digital future for our clients.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/working-student-talent-acquisition-the-hague-29126","tags":["Foundation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1792172419},{"slug":"c005433-principal-technician-ict-systems-ns-tue-27-oct-the-hague-415586","company_name":"Emw","title":"C005433 Principal Technician (ICT Systems) (NS) - TUE 27 Oct","description":"<p><strong>Deadline Date:</strong> Tuesday 27 October 2026</p><p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Principal Technician (ICT Systems)</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> The Hague, NL</p><p><strong>Full Time On-Site:</strong> Yes</p><p><strong>Time On-Site:</strong> 100% </p><p><strong>Total Scope of the request (hours):</strong> 300</p><p><strong>Required Start Date:</strong> 9 December 2026</p><p><strong>End Contract Date: </strong>31 December 2026 </p><p><strong>Required Security Clearance:</strong> NATO SECRET</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duties &amp; Role:&nbsp; </strong></p><p>The Principal Technician (ICT Systems) is responsible for the installation, maintenance, and repair of information and communication technology systems. He/she provide technical support to end-users and troubleshoot any issues that arise. They stay up to date with the latest technology trends and make recommendations for system improvements. They handle tasks related to configuring hardware and software, managing computers and networks devices, troubleshooting technical issues, ensuring data security and system reliability, and provide technical support to end-users. They collaborate with various departments to understand their technology needs and optimize the organization's ICT infrastructure to support business operations efficiently. </p><p><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></p><p><u>Software configuration</u></p><ul><li>Assists in designing, verifying, documenting, amending and refactoring moderately complex software configurations for deployment.</li><li>Applies agreed standards and tools, to achieve a well-engineered result.</li><li>Collaborates in reviews of work with others as appropriate.</li></ul><p><u>System software</u></p><ul><li>Monitors operational systems for resource usage and failure rates, to inform and facilitate system software tuning.</li><li>Applies system software parameters to maximise throughput and efficiency.</li><li>Installs and tests new versions of system software.</li><li>Contributes to preparation of software implementation procedures with fall back contingency plans.</li></ul><p><u>Network support</u></p><ul><li>Carries out agreed network maintenance tasks and specified operational configuration of network components.</li><li>Establish and diagnose network problems/faults using the required troubleshooting methodology and tools.</li><li>Uses network management software and tools to collect agreed performance and traffic statistics.</li></ul><p><u>Systems installation and removal</u></p><ul><li>Installs or removes hardware and/or software, using supplied installation instructions and tools, including handover to the client.</li><li>Uses standard procedures and diagnostic tools to test installations, correct problems, and document results.</li><li>Records details of all components that have been installed and removed.</li><li>Assists users and follows agreed procedures for further help or escalation.</li><li>Contributes to the development of installation procedures and standards.</li></ul><p><u>Release and deployment</u></p><ul><li>Uses approved tools and techniques for specific deployment activities.</li><li>Administers the recording of activities, logging of results and documents technical activities undertaken.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional duties for this post:</strong></p><p>The Principal Technician (ICT Systems) will provide 24/7 Immediate On-Call Response to the Service Operations with technical AirC2 expertise and solutions at Level 2 support with ticket response and resolutions that will meet current operational needs and defined Key Performance Indicators (KPIs).</p><p>The Principal Technician (ICT Systems) will work as an on-site integrated member of the assigned service team, when not on 24/7 on-call duty for immediate ticket response and resolution. He will help with the design, development, test and on-site support of engineering changes to services, processes, organisation, operating model and other aspects. This effort may be required in addition to his/her daily service operations and maintenance tasks.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Experience:</strong></p><ul><li>The candidate must have a currently active NATO SECRET security clearance </li><li>Higher vocational training in a relevant discipline with 3 years post-related experience. Or a secondary educational qualification with 5 years post-related experience.</li><li>At least 3 years practical experience of implementation and maintenance of ICT end systems within a large organization.</li><li>Good experience configuring hardware and software.</li><li>Good understanding of ICT systems and the ability to work independently to solve problems.</li><li>Hands-on experience troubleshooting technical issues and providing technical support to end-users.</li></ul><p>Desirable:</p><ul><li>Hands-on experience on troubleshooting technical issues and providing technical support to end-users.</li><li>Network configuration, debugging trouble shouting (TCP/IP, VPN, VLAN, firewall, DNS).</li><li>Cybersecurity infrastructure understanding.</li><li>Software development in java, C, C++, python, scripting language.</li><li>Hardware and software configuration of Server hosting platforms, custom disk configurations with specific storage controllers, RAID configuration, redundancy management.</li><li>Overall Strong analytical and problem-solving skills on: Remote server administration; Log analysis; Network tool usage (Wireshark)</li><li>ITIL foundation or advanced level training and certification.</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/emw/c005433-principal-technician-ict-systems-ns-tue-27-oct-the-hague-415586","tags":["Computer & Network Security","AAS"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"The Hague, Netherlands","created_at":1792164023},{"slug":"c004912-penetration-tester-ns-tue-27-oct-relaunch-the-hague-148917","company_name":"Emw","title":"C004912 Penetration Tester (NS) - TUE 27 Oct RELAUNCH","description":"<p><u><strong>NOTE: Please do not resubmit candidates who were found non-compliant in the earlier rounds of this RFQ.</strong></u></p><p><strong>Previously proposed candidates were non-compliant for the following reason: </strong></p><ul><li>The profiles do not demonstrate clear, independently verifiable experience aligning with the minimum requirement of 3 years in hands-on penetration testing. </li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Deadline Date:</strong> Tuesday 27 October 2026</p><p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Penetration Tester</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> The Hague, NL</p><p><strong>Full Time On-Site:</strong> Yes</p><p><strong>Time On-Site:</strong> 100% </p><p><strong>Total Scope of the request (hours):</strong> 400</p><p><strong>Required Start Date:</strong> 30 November 2026</p><p><strong>End Contract Date: </strong>31 December 2026 </p><p><strong>Required Security Clearance:</strong> NATO SECRET</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Duties &amp; Role: &nbsp;</strong></p><p>The duties of the individual mainly focus on:</p><ul><li>Lead and/or be part of the Red/Blue Team during NATO military exercises;</li><li>Provide Web, infrastructure and application level penetration testing;</li><li>Provide security design reviews to ensure compliance with NATO policies and directives;</li><li>Provide security consultancy and advice to projects, plans, and other entities;</li><li>Build and sustain effective communications with different stakeholders; specifically, the NCIA Configuration Control Board, Security Accreditation Boards, NATO Security Accreditation Authorities, and NCI Agency organization units supporting accreditation processes.</li><li>Brief at both executive and technical levels on security reports and testing outcome, including at flag officer level;</li><li>In co-ordination with the Head of the Penetration testing Cell, ensure proactive collaboration and coordination with internal and external stakeholders.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>Skill, Knowledge &amp; Experience:</strong></p><ul><li>The candidate must have a currently active NATO SECRET security clearance</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in web application penetration testing;</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in IT infrastructure penetration testing;</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in network security architecture design;</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in assessing security vulnerabilities within OS, software, protocols &amp; networks;</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in researching and evaluating security products &amp; technologies;</li><li>Knowledge in system and network administration of UNIX and Windows systems;</li><li>Extensive knowledge and experience (more than 3 years) in the use of penetration testing tools, techniques, and recognized testing methodologies;</li><li>Scripting skills in at least one of the following: Perl, Python, Ruby, shell (bash, ksh, csh);</li><li>Technical knowledge in system and network security, authentication and security protocols, cryptography, application security, as well as, malware infection techniques and protection technologies.</li><li>Ability to evaluate risks and formulate mitigation plans;</li><li>Proven ability to write clear and structured technical reports including executive summary, technical findings and remediation plan for several different audiences </li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/emw/c004912-penetration-tester-ns-tue-27-oct-relaunch-the-hague-148917","tags":["Computer & Network Security","AAS"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"The Hague, Netherlands","created_at":1792164023},{"slug":"senior-manager-commercial-sourcing-contracts-39828","company_name":"Bridgebio","title":"Senior Manager, Commercial Sourcing & Contracts","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Commercial Sourcing and Contracts will report directly to the Head of International Supply Chain. This role will be responsible for supporting the development and execution of sourcing strategies, managing the end-to-end contracting lifecycle for commercial goods and services. You will partner closely with cross-functional stakeholders (Supply Chain, Legal, Finance, CMC and Quality) to manage supplier relationships and ensure contractual compliance across Contract Manufacturing Organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sourcing Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and implementation of sourcing strategies for Contract Manufacturing Organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RFP processes, supplier evaluations, and negotiations to secure optimal cost, quality, and service outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market analysis and benchmarking to support the identification of sourcing opportunities and mitigate supply risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier consolidation, dual-sourcing, or diversification strategies where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, negotiate, and finalize commercial contracts, master service agreements (MSAs), and supply agreements in collaboration with the relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a contract repository/tracker ensuring visibility of key terms, renewal dates, and obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contract amendments, renewals, and terminations in line with business needs and risk exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as primary Commercial Supply Chain point of contact for Contract Manufacturing Organizations, managing performance reviews and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor supplier performance against SLAs/KPIs and drive corrective action plans where needed with relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support supplier risk assessments (financial, operational, compliance) in coordination with Quality and Supply Chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in the Netherlands, with approximately 10–15% travel anticipated to visit Contract Manufacturing Organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a related field, such as Supply Chain, Logistics, or Business Administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 10 years of supply chain experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life sciences industry experience; experience with commercial products is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience negotiating and managing commercial contracts with Contract Manufacturing Organizations in a regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and sustain trusted relationships, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and cross-functional collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to translate contract terms into sourcing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, organized, and comfortable managing multiple contracts/projects simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market-leading compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model – we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career development through regular feedback, continuous education, and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognition for strong performance through financial rewards, peer-to-peer feedback, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
