&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate AI Policy&lt;/strong&gt;: Planet embraces Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools, and we encourage its responsible use. We understand that candidates may use various resources, including AI tools, to &lt;em&gt;prepare&lt;/em&gt; for interviews and assessments. However, &lt;em&gt;during any live interview stage or when actively completing assessments for this position, the use of AI tools—e.g. Large Language Models (LLMs), deep fake technology, etc.—is strictly prohibited unless explicitly prompted by an interviewer or assessment instructions&lt;/em&gt;. If you are unsure about acceptable use, please contact your recruiter for clarification. If an AI tool or similar technology is desired as an accommodation, please contact ----- with your request for assistance. Your message will be confidential, and we will be happy to assist you. Violation of this policy may result in disqualification of your application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/planetlabs/senior-product-manager-sovereign-hybrid-deployments-haarlem-287300","tags":["Imagery & Data"],"job_types":[],"location":"Haarlem","created_at":1792162519},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-benelux-378923","company_name":"Lyric","title":"Enterprise Account Executive (Benelux)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>About the Company</u></strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why We Built Lyric:</strong> Supply chains are more critical and complex than ever. Every day, large enterprises navigate trillions of possible decisions that could impact the bottom line. Powerful algorithms and AI can address these problems, yet most organizations struggle to leverage supply chain AI at scale. The current SCM technologies are either rigid, limited-scope point solutions or custom solutions built in-house, which demand immense expertise and investment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is…until now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enter Lyric</strong>: Lyric is an enterprise AI platform built specifically for supply chains, offering the best of both worlds:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Out-of-the-box AI solutions</strong> for optimizing networks, allocating inventory, scheduling routes, planning fulfillment capacity, promising orders, propagating demand, building predictions, analyzing scenarios, and more, <em><strong>plus</strong></em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A platform-first approach</strong> that empowers both business and technical users with end-to-end product composability, leveraging no-code tools, their own code, or even forking our code to build and refine supply chain decision intelligence</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">With Lyric, enterprises no longer have to choose between flexibility and speed, they get both.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Mission:</strong> We’re building a new era in supply chain with the team best equipped to lead it. With over 20 years at the intersection of supply chain and algorithms, we developed a deep conviction that global supply chains needed something like Lyric. Since our inception in December 2021, that conviction has been validated time and time again.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, a growing number of Fortune 500 companies, including Smurfit WestRock, Estée Lauder, Coca-Cola, and more, are innovating on their own terms with Lyric. We can’t wait to see what our customers, both current and future, are empowered to build with us next. Come build with us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an experienced Account Executive to join our growing enterprise sales team. You will own the entire deal cycle, generating pipeline, closing target customers, and expanding relationships over time. You’re the right fit for this role if you are excited by joining an early-stage team and building in an autonomous and highly creative environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our land and expand deal cycle from initial conversation to close with critical stakeholders in enterprise companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the development of the Lyric Land and Expand sales playbook and execution strategy, including the implementation of an effective sales methodology</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and provide regular forecasting across your book of business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join Lyric’s best in class GTM team, consisting of highly experienced, top-performers evangelizing the market on the premier SCM AI platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide input to the direction of sales strategy, enablement, and operations tools and workflows (CRM, forecasting, lead gen tools, pipeline management, outreach automation)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5-6+ years of complex enterprise sales experience. This experience can come in two different forms, both equally weighted in importance</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience closing enterprise platform, AI, and/or Data &amp; Analytics <em>software </em>deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience closing enterprise supply chain, AI, and/or Data &amp; Analytics <em>services</em> deals</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to deliver and drive logo acquisition deals in a fast paced and early stage environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to prospect to and engage with customers to understand their supply chain and operational challenges, and translate those challenges to business impacts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated comfort with Supply Chain or Operations Research terminology and mid-level to executive personas</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re Also Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of overachievement in previous revenue-generating roles, driving 6- and 7-figure multi-year enterprise deals to close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling and negotiating enterprise contracts to C- level, senior technical, and/or business stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-starter with infectious enthusiasm, an out-of-the-box thinker who sees opportunities and solutions, not roadblocks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Even if you don’t meet 100% of the qualifications, we recommend applying to the role!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote - Benelux: Belgium, Netherlands, or Luxembourg. Some travel is required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:</strong> We provide a competitive mix of salary, commissions, local benefits, and equity, designed to reward both your impact and growth. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/lyric/enterprise-account-executive-benelux-378923","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Benelux","created_at":1792161619},{"slug":"early-career-product-designer-mobile-app-amsterdam-414520","company_name":"Teampicnic","title":"Early career Product Designer - Mobile App","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in designing the future of grocery shopping. As a Product Designer in our consumer team, you&#39;ll own the design of our core mobile app, shaping the daily shopping experience for hundreds of thousands of people in The Netherlands, Germany and France. You&#39;ll tackle the unique challenge of designing for a task that is frequent, personal, and central to our customers&#39; lives. You&#39;ll be part of a dedicated product team and our wider UX Guild, a creative community that ensures a world-class user experience across Picnic. We’re looking for a passionate designer to join our Amsterdam HQ and help build a product people genuinely love, in a fast-scaling environment that values autonomy, collaboration, and adaptability over rigid processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the autonomy to own the design of new features from beginning to end. Everything you do matters and will be developed and tested at a fast pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharpen project briefs based on explorative research together with UX researchers and product owners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build low and high fidelity prototypes to be tested and evaluated on a weekly basis with real users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document the final design requirements on interaction and UI level to brief and support developers during the development phase.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow through the continuous feedback and mentoring by seasoned UX designers and researchers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and maintenance of our design libraries and system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously explore new ideas in order to initiate new projects and improvements, design is never done ;).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have a completed degree in a relevant design field (e.g. CMD, UX, Interaction or Product Design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have 0-3 years of experience as a UX designer and have worked on or have a strong interest in building great products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Your portfolio has user-centered design cases that show your problem solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have a deep curiosity to understand our customers and have hands-on experience in exploratory research to discover and define user problems from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You know your way around Figma and are able to craft high-fidelity designs that fit into our design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You bring a low-ego, collaborative mindset and enjoy building solutions together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You’re fluent in English and holder of an EU work permit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You&#39;re open to work on-site fulltime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic perks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏼‍♂️Health insurance discount &amp;amp; bike plan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a partnership with CZ (a health insurance provider). Picnic employees get a discount on CZ insurance packages between 5% and 15%. Furthermore, through our partnership with Lease a Bike, you can rent-to-own a new (e)bike at a discounted rate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🏠 Relocation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re moving from another country to join Picnic we make it as smooth as possible for you. We’ll cover your flight costs for you and your partner and kids, your first month&#39;s rent and moving costs (up to €2000), and help you with the 30% tax ruling setup and application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Learning &amp;amp; development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get ample opportunity to work on yourself at Picnic. We offer personal development through Lepaya courses, Academy trainings, and more. Interested in improving your mental wellbeing? Through OpenUp you get free access to trained psychologists and many courses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All the rest&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic you get 25 holidays, we cover your travel expenses and offer a pension plan. And your phone and laptop are on us, as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/teampicnic/early-career-product-designer-mobile-app-amsterdam-414520","tags":["Consumer"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792151719},{"slug":"senior-ml-engineer-kimchi-inference-stack-optimization-375002","company_name":"Kimchi","title":"Senior ML Engineer | Kimchi (Inference Stack Optimization)","description":"&lt;h4&gt;Why Kimchi?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great models are raw ingredients. Kimchi is what happens when you ferment them with good engineering. We started inside CAST AI helping companies run LLMs on their own Kubernetes clusters; today we run our own coding harness on any model you pick, and we run the models underneath it ourselves.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimchi Inference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One API line and a customer&#39;s existing client just works: DeepSeek, GLM, Kimi, MiniMax, Nemotron served serverless from our own GPU fleet (OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible, pay per token, spend visible per user, team, and key). When control matters, the same models run on the customer&#39;s own cluster instead. Behind that one line sits the machinery you&#39;ll own: SGLang and vLLM engines, B300 nodes, a shared cluster filesystem that holds every checkpoint exactly once, KV caches riding coding traffic with heavy prefix reuse, and the benchmark harness that gates every change we ship.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;em&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;Made by Cast AI — a Miami-headquartered, globally distributed team across 34 countries that hit unicorn status in January 2026 with a $50B+ backed investment pushing its valuation past $1 billion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Throughput. Latency. Cold starts. Cost per token.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Move those four numbers in the right direction and two things happen: customers get faster, cheaper inference, and our margins improve. That&#39;s the entire thesis of this role. Every loader you tune, every scheduler decision you land, every kernel you stare at shows up in a customer&#39;s p99 and on our P&amp;amp;L. Your mandate is the inference stack&#39;s optimization, whatever it takes, and the technical direction of how we optimize it is yours to argue with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The problem:&lt;/strong&gt; the checkpoints run 0.3-1.5 TB, and the &quot;right&quot; serving configuration depends on traffic shape, sequence-length distribution, batch dynamics, GPU SKU, memory bandwidth, and quantization tolerance, all variables that shift week to week. Most teams pick a configuration once, over-provision GPUs, and absorb the cost. We don&#39;t: we took Kimi-K3 (1.5 TB) from over an hour cold-to-serving to under twelve minutes with a shared filesystem, O_DIRECT weight loaders, and node-local JIT caches, and we&#39;re nowhere near done. Prefill/decode disaggregation and tiered KV caches are next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Python; SGLang; vLLM; TensorRT-LLM; PyTorch; fastsafetensors; CUDA-adjacent tooling; Kubernetes; virtiofs shared filesystems; ClickHouse; OpenTelemetry; Prometheus; Grafana; GitLab CI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built real ML systems for 5+ years, and your portfolio shows depth in inference or training infrastructure, not just model training notebooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your Python is production-grade: services, not scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve run vLLM, SGLang, or TensorRT-LLM for real, and you have a working mental model of why an engine performs the way it does on a given GPU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve measured quantization regressions, not just compression ratios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-GPU and multi-node setups hold no fear: tensor and expert parallelism, collective communication, and their practical failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know where the bytes live (page caches, O_DIRECT, network filesystems under terabyte-scale reads) and how fast they move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You instrument before you optimize, and you can tell a real win from a benchmark artifact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wide mandate excites you more than it unsettles you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to haves&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked on LLM routing specifically: RouterBench-class evals, cost/quality/latency Pareto fronts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calibration, abstention, or conformal methods in production decision systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve run online A/B loops with drift monitoring on a model that touches real money.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push throughput. Continuous batching, chunked prefill, speculative decoding with draft models, CUDA-graph capture, and scheduler tuning across the engine&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;fleet. Find the ceiling on each GPU SKU, then raise it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cut latency. Attack TTFT and inter-token latency separately; profile to find the actual bottleneck (compute, memory bandwidth, scheduling, storage, or&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;network) and fix it, not the one you assumed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get more out of the KV cache. Hierarchical and paged attention, prefix caching on heavy-reuse coding traffic, eviction policies, quantized KV. A lot of the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;unrealized throughput lives here, and you&#39;ll own it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kill cold starts. Weight loaders (O_DIRECT, fastsafetensors-class), JIT and compile caches, shared-filesystem read paths. A 1.5 TB checkpoint has no business&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;taking an hour to reach serving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantize without regressing quality. INT8/INT4, FP8/FP4 across weights, activations, and KV, measured on real workloads, not just perplexity benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale across nodes. Distributed inference topologies, network-aware placement, prefill/decode disaggregation, checkpointing strategies that don&#39;t bottleneck&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;on storage or interconnect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction. Decide what we benchmark, what we adopt, and what we build ourselves. Bring the team along with strong writeups and reproducible&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (depending on the level of experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a flexible, remote-first global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a global team of cloud experts and innovators, passionate about pushing the boundaries of Kubernetes technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get quick feedback with a fast-paced workflow. Most feature projects are completed in 1 to 4 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend 10% of your work time on personal projects or self-improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning budget for professional and personal development - including access to international conferences and courses that elevate your skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual hackathon to spark new ideas and strengthen team bonds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-building budget and company events to connect with your colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment budget to ensure you have everything you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra days off to help maintain a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Hiring process&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening call with Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring Manager interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical interview (system design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture Check interview with an executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of our standard hiring process, we would like to inform you that a background check may be conducted at the final stage of recruitment through our third-party provider, Checkr.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that Cast AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;em&gt;does not&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;em&gt; provide any form of visa sponsorship/work permit.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/kimchi/senior-ml-engineer-kimchi-inference-stack-optimization-375002","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792140925},{"slug":"senior-applied-ml-engineer-kimchi-model-router-336004","company_name":"Kimchi","title":"Senior Applied ML Engineer | Kimchi (Model Router)","description":"&lt;h4&gt;Why Kimchi?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great models are raw ingredients. Kimchi is what happens when you ferment them with good engineering. We started inside CAST AI helping companies run LLMs on their own Kubernetes clusters; today we run our own coding harness on any model you pick, and the router deciding which model answers each request is ours too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Auto Router&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our promise is one enforcement layer for your AI: budgets, spend attribution, and model routing, applied before a request ever hits a model. The Auto Router makes the call: for every request, which model serves it. Eight open-source models whose input prices span more than 20×, cached input up to 50× cheaper than fresh, frontier providers on customers&#39; own keys, and a coding agent that fires hundreds of requests before its task is done. Frontier-level task success at a fraction of the token cost: that sentence is the product, and it stays true only if the model inside the router keeps getting better. That model is yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;em&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;Made &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;em&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;by Cast AI — a Miami-headquartered, globally distributed team across 34 countries that hit unicorn status in January 2026 with a $50B+ backed investment pushing its valuation past $1 billion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every request gets a decision: which model serves it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an applied-ML seat, not an infrastructure one. Platform engineers own the proxy, the streaming path, and the fleet. You own the model inside them: the training data, the objective, the evaluation, and the iteration loop that ships a better router every cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The problem:&lt;/strong&gt; routing is a prediction problem wearing a product&#39;s clothes. For every request you predict the quality each candidate model would deliver, what it would cost, and how fast it would decode, and you have to be right enough, in aggregate, that the savings are real and the quality never dips below frontier. The data is messy: rollout outcomes from benchmark harnesses, per-request records from the live fleet, override signals, and token streams whose speed depends on the serving concurrency at the moment. Speed itself is a correctness variable: on deadline-bound agentic work, a model that decodes three times slower doesn&#39;t do the same work slower, it does less work. That&#39;s why naive cost-per-token objectives quietly optimize for the wrong thing. And the bar for evidence is high: a router change ships only after production-parity evaluation with error bars, then gets held to its numbers in live traffic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Python; PyTorch; SQL at scale (ClickHouse); OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible LLM APIs; benchmark and rollout harnesses (RouterBench-class); GitLab CI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve spent 5+ years in applied ML or ML research, and you&#39;ve trained, evaluated, and shipped models that make real-time decisions (ranking, recommendation, bandits, pricing, or LLM routing) and you can tell that story with receipts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python and SQL at scale: you can pull, clean, and interrogate millions of request-level records without waiting on anyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know the difference between a model that got better and an eval that got easier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have real opinions about what LLM benchmarks measure, agentic harnesses included.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know enough serving reality (TTFT, decode speed, batching, prefix caching, concurrency) to model the objective honestly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You instrument before you optimize, error bars and all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wide mandate excites you more than it unsettles you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to haves&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked on LLM routing specifically: RouterBench-class evals, cost/quality/latency Pareto fronts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calibration, abstention, or conformal methods in production decision systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve run online A/B loops with drift monitoring on a model that touches real money.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the routing model end to end: features, objective, training, calibration, and release cadence. Iterate it like a product, not a research artifact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the evaluation that gates every change: production-parity benchmarks, router-vs-router comparisons, holdouts by task family, error bars on pass rates.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;Nothing ships on vibes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn fleet data into training signal: per-request outcomes from production, benchmark rollouts, and override feedback, with failure categorization (infra vs&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;task) so poisoned labels never reach the policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model the objective the user actually experiences: task success × token cost × wall-clock speed under the real concurrency regime, with cached-input&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;economics in the picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the online loop: shadow, A/B, full rollout, drift monitoring, retrain. When production disagrees with your offline eval, you find out why before the next&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push the frontier where it pays: calibrated decisions, abstention under uncertainty, speed-aware routing. We experiment on what a router should be, not just&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;which model it picks today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with platform engineers on instrumentation: the features and labels recorded per request (decode speed first-class among them) and the experiments&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;the data path must support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (depending on the level of experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a flexible, remote-first global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a global team of cloud experts and innovators, passionate about pushing the boundaries of Kubernetes technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get quick feedback with a fast-paced workflow. Most feature projects are completed in 1 to 4 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend 10% of your work time on personal projects or self-improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning budget for professional and personal development - including access to international conferences and courses that elevate your skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual hackathon to spark new ideas and strengthen team bonds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-building budget and company events to connect with your colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment budget to ensure you have everything you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra days off to help maintain a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Hiring process&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening call with Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring Manager interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical interview (system design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture Check interview with an executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
